('806d1488-be70-4917-b728-0e650843efda', 'Shoulder Flexion Back To Wall - Y Raise (Wall) - Alternating', 'Shoulders', 'Wall', '{"Rear Delts"}'::text[], '{"Upper Back","Rotator Cuff"}'::text[], 'The Alternating Shoulder Flexion Back To Wall (Y Raise is a raising exercise that targets your delts for shoulder development. You''ll also feel your upper back working to support the movement. Strong shoulders improve overhead strength and support nearly all upper body movements.', '43941201', '43941201-Alternating-Shoulder-Flexion-Back-to-Wall-(Y-Raise.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:26.808474+00', '1. Position yourself at the appropriate distance from a wall. 2. Raise the weight in the prescribed direction for Alternating Shoulder Flexion Back To Wall (Y Raise. 3. Lower with control, maintaining tension throughout. 4. Alternate between sides/arms/legs with each repetition. 5. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 62, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'lateral_raise', 'Shoulder Flexion Back To Wall (Y Raise - Alternating', 'shoulder_press, front_raise, rear_delt', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('806d2948-c8dc-4efc-9cfe-e2f20eaf9f5e', 'Incline Triceps Extension (Band)', 'Arms', 'Resistance Band, Incline Bench', '{"Triceps"}'::text[], '{"Chest","Shoulders"}'::text[], 'Build stronger triceps with this extension exercise for bigger arms. Using an incline changes the angle of resistance for varied muscle recruitment. The band creates increasing tension as it stretches, challenging the lockout. Dedicated arm training builds both strength and muscular definition.', '68621201', '68621201-Band-Incline-Triceps-Extension_Upper-Arms_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:22.644637+00', '1. Secure the resistance band appropriately for Band Incline Triceps Extension. 2. Extend at the elbow until your arm is straight, squeezing the tricep. 3. Lower with control, keeping your upper arm stationary. 4. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 88, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'tricep_extension', 'Incline Triceps Extension', 'tricep_pushdown, close_grip_bench', FALSE, 'band', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 60, 85, 90, 50),
('8071a1ac-676c-45bc-ac84-76500f82b97e', 'Two Arm Military Press (Kettlebell)', 'Shoulders', 'Kettlebell', '{"Front Delts"}'::text[], '{"Side Delts","Triceps"}'::text[], 'This pressing exercise works your delts for improved shoulder strength and aesthetics. Secondary activation of your triceps provides additional muscle engagement. Kettlebells are excellent for building functional, real-world strength. Strong shoulders improve overhead strength and support nearly all upper body movements.', '5531201', '05531201-Kettlebell-Two-Arm-Military-Press_Shoulders_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:28.851102+00', '1. Position two kettlebells for Kettlebell Two Arm Military Press. 2. Start with the weight at shoulder level. 3. Press directly overhead until your arms are fully extended. 4. Lower back to shoulder level with control. 5. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 93, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'shoulder_press', 'Two Arm Military Press', 'lateral_raise, front_raise, rear_delt', FALSE, 'kettlebell', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 75, 88, 88, 78),
('80727bad-d6f2-4056-add7-89b8b346297f', 'Elbow To Arm Open Side Step', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'Build power and athleticism with this high-intensity stepping exercise that challenges your entire body. Secondary activation of your quads provides additional muscle engagement. Plyometric training builds explosive power that transfers to sports and daily activities.', '64771201', '64771201-Elbow-to-Arm-Open-Side-Step-(female)_Plyometrics_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:33.298565+00', '1. Set up a box or step platform at the appropriate height. 2. Set up in the starting position for Elbow To Arm Open Side Step. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your full body. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 5. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'arm_exercise', 'Elbow To Arm Open Side Step', 'bicep_curl, tricep_extension, hammer_curl', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('80811757-d2ac-4166-ad4f-336580cee6d0', 'Sideward Shuffle', 'Full Body', 'Bodyweight', '{"Full Body"}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'The Sideward Shuffle is an explosive exercise that combines cardiovascular training with dynamic movement movements. A versatile bodyweight movement perfect for home or gym training. Plyometric training builds explosive power that transfers to sports and daily activities.', '80591201', '80591201-Sideward-Shuffle-(male)_Plyometrics_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:26.146796+00', '1. Set up in the starting position for Sideward Shuffle. 2. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your full body. 3. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 4. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 4, NULL, 8, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 7, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Plyometrics', 50, 9, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'shuffle', 'Sideward Shuffle', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('8085f221-7919-4cba-988e-aa97012acfb3', 'Seated Thumbs Up Pulse', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'Build a stronger back with this movement movement targeting your core. The seated position helps isolate the target muscles by removing momentum. A strong back improves posture, prevents injury, and balances pressing movements.', '89411201', '89411201-Seated-Thumbs-Up-Pulse-(female)_Back_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:36.848698+00', '1. Sit with your back supported, core engaged, feet flat on the floor. 2. At the bottom or top, pulse up and down in small movements before completing the rep. 3. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout. Engage your stabilizer muscles for better control.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, 'Seated', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 52, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'pulse', 'Seated Thumbs Up Pulse', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('808feb85-477e-4460-8745-0c551b59a7c3', 'Lateral Step Up (Platform)', 'Legs', 'Step Platform', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'Build stronger quads with this stepping movement that develops leg drive and power. You''ll also feel your glutes, hamstrings working to support the movement. Lower body strength improves everything from walking to heavy compound lifts.', '65621201', '65621201-Bodyweight-Lateral-Step-up-(male)_Thighs_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:24.941834+00', '1. Set up a box or step platform at the appropriate height. 2. Step one foot onto the elevated surface. 3. Drive through that foot to lift your body up onto the platform. 4. Step back down with control and repeat. 5. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions. Ensure full range of motion on each rep.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 70, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'step_up', 'Lateral Step Up', 'lunge, split_squat, squat', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('80963d54-55a1-497d-9768-249f1dbd2942', 'Wall Sit Narrow Stance (Wall)', 'Back', 'Wall', '{"Upper Back"}'::text[], '{"Lats","Biceps","Rear Delts"}'::text[], 'This rowing movement emphasizes your quadriceps for stronger, more powerful legs. You''ll also feel your glutes working to support the movement. Leg training boosts metabolism and builds functional, real-world strength.', '75571201', '75571201-Wall-sit-(narrow-stance)-(male)_Thighs_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:28.851102+00', '1. Position yourself at the appropriate distance from a wall. 2. Use a close/narrow grip (hands closer than shoulder-width). 3. Pull the weight toward your torso, leading with your elbow(s). 4. Squeeze your shoulder blades together at the peak contraction. 5. Extend back out with control, feeling the stretch in your back. 6. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout. Exhale during the exertion phase of the movement.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 70, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'wall_sit', 'Wall Sit', 'squat, leg_press, lunge', FALSE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('80a05fed-54e3-453b-ad02-e0514c841992', 'High Jump Rope (Jump Rope)', 'Full Body', 'Jump Rope', '{"Full Body"}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'Build your aerobic capacity with this steady-state cardio movement. Your quads, calves work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. Regular cardio training builds the aerobic base for better overall fitness.', '71601201', '71601201-High-Jump-Rope-(female)_Cardio_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:33.960339+00', '1. Set up in the starting position for High Jump Rope. 2. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your cardio. 3. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 4. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'jump_rope', 'High Jump Rope', 'running, jumping_jack, high_knees', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('80a4fcdb-da68-4e18-8bb4-28d372b5e23c', 'Quadriceps Stretch', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'This stretch specifically works on your quads, promoting flexibility and reducing muscle tightness. Include this in your routine for better mobility and reduced muscle tension.', '9401201', '09401201-Quadriceps-Stretch-(female)_Thighs.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:35.936279+00', '1. Move into the stretch position for Quadriceps Stretch. 2. Ease into the stretch until you feel gentle tension (not pain). 3. Hold for 20-30 seconds, breathing deeply and relaxing into the stretch. Control the movement—avoid using momentum.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 1, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Stretch', 40, 2, 6, FALSE, TRUE, 'stretch_general', 'Quadriceps Stretch', 'stretch_hip, stretch_hamstring', FALSE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 1, 30, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('80b7942e-2856-4482-b603-6c0fc1c9d455', 'Weighted Full Squat From Deficit (Step Platform)', 'Legs', 'Step Platform', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'Build stronger quads with this squatting movement that develops leg drive and power. The glutes, hamstrings assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. No equipment needed—your body provides all the resistance. Lower body strength improves everything from walking to heavy compound lifts. Control the negative portion for maximum muscle engagement.', '74111201', '74111201-Weighted-Full-Squat-from-Deficit-(male)_Thighs_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:23.987963+00', '1. Push your hips back and bend your knees to lower your body. 2. Keep your chest up and knees tracking over your toes. 3. Drive through your heels to stand back up, squeezing your glutes at the top. 4. Complete all reps with control before resting. Maintain consistent tempo throughout the set.', 'Squat', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 4, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 85, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'squat', 'Weighted Full Squat From Deficit', 'leg_press, front_squat, goblet_squat, lunge, leg_extension', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('80be258a-4009-4c8c-a600-dfdde2231142', 'Step Up On Box (Plyo Box)', 'Legs', 'Plyo Box', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'Build stronger quads with this stepping movement that develops leg drive and power. You''ll also feel your glutes, hamstrings working to support the movement. Leg training boosts metabolism and builds functional, real-world strength.', '107241201', '107241201-Step-Up-on-Box-(female)_Thighs_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:39.21093+00', '1. Set up a box or step platform at the appropriate height. 2. Step one foot onto the elevated surface. 3. Drive through that foot to lift your body up onto the platform. 4. Step back down with control and repeat. 5. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions. Maintain a neutral spine throughout. This variation specifically emphasizes the quads.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 70, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'step_up', 'Step Up On Box', 'lunge, split_squat, squat', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('80e28c20-f651-422d-9b58-dc51fcdb6449', 'Back Squat (Kettlebell)', 'Legs', 'Kettlebell', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'Target the front of your thighs with this squatting exercise for quad development. Secondary activation of your glutes, hamstrings provides additional muscle engagement. The kettlebell''s offset center of mass increases the stability challenge. Strong legs are the foundation for athletic performance and functional fitness.', '106741201', '106741201-Kettlebell-Back-Squat-(male)_Thighs_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:29.837118+00', '1. Select an appropriately weighted kettlebell for Kettlebell Back Squat. 2. Push your hips back and bend your knees to lower your body. 3. Keep your chest up and knees tracking over your toes. 4. Drive through your heels to stand back up, squeezing your glutes at the top. 5. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', 'Squat', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 93, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'squat', 'Back Squat', 'leg_press, front_squat, goblet_squat, lunge, leg_extension', FALSE, 'kettlebell', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 75, 88, 88, 78),
('80e2b448-54fb-41d9-92b0-c84a9a49e5f8', '90 To 90 Overhead Reach', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Hips"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'This stretch specifically works on your hips, promoting flexibility and reducing muscle tightness. The glutes assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. Flexibility work like this enhances performance and prevents stiffness.', '79171201', '79171201-90-to-90-Overhead-Reach-(female)_Stretching_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:30.292204+00', '1. Move into the stretch position for 90 To 90 Overhead Reach. 2. Ease into the stretch until you feel gentle tension (not pain). 3. Hold for 20-30 seconds, breathing deeply and relaxing into the stretch.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'general_exercise', '90 To 90 Overhead Reach', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('80f0b142-7fac-45c4-a212-dfa05c5039da', 'Easy Pose (Hands Behind Interlocked And Bend Forward)', 'Full Body', 'Bodyweight', '{"Full Body"}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'This stretch specifically works on your full body, promoting flexibility and reducing muscle tightness. Flexibility work like this enhances performance and prevents stiffness. Aim for full range of motion on every rep. Consistency with this movement will yield noticeable results.', '81551201', '81551201-Easy-Pose-(hands-behind-interlocked-and-bend-forwa.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:33.298565+00', '1. Move into the stretch position for Easy Pose (hands Behind Interlocked And Bend Forwa. 2. Ease into the stretch until you feel gentle tension (not pain). 3. Hold for 20-30 seconds, breathing deeply and relaxing into the stretch.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 1, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Stretch', 15, 2, 6, FALSE, TRUE, 'general_exercise', 'Easy Pose (hands Behind Interlocked And Bend Forwa', 'stretch_hip, stretch_back, plank', FALSE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 1, 30, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('80f8c86b-5943-412a-9b18-357dcdc5642d', 'Hip Extension Stretch', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Glutes"}'::text[], '{"Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'The Hip Extension Stretch is a hip-dominant extension exercise that targets your glutes. The hamstrings assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. This bodyweight exercise requires no equipment and can be done anywhere. Strong legs are the foundation for athletic performance and functional fitness.', '4831201', '04831201-Hip-Extension-Stretch_Hips-FIX_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:34.073704+00', '1. Extend through the target joint(s) for Hip Extension Stretch. 2. Set up in the starting position for Hip Extension Stretch. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your glutes. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 5. Complete all reps with control before resting. Focus on the mind-muscle connection.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 1, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Stretch', 60, 2, 6, FALSE, TRUE, 'glute_kickback', 'Hip Extension Stretch', 'stretch_hamstring, stretch_glute, stretch_back', FALSE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 1, 30, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('811033e1-da30-40e3-b944-5df10d9e01a7', 'Chair Sit Heel Raise (Against Wall) - Alternating', 'Legs', 'Wall, Chair', '{"Calves"}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'Build stronger calves with this targeted raising exercise. Strong legs are the foundation for athletic performance and functional fitness. Perfect for including in both strength and hypertrophy programs.', '89591201', '89591201-Chair-Sit-Alternate-Heel-Raise-agains-Wall-(male)_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:25.123298+00', '1. Position yourself with a sturdy chair for support or as part of the movement. 2. Position yourself at the appropriate distance from a wall. 3. Raise the weight in the prescribed direction for Chair Sit Alternate Heel Raise Against Wall. 4. Lower with control, maintaining tension throughout. 5. Alternate between sides/arms/legs with each repetition. 6. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 47, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'calf_raise', 'Chair Sit Heel Raise Against Wall - Alternating', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('81122607-7bd9-48cc-a804-fb8741a7ce5d', 'Handstand Walk', 'Shoulders', 'Bodyweight', '{"Shoulders"}'::text[], '{"Traps"}'::text[], 'Build stronger shoulders with this stepping movement focusing on your delts. This bodyweight exercise requires no equipment and can be done anywhere. Strong shoulders improve overhead strength and support nearly all upper body movements.', '43761201', '43761201-Handstand-Walk_Shoulders_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:27.263406+00', '1. Set up in the starting position for Handstand Walk. 2. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your delts. 3. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 4. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 5, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 5, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'yoga', 'Handstand Walk', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('8120a576-6baa-46e9-9821-528023e1fd4d', 'Decline Diamond Push Up', 'Chest', 'Bodyweight', '{"Chest","Lower Chest"}'::text[], '{"Front Delts","Triceps"}'::text[], 'The Decline Diamond Push Up is a pushing exercise that targets your chest muscles. You''ll also feel your chest working to support the movement. Declining shifts the emphasis to hit the muscles from a different angle. Chest strength improves pushing power for sports, daily tasks, and other lifts.', '58661201', '58661201-Decline-Diamond-Push-up_Chest_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:27.937212+00', '1. Keep your body in a straight line from head to heels throughout. 2. Lower your chest toward the floor by bending your elbows. 3. Push through your palms to return to the starting position. 4. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions. Keep your core engaged for stability. Works well for chest activation.', 'Push Up', 'Push', 'Compound', 'Bilateral', NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 73, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'push_up', 'Decline Diamond Push Up', 'bench_press, chest_fly, dip', TRUE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('81273abf-0be2-4f13-86d7-ff8caac8f538', 'X Side Walk (Resistance Band)', 'Full Body', 'Resistance Band', '{"Full Body"}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'The Resistance Band X Side Walk is an explosive exercise that combines cardiovascular training with dynamic stepping movements. Resistance bands provide accommodating resistance that increases through the range of motion. Great for improving athletic performance, burning calories, and building conditioning.', '81661201', '81661201-Resistance-Band-X-Side-Walk-(male)_Plyometrics_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:26.808474+00', '1. Secure the resistance band appropriately for Resistance Band X Side Walk. 2. Set up in the starting position for Resistance Band X Side Walk. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your full body. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 5. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 55, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'walking', 'X Side Walk', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'band', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 60, 85, 90, 50),
('81332997-8537-4c7e-ba28-04ed5699af1e', 'Standing Upright Palms Back Squeeze', 'Full Body', 'Bodyweight', '{"Full Body"}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'The Standing Upright Palms Back Squeeze is a movement exercise that develops back strength and muscle. Performing this standing challenges your balance and core engagement. This bodyweight exercise requires no equipment and can be done anywhere. A strong back improves posture, prevents injury, and balances pressing movements.', '72201201', '72201201-Standing-Upright-Palms-Back-Squeeze-(female)_Back_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:38.992671+00', '1. Begin in a standing position with good posture. 2. Set up in the starting position for Standing Upright Palms Back Squeeze. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your full body. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 5. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, 'Standing', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 52, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'back_exercise', 'Standing Upright Palms Back Squeeze', 'lat_pulldown, bent_over_row, pull_up', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('8134810b-f66f-4d2c-97f4-4edfcd827d1b', 'Standing Back Pulsing Raise', 'Full Body', 'Bodyweight', '{"Full Body"}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'The Standing Back Pulsing Raise is a raising exercise that develops back strength and muscle. The standing position engages your core for stability. No equipment needed—your body provides all the resistance. A strong back improves posture, prevents injury, and balances pressing movements.', '95451201', '95451201-Standing-Back-Pulsing-Raise-(female)_Back_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:38.425788+00', '1. Stand with feet about shoulder-width apart. 2. Raise the weight in the prescribed direction for Standing Back Pulsing Raise. 3. Lower with control, maintaining tension throughout. 4. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, 'Standing', NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 72, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'pulse', 'Standing Back Pulsing Raise', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('81352023-bd5e-4c8a-97b7-77a43ade2eed', 'Step Out And Side Leg Lift', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'Elevate your training with this stepping exercise that develops speed, power, and coordination. Secondary activation of your quads provides additional muscle engagement. Plyometric training builds explosive power that transfers to sports and daily activities.', '99011201', '99011201-Step-Out-and-Side-Leg-Lift-(female)_Plyometrics_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:39.21093+00', '1. Set up a box or step platform at the appropriate height. 2. Set up in the starting position for Step Out And Side Leg Lift. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your full body. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 5. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'step_up', 'Step Out And Side Leg Lift', 'stretch_hip, dynamic_warmup, yoga_pose', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('8135d31f-0ad8-4f6e-88e9-6b4dd90ddaac', 'Rear Pulldown (Cable)', 'Back', 'Cables', '{"Lats"}'::text[], '{"Biceps","Upper Back"}'::text[], 'This pulling exercise emphasizes your lats for improved back development. You''ll also feel your biceps, upper back working to support the movement. The cable setup allows you to adjust the angle of resistance. A strong back improves posture, prevents injury, and balances pressing movements. This variation is excellent for building mind-muscle connection.', '2051201', '02051201-Cable-Rear-Pulldown_Back.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:25.737494+00', '1. Adjust the cable machine to the correct height and attachment for Cable Rear Pulldown. 2. Pull the bar/handle down toward your upper chest. 3. Drive your elbows down and back, squeezing your lats. 4. Control the weight back up without letting it yank your arms. 5. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 8, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 60, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'lat_pulldown', 'Rear Pulldown', 'pull_up, bent_over_row, cable_row, face_pull', TRUE, 'cable', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 85, 88, 30, 92),
('8139c577-9008-4d73-9d47-68be6371412f', 'Kneeling Single Hamstring Curl (Gymnastic Rings)', 'Legs', 'Gymnastic Rings', '{"Hamstrings"}'::text[], '{"Glutes"}'::text[], 'This curling movement works your hamstrings for balanced leg development. Your forearms work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. The kneeling position adds a core stability challenge. Strong legs are the foundation for athletic performance and functional fitness.', '89341201', '89341201-Kneeling-Single-Hamstring-Curl-(male)_Thighs_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:28.851102+00', '1. Kneel on the floor (use a pad for comfort if needed). 2. Keep your elbows in a fixed position throughout the movement. 3. Curl the weight up by contracting your biceps, squeezing at the top. 4. Lower with control, resisting the weight on the way down. 5. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 58, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'leg_curl', 'Kneeling Single Hamstring Curl', 'romanian_deadlift, hip_thrust', FALSE, 'gymnastic_rings', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 68, 85, 85, 70),
('813cd69a-0309-4fbe-b9cd-ad576aff7a02', 'Warrior Pose I Virabhadrasana', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors","Core"}'::text[], 'Designed to lengthen your full body, the Warrior Pose I Virabhadrasana helps improve mobility and prevent stiffness. The hips, shoulders, quads assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. Flexibility work like this enhances performance and prevents stiffness.', '9641201', '09641201-Warrior-Pose-I-Virabhadrasana-(female)_Stretching_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:39.91585+00', '1. Move into the stretch position for Warrior Pose I Virabhadrasana. 2. Ease into the stretch until you feel gentle tension (not pain). 3. Hold for 20-30 seconds, breathing deeply and relaxing into the stretch.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 1, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Stretch', 15, 2, 6, FALSE, TRUE, 'yoga', 'Warrior Pose I Virabhadrasana', 'stretch_hip, stretch_back, plank', FALSE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 1, 30, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('8147a513-d27e-4df4-99a2-b8c9fd11e614', 'Push Up Inside Leg Kick', 'Chest', 'Bodyweight', '{"Chest"}'::text[], '{"Triceps","Front Delts"}'::text[], 'Build leg strength with this pushing movement focusing on your chest. The triceps, front delts assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. A versatile bodyweight movement perfect for home or gym training. Strong legs are the foundation for athletic performance and functional fitness.', '6611201', '06611201-Push-Up-Inside-Leg-Kick_Hips_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:22.123147+00', '1. Keep your body in a straight line from head to heels throughout. 2. Lower your chest toward the floor by bending your elbows. 3. Push through your palms to return to the starting position. 4. Complete all reps with control before resting. Keep the movement smooth and controlled. Great for building strength in your chest.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 70, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'push_up', 'Push Up Inside Leg Kick', 'bench_press, chest_fly, dip', TRUE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('814c47fd-3fb3-4af5-a0ee-02968e2dfd6f', 'Roll Hamstrings Seated On Floor (Gymnastic Rings)', 'Legs', 'Gymnastic Rings', '{"Hamstrings"}'::text[], '{"Glutes"}'::text[], 'Strengthen the back of your thighs with this movement exercise. The seated position helps isolate the target muscles by removing momentum. Leg training boosts metabolism and builds functional, real-world strength.', '54311201', '54311201-Roll-Hamstrings-Sitting-on-Floor-(female)_Thighs_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:36.38616+00', '1. Position yourself on the floor for Roll Hamstrings Seated On Floor. 2. Sit on the floor with your legs positioned as required. 3. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 45, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'general_exercise', 'Roll Hamstrings Seated On Floor', 'squat, lunge, leg_press', FALSE, 'gymnastic_rings', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 68, 85, 85, 70),
('814cbd46-983b-4153-a72a-2201d8713081', 'Standing Chest Cross Stretch', 'Chest', 'Bodyweight', '{"Chest"}'::text[], '{"Front Delts"}'::text[], 'Target your chest with this stretching stretch that helps restore range of motion. The shoulders assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. The standing position engages your core for stability. Regular stretching improves flexibility, reduces injury risk, and aids recovery.', '94271201', '94271201-Standing-Chest-Cross-Stretch-(female)_Stretching_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:38.570929+00', '1. Begin in a standing position with good posture. 2. Move into the stretch position for Standing Chest Cross Stretch. 3. Ease into the stretch until you feel gentle tension (not pain). 4. Hold for 20-30 seconds, breathing deeply and relaxing into the stretch.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 3, 'Standing', NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 1, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Stretch', 42, 2, 6, FALSE, TRUE, 'stretch_general', 'Standing Chest Cross Stretch', 'stretch_shoulder, stretch_back', FALSE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 1, 30, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('8163c6f7-55f7-4ddd-9485-d9fd7e28bf3b', 'Standing Single Arm Lateral Shoulder (Resistance Band)', 'Full Body', 'Resistance Band', '{"Full Body"}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'Develop functional strength with the Resistance Band Standing Single Arm Lateral Shoulder, a comprehensive movement exercise. The standing position engages your core for stability. The band creates increasing tension as it stretches, challenging the lockout. Full body exercises are time-efficient and build functional, real-world strength.', '64401201', '64401201-Resistance-Band-Standing-Single-Arm-Lateral-Should.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:36.266593+00', '1. Secure the resistance band appropriately for Resistance Band Standing Single Arm Lateral Shoulder. 2. Begin in a standing position with good posture. 3. Complete all reps on one side, then switch to the other side. 4. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, 'Standing', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 42, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'back_exercise', 'Standing Single Arm Lateral Shoulder', 'lateral_raise, shoulder_press, front_raise', FALSE, 'band', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 60, 85, 90, 50),
('81690397-723c-40d9-862d-513fd71a456a', 'Glute Bridge Hip Abduction', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Glutes"}'::text[], '{"Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'Build stronger glutes with this bridging movement focused on hip extension. The glutes assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. No equipment needed—your body provides all the resistance. Leg training boosts metabolism and builds functional, real-world strength.', '58701201', '58701201-Glute-Bridge-Hip-Abduction-(female)_Hips_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:33.778367+00', '1. Drive through your heels to lift your hips toward the ceiling. 2. Squeeze your glutes hard at the top of the movement. 3. Lower your hips back down with control. 4. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions. Focus on the mind-muscle connection. Include this in your legs training.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 70, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'glute_bridge', 'Glute Bridge Hip Abduction', 'hip_thrust, romanian_deadlift', TRUE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('817c26f8-bc44-4b9b-9d50-cb5d31df9939', 'Air Walk (Machine)', 'Legs', 'Lever Machine', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'Enhance your stamina and burn calories with this effective cardio movement. The machine guides your movement path for safer, more controlled repetitions. Regular cardio training builds the aerobic base for better overall fitness.', '82191201', '82191201-Lever-Air-Walk-(male)_Cardio_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:22.536005+00', '1. Adjust the machine settings (seat height, weight, pads) to fit your body for Lever Air Walk. 2. Set up in the starting position for Lever Air Walk. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your cardio. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 5. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 58, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'walking', 'Lever Air Walk', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'machine', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 80, 75, 20, 88),
('8199f2ec-614d-4982-b389-5ff471297f18', 'Front Plank To Toe Tap', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Shoulders","Lower Back"}'::text[], 'Build leg strength with this stabilization movement focusing on your abs. The shoulders, lower back assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. A versatile bodyweight movement perfect for home or gym training. Strong legs are the foundation for athletic performance and functional fitness. Progress gradually by increasing resistance over time.', '106971201', '106971201-Front-Plank-to-Toe-Tap-(female)_Hips_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:33.640031+00', '1. Hold your body in a straight line from head to heels. 2. Don''t let your hips sag or pike up—engage your core and glutes. 3. Breathe steadily while maintaining the position. 4. Complete all reps with control before resting. Ensure full range of motion on each rep. A solid choice for legs day.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 70, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'plank', 'Front Plank To Toe Tap', 'side_plank, dead_bug, hollow_hold', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('819ebee3-9c08-48e8-8aec-a28e1b4c96c4', 'Incline Powell Raise (Dumbbell)', 'Shoulders', 'Dumbbells, Incline Bench', '{"Shoulders"}'::text[], '{"Traps"}'::text[], 'This raising exercise works your delts for improved shoulder strength and aesthetics. Using an incline changes the angle of resistance for varied muscle recruitment. Using dumbbells requires more stabilization than barbell variations. Strong shoulders improve overhead strength and support nearly all upper body movements.', '72521201', '72521201-Dumbbell-Incline-Powell-Raise-(male)_Shoulders_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:24.941834+00', '1. Select a pair of dumbbells at an appropriate weight for Dumbbell Incline Powell Raise. 2. Raise the weight in the prescribed direction for Dumbbell Incline Powell Raise. 3. Lower with control, maintaining tension throughout. 4. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 85, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'general_exercise', 'Incline Powell Raise', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', TRUE, 'dumbbell', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 92, 90, 92, 90),
('81a8ac7e-8f94-4404-b2f1-85543802c877', 'Single Leg Split Squat (TRX)', 'Legs', 'TRX', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'Build stronger quads with this squatting movement that develops leg drive and power. Secondary activation of your glutes, hamstrings provides additional muscle engagement. Suspension training adds instability, increasing core activation throughout. Lower body strength improves everything from walking to heavy compound lifts.', '11001201', '11001201-Suspender-Single-Leg-Split-Squat-(female)_Hips_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:39.472701+00', '1. Adjust the TRX/suspension straps to the appropriate length for Suspender Single Leg Split Squat. 2. Push your hips back and bend your knees to lower your body. 3. Keep your chest up and knees tracking over your toes. 4. Drive through your heels to stand back up, squeezing your glutes at the top. 5. Complete all reps on one side, then switch to the other side. 6. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', 'Squat', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 70, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'split_squat', 'Suspender Single Leg Split Squat', 'lunge, bulgarian_split_squat, squat', FALSE, 'trx', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 68, 85, 85, 70),
('81abdaa9-1541-4b8e-b9f1-bebecec3de93', 'Weighted Chains Lying Bench Fly', 'Chest', 'Bodyweight', '{"Chest"}'::text[], '{"Front Delts"}'::text[], 'This flying exercise focuses on your pectorals for improved chest strength and development. You''ll also feel your front delts working to support the movement. The lying position provides back support and helps isolate the target muscles. Chest strength improves pushing power for sports, daily tasks, and other lifts.', '42001201', '42001201-Weighted-Chains-Lying-Bench-Fly-(male)_Chest_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:21.608253+00', '1. Lie down in the appropriate position for Weighted Chains Lying Bench Fly. 2. With a slight bend in your elbows, move the weight in a wide arc. 3. Squeeze your chest muscles at the center/top of the movement. 4. Return with control, feeling the stretch at the bottom. 5. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, 'Lying', NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 70, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'chest_fly', 'Weighted Chains Lying Bench Fly', 'bench_press, incline_press, push_up', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('81aee896-f7bf-4227-baab-78bffe2e66de', 'Bird Dog Plank', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Shoulders","Lower Back"}'::text[], 'Build lower back resilience with this stabilization movement that supports spinal health. You''ll also feel your glutes, abs working to support the movement. No equipment needed—your body provides all the resistance. Building core stability helps with everything from heavy deadlifts to daily activities.', '90021201', '90021201-Bird-Dog-Plank-(male)_Waist_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:20.667107+00', '1. Hold your body in a straight line from head to heels. 2. Don''t let your hips sag or pike up—engage your core and glutes. 3. Breathe steadily while maintaining the position. 4. Complete all reps with control before resting. Keep your shoulders relaxed and away from your ears.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 70, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'bird_dog', 'Bird Dog Plank', 'crunch, leg_raise, russian_twist, dead_bug', TRUE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('81b29fea-5621-481d-b3b8-0c4f5f3a0630', 'Lying Single Arm Rear Lateral Raise (Dumbbell)', 'Shoulders', 'Dumbbells, Flat Bench', '{"Side Delts"}'::text[], '{"Traps"}'::text[], 'This raising exercise works your lateral delts for improved shoulder strength and aesthetics. The lying position provides back support and helps isolate the target muscles. Using dumbbells requires more stabilization than barbell variations. Shoulder development enhances both performance and upper body aesthetics.', '101731201', '101731201-Dumbbell-Lying-One-Arm-Rear-Lateral-Raise-(female.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:32.914483+00', '1. Select an appropriate weight dumbbell and hold it in one hand. 2. Lie down in the appropriate position for Dumbbell Lying One Arm Rear Lateral Raise. 3. Raise your arms out to the sides until parallel to the floor. 4. Lower with control, maintaining tension throughout. 5. Complete all reps on one side, then switch to the other side. 6. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, 'Lying', NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 87, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'lateral_raise', 'Lying Single Arm Rear Lateral Raise', 'shoulder_press, front_raise, rear_delt', TRUE, 'dumbbell', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 92, 90, 92, 90),
('81b67b74-b030-4aeb-9f86-661480970f4c', 'Side Step Triceps Kickback', 'Arms', 'Bodyweight', '{"Triceps"}'::text[], '{"Rear Delts"}'::text[], 'The Side Step Triceps Kickback is an explosive exercise that combines cardiovascular training with dynamic kicking movements. Your hamstrings work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. Develops fast-twitch muscle fibers for quicker, more powerful movements.', '92571201', '92571201-Side-Step-Tricep-Kickback-(female)_Plyometrics_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:37.303932+00', '1. Set up a box or step platform at the appropriate height. 2. Keep your upper arm stationary and extend your forearm back. 3. Squeeze at full extension, then return with control. 4. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'tricep_kickback', 'Side Step Triceps Kickback', 'tricep_pushdown, tricep_extension', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('81b6be94-4c72-4d64-aff2-fc22eb04d3ec', 'Standing Leg Raise (Machine)', 'Core', 'Lever Machine', '{"Lower Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'Build leg strength with this raising movement focusing on your abs. Your hip flexors work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. The standing position engages your core for stability. Machine exercises are great for isolating muscles and training to failure safely. Strong legs are the foundation for athletic performance and functional fitness.', '10361201', '10361201-Lever-Standing-Leg-Raise_Hips_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:29.242428+00', '1. Adjust the machine settings (seat height, weight, pads) to fit your body for Lever Standing Leg Raise. 2. Stand tall with your feet firmly planted. 3. Keeping legs mostly straight, raise them toward the ceiling. 4. Lower with control, stopping just before touching down. 5. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, 'Standing', NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 80, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'leg_raise', 'Lever Standing Leg Raise', 'crunch, plank, v_up', FALSE, 'machine', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 80, 75, 20, 88),
('81bde4bf-4aeb-4e8a-b9bc-6879a2d497ac', 'Crossover Variation (Cable)', 'Full Body', 'Cables', '{"Full Body"}'::text[], '{"Shoulders","Core"}'::text[], 'Elevate your training with this movement exercise that develops speed, power, and coordination. Secondary activation of your shoulders, core provides additional muscle engagement. Cables provide constant tension throughout the full range of motion. Great for improving athletic performance, burning calories, and building conditioning.', '1551201', '01551201-Cable-Crossover-Variation_Chest_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:20.982555+00', '1. Adjust the cable machine to the correct height and attachment for Cable Crossover Variation. 2. Set up in the starting position for Cable Crossover Variation. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your full body. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 5. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 8, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 60, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'chest_fly', 'Crossover Variation', 'bench_press, incline_press, push_up', FALSE, 'cable', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 85, 88, 30, 92),
('81d99104-d5c5-4c35-8fb7-ac311dd737c0', 'Arm Circle Stepback', 'Full Body', 'Bodyweight', '{"Full Body"}'::text[], '{"Quads","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'A challenging plyometric exercise, the Arm Circle Stepback builds reactive power and improves conditioning. Plyometric training builds explosive power that transfers to sports and daily activities.', '56171201', '56171201-Arm-Circle-Stepback-(female)_Plyometrics_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:30.54809+00', '1. Set up a box or step platform at the appropriate height. 2. Set up in the starting position for Arm Circle Stepback. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your full body. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 5. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, 'Compound', 'Bilateral', NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, 'Standing', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'back_exercise', 'Arm Circle Stepback', 'high_knees, butt_kicks, jumping_jack', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('81df338e-984f-4c73-8241-0ccc49f84858', 'Side Seated Single Arm Rear Delt Fly (Machine)', 'Shoulders', 'Fly Machine', '{"Rear Delts"}'::text[], '{"Upper Back","Traps"}'::text[], 'Build stronger shoulders with this flying movement focusing on your rear delts. You''ll also feel your upper back working to support the movement. Being seated provides stability, allowing you to focus on the working muscles. Machine exercises are great for isolating muscles and training to failure safely. Shoulder development enhances both performance and upper body aesthetics.', '89901201', '89901201-Lever-Side-Seated-Single-Arm-Rear-Delt-Fly-(male)_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:22.938497+00', '1. Adjust the machine settings (seat height, weight, pads) to fit your body for Lever Side Seated Single Arm Rear Delt Fly. 2. Sit with your back supported, core engaged, feet flat on the floor. 3. With a slight bend in your elbows, move the weight in a wide arc. 4. Squeeze your chest muscles at the center/top of the movement. 5. Return with control, feeling the stretch at the bottom. 6. Complete all reps on one side, then switch to the other side. 7. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, 'Seated', NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 75, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'rear_delt', 'Lever Side Seated Single Arm Rear Delt Fly', 'bench_press, incline_bench_press, push_up', FALSE, 'machine', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 80, 75, 20, 88),
('81e438fa-224f-4982-9452-f48184681865', 'Standing Elbow Together Scoop', 'Full Body', 'Bodyweight', '{"Full Body"}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'The Standing Elbow Together Scoop is an arm movement exercise targeting your full body. The standing position engages your core for stability. This bodyweight exercise requires no equipment and can be done anywhere. Dedicated arm training builds both strength and muscular definition.', '87401201', '87401201-Standing-Elbow-Together-Scoop-(male)_Upper-Arms_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:28.52454+00', '1. Stand with feet about shoulder-width apart. 2. Set up in the starting position for Standing Elbow Together Scoop. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your full body. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 5. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, 'Standing', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 52, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'general_exercise', 'Standing Elbow Together Scoop', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('81e530d9-0c1a-4405-9b93-afd7054c769f', 'Seated Lats Stretch (Chair)', 'Back', 'Chair', '{"Lats"}'::text[], '{"Lower Back"}'::text[], 'The Seated Lats Stretch On A Chair provides a deep stretch for your lats, ideal for recovery and mobility work. The shoulders assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. Being seated provides stability, allowing you to focus on the working muscles. Regular stretching improves flexibility, reduces injury risk, and aids recovery.', '104671201', '104671201-Seated-Lats-Stretch-on-a-Chair-(male)_Stretching_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:26.146796+00', '1. Position yourself with a sturdy chair for support or as part of the movement. 2. Sit with your back supported, core engaged, feet flat on the floor. 3. Move into the stretch position for Seated Lats Stretch On A Chair. 4. Ease into the stretch until you feel gentle tension (not pain). 5. Hold for 20-30 seconds, breathing deeply and relaxing into the stretch.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 3, 'Seated', NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 1, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Stretch', 27, 2, 6, FALSE, TRUE, 'stretch_general', 'Seated Lats Stretch On A Chair', 'stretch_hip, stretch_back', FALSE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 1, 30, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('81e7154d-9a60-4e01-b4e5-d9e2371fa223', 'Decline Crunch (Decline Bench)', 'Core', 'Decline Bench', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'Strengthen your midsection with this crunching movement that works your abs. You''ll also feel your hip flexors working to support the movement. The decline position targets the lower portion of the muscles more intensely. Building core stability helps with everything from heavy deadlifts to daily activities.', '70811201', '70811201-Decline-Crunch-(female)_Waist_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:32.501166+00', '1. Curl your shoulders off the floor by contracting your abs. 2. Don''t pull on your neck—focus on the abdominal contraction. 3. Lower with control, maintaining some tension. 4. Complete all reps with control before resting. Keep tension on the target muscles throughout.', 'Crunch', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 12, 20, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 73, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'crunch', 'Decline Crunch', 'leg_raise, plank, russian_twist, v_up', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('81f2d498-0657-4ea9-9df9-2e4b1a909a1e', 'Incline Wide Bench Press - Reverse Grip (Barbell)', 'Chest', 'Barbell, Incline Bench', '{"Chest"}'::text[], '{"Front Delts","Triceps"}'::text[], 'This pressing exercise focuses on your pectorals for improved chest strength and development. You''ll also feel your triceps, front delts working to support the movement. Using an incline changes the angle of resistance for varied muscle recruitment. Barbells enable bilateral loading for building raw strength. A well-developed chest contributes to upper body strength and aesthetics.', '11731201', '11731201-Barbell-Incline-Wide-Reverse-Grip-Bench-Press_Ches.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:22.755209+00', '1. Load a barbell and set it on a bench rack at the appropriate height. 2. Use a wide grip (wider than shoulder-width) for this variation. 3. Lower the weight toward your chest with control. 4. Press the weight up until your arms are extended (don''t lock elbows). 5. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 10, 10, NULL, 4, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 5, 8, NULL, 8, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 100, 7, 9, TRUE, FALSE, 'bench_press', 'Incline Wide Bench Press - Reverse Grip', 'Incline Wide Bench Press - Reverse Grip', TRUE, 'barbell', FALSE, 4, 120, 4, 95, 80, 65, 95),
('81fb4e3d-f8d4-4129-b90a-ade9d6660d93', 'Shoulder Tap Push Up', 'Chest', 'Bodyweight', '{"Chest"}'::text[], '{"Triceps","Front Delts"}'::text[], 'Elevate your training with this pushing exercise that develops speed, power, and coordination. Secondary activation of your triceps, front delts provides additional muscle engagement. No equipment needed—your body provides all the resistance. Plyometric training builds explosive power that transfers to sports and daily activities.', '6991201', '06991201-Shoulder-Tap-Push-up_Plyometrics-FIX_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:30.099411+00', '1. Keep your body in a straight line from head to heels throughout. 2. Lower your chest toward the floor by bending your elbows. 3. Push through your palms to return to the starting position. 4. Complete all reps with control before resting. Keep your core engaged for stability.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 70, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'push_up', 'Shoulder Tap Push Up', 'bench_press, chest_fly, dip', TRUE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('8200bd25-eec5-43f0-88d4-36734666e160', 'Cossack Squat (Dumbbell)', 'Legs', 'Dumbbells', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'The Dumbbell Cossack Squats is a squatting exercise that primarily loads your quadriceps. You''ll also feel your glutes, hamstrings working to support the movement. The dumbbell variation provides freedom of movement and greater range of motion. Lower body strength improves everything from walking to heavy compound lifts.', '47321201', '47321201-Dumbbell-Cossack-Squats-(VERSION-2)-(male)_Thighs_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:22.644637+00', '1. Select a pair of dumbbells at an appropriate weight for Dumbbell Cossack Squats. 2. Push your hips back and bend your knees to lower your body. 3. Keep your chest up and knees tracking over your toes. 4. Drive through your heels to stand back up, squeezing your glutes at the top. 5. Complete all reps with control before resting.', 'Squat', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 10, 10, NULL, 4, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 5, 8, NULL, 9, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 97, 7, 9, TRUE, FALSE, 'squat', 'Cossack Squat', 'leg_press, front_squat, goblet_squat, lunge, leg_extension', FALSE, 'dumbbell', FALSE, 4, 120, 5, 92, 90, 92, 90),
('820b20ac-1d6f-4e4f-ac2b-e545d66a0062', '2 Point Bench Press (Dumbbell)', 'Chest', 'Dumbbells, Flat Bench', '{"Chest"}'::text[], '{"Triceps","Front Delts"}'::text[], 'The Dumbbell 2 Point Bench Press is a pressing exercise that targets your chest muscles. The triceps, front delts assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. The dumbbell variation provides freedom of movement and greater range of motion. A well-developed chest contributes to upper body strength and aesthetics.', '80041201', '80041201-Dumbbell-2-Point-Bench-Press-(male)_Chest_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:23.172397+00', '1. Select a pair of dumbbells at an appropriate weight for Dumbbell 2 Point Bench Press. 2. Lower the weight toward your chest with control. 3. Press the weight up until your arms are extended (don''t lock elbows). 4. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 10, 10, NULL, 4, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 5, 8, NULL, 8, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 97, 7, 9, TRUE, FALSE, 'bench_press', '2 Point Bench Press', 'incline_press, decline_press, chest_fly, push_up, dip', FALSE, 'dumbbell', FALSE, 4, 120, 4, 92, 90, 92, 90),
('821d4327-86f1-448c-a843-284a584647c1', 'Pullover (Stability Ball, Dumbbell)', 'Chest', 'Dumbbells, Stability Ball, Flat Bench', '{"Chest"}'::text[], '{"Lats","Triceps"}'::text[], 'Build a stronger chest with this pulling movement that develops pressing power. Your lats, triceps work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. Dumbbells allow each arm to work independently, helping correct imbalances. A well-developed chest contributes to upper body strength and aesthetics.', '26211201', '26211201-Dumbbell-Pullover-on-Exercise-Ball-(female)_Chest_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:33.034396+00', '1. Select a pair of dumbbells at an appropriate weight for Dumbbell Pullover. 2. With arms slightly bent, lower the weight behind your head in an arc. 3. Pull the weight back over your chest, squeezing your lats and chest. 4. Complete all reps with control before resting. Ensure full range of motion on each rep.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 8, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 46, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'pullover', 'Pullover', 'bicep_curl, face_pull, lat_pulldown', TRUE, 'dumbbell', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 92, 90, 92, 90),
('8220a3a5-40a4-48f2-a731-c06c0cf14a63', 'High To Side Hip Stretch', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Hips"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'Designed to lengthen your hips, the High To Side Hip Stretch helps improve mobility and prevent stiffness. You''ll also feel your glutes working to support the movement. Include this in your routine for better mobility and reduced muscle tension.', '103751201', '103751201-High-to-Side-Hip-Stretch-(male)_Stretching_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:24.831811+00', '1. Move into the stretch position for High To Side Hip Stretch. 2. Ease into the stretch until you feel gentle tension (not pain). 3. Hold for 20-30 seconds, breathing deeply and relaxing into the stretch. 4. Switch sides and repeat for equal time.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 1, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Stretch', 40, 2, 6, FALSE, TRUE, 'hip_stretch', 'High To Side Hip Stretch', 'stretch_hamstring, stretch_glute, stretch_back', FALSE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 1, 30, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('8227218f-30e1-4beb-9350-c6e869c2c1e5', 'Hip And Knee Flexion Squatting Stretch', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'The Hip And Knee Flexion Squatting Stretch provides a deep stretch for your hips, ideal for recovery and mobility work. Secondary activation of your glutes, hamstrings provides additional muscle engagement. Flexibility work like this enhances performance and prevents stiffness.', '19311201', '19311201-Hip-And-Knee-Flexion-Squatting-Stretch-(female)_Hi.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:34.073704+00', '1. Push your hips back and bend your knees to lower your body. 2. Keep your chest up and knees tracking over your toes. 3. Drive through your heels to stand back up, squeezing your glutes at the top. Engage your stabilizer muscles for better control. Perfect for targeting your hips.', 'Squat', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 1, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Stretch', 75, 2, 6, FALSE, TRUE, 'stretch_general', 'Hip And Knee Flexion Squatting Stretch', 'leg_press, leg_extension, leg_curl, lunge, front_squat, hack_squat', FALSE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 1, 30, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('82290361-3afe-43af-bb20-95e29b0c29d9', 'Split Stance Bicep Curl (Dumbbell)', 'Arms', 'Dumbbells', '{"Biceps"}'::text[], '{"Forearms"}'::text[], 'This curling exercise focuses on your biceps for improved arm size and strength. Your forearms work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. The dumbbell variation provides freedom of movement and greater range of motion. Dedicated arm training builds both strength and muscular definition. Focus on controlled form throughout each repetition.', '74781201', '74781201-Dumbbell-Split-Stance-Biceps-Curl-(male)_Upper-Arm.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:27.504261+00', '1. Select a pair of dumbbells at an appropriate weight for Dumbbell Split Stance Biceps Curl. 2. Keep your elbows in a fixed position throughout the movement. 3. Curl the weight up by contracting your biceps, squeezing at the top. 4. Lower with control, resisting the weight on the way down. 5. Complete all reps with control before resting.', 'Curl', 'Pull', NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 92, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'bicep_curl', 'Split Stance Biceps Curl', 'hammer_curl, preacher_curl, cable_curl', TRUE, 'dumbbell', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 92, 90, 92, 90),
('8233f5c3-da0c-4181-b0d9-1974d4c23f07', 'Single Leg Kickback Bent Position (Resistance Band)', 'Legs', 'Resistance Band', '{"Glutes"}'::text[], '{"Rear Delts"}'::text[], 'Develop your posterior chain with this kicking movement that emphasizes the glutes. Your hamstrings work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. Bands are joint-friendly and portable, perfect for any training environment. Leg training boosts metabolism and builds functional, real-world strength.', '21601201', '21601201-Resistance-Band-One-Leg-Kickback-(Bent-Position)-(female)_Hips.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:36.128549+00', '1. Secure the resistance band appropriately for Resistance Band One Leg Kickback. 2. Keep your upper arm stationary and extend your forearm back. 3. Squeeze at full extension, then return with control. 4. Complete all reps on one side, then switch to the other side. 5. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 42, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'tricep_kickback', 'Single Leg Kickback', 'squat, lunge, leg_press', FALSE, 'band', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 60, 85, 90, 50),
('825322f8-2c36-4cbf-9a2a-3495a59a7c5d', 'Revolved Triangle Pose', 'Full Body', 'Bodyweight', '{"Full Body"}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'Designed to lengthen your full body, the Revolved Triangle Pose helps improve mobility and prevent stiffness. Flexibility work like this enhances performance and prevents stiffness.', '59011201', '59011201-Revolved-Triangle-Pose-(female)_Stretching_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:36.38616+00', '1. Move into the stretch position for Revolved Triangle Pose. 2. Ease into the stretch until you feel gentle tension (not pain). 3. Hold for 20-30 seconds, breathing deeply and relaxing into the stretch.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 1, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Stretch', 50, 2, 6, FALSE, TRUE, 'yoga', 'Revolved Triangle Pose', 'stretch_hip, stretch_back, plank', FALSE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 1, 30, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('8259c082-c21a-4842-a5d4-5155b4057736', 'Butt Kick With Shoulder Tap', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], '{"Calves"}'::text[], 'A challenging plyometric exercise, the Butt Kick With Shoulder Tap builds reactive power and improves conditioning. Secondary activation of your hamstrings provides additional muscle engagement. A versatile bodyweight movement perfect for home or gym training. Plyometric training builds explosive power that transfers to sports and daily activities.', '60871201', '60871201-Butt-Kick-with-Shoulder-Tap-(female)_Plyometrics_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:31.723232+00', '1. Set up in the starting position for Butt Kick With Shoulder Tap. 2. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your full body. 3. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 4. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'glute_kickback', 'Butt Kick With Shoulder Tap', 'high_knees, jumping_jack, running', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('82629364-3b3f-4d3a-8b64-21b05f8a038c', 'Squat And 5 Bounces', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'Build stronger quads with this squatting movement that develops leg drive and power. The glutes, hamstrings assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. No equipment needed—your body provides all the resistance. Lower body strength improves everything from walking to heavy compound lifts. Perfect for including in both strength and hypertrophy programs.', '63091201', '63091201-Squat-and-5-Bounces-(female)_Thighs_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:38.153182+00', '1. Push your hips back and bend your knees to lower your body. 2. Keep your chest up and knees tracking over your toes. 3. Drive through your heels to stand back up, squeezing your glutes at the top. 4. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions. Focus on maintaining proper breathing throughout. Beneficial for overall legs development.', 'Squat', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 85, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'squat', 'Squat And 5 Bounces', 'leg_press, front_squat, goblet_squat, lunge, leg_extension', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('82706f20-f2d0-4ba5-bbd8-976f4ab0a58d', 'Rear Lunge (Kettlebell)', 'Legs', 'Kettlebell', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'The Kettlebell Rear Lunge is a lunging exercise that primarily loads your quadriceps. You''ll also feel your glutes, hamstrings working to support the movement. The kettlebell grip position adds a unique training stimulus. Strong legs are the foundation for athletic performance and functional fitness.', '50701201', '50701201-Kettlebell-Rear-Lunge_Thighs-FIX_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:29.61214+00', '1. Select an appropriately weighted kettlebell for Kettlebell Rear Lunge. 2. Step forward into a lunge until both knees are at about 90 degrees. 3. Push through your front/working leg to return to the starting position. 4. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 78, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'lunge', 'Rear Lunge', 'split_squat, step_up, squat', FALSE, 'kettlebell', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 75, 88, 88, 78),
('8286e181-77f9-42f1-97dc-5039236a53d1', 'Wide Mountain Hop', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Calves"}'::text[], 'This dynamic movement movement gets your heart rate up while developing explosive strength. A versatile bodyweight movement perfect for home or gym training. Develops fast-twitch muscle fibers for quicker, more powerful movements. Control the negative portion for maximum muscle engagement.', '71431201', '71431201-Wide-Mountain-Hop-(male)_Plyometrics_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:23.172397+00', '1. Set up in the starting position for Wide Mountain Hop. 2. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your full body. 3. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 4. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 4, NULL, 8, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 7, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Plyometrics', 50, 9, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'hop', 'Wide Mountain Hop', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('8287ec12-874f-4960-92fc-ffa5c6d8d046', 'Lunge Stretch', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'Target the front of your thighs with this lunging exercise for quad development. Your glutes, hamstrings work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. This bodyweight exercise requires no equipment and can be done anywhere. Lower body strength improves everything from walking to heavy compound lifts.', '49301201', '49301201-Lunge-Stretch-(female)_Thighs_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:35.010404+00', '1. Step forward into a lunge until both knees are at about 90 degrees. 2. Push through your front/working leg to return to the starting position. 3. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout. Start with lighter weight to perfect your form. Great for building strength in your quads.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 1, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Stretch', 60, 2, 6, FALSE, TRUE, 'hip_stretch', 'Lunge Stretch', 'squat, split_squat, step_up, leg_press', FALSE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 1, 30, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('8298e85e-7307-4143-a631-2f5968e0146a', 'Lying Slight Bent Back Leg Raise - Alternating', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Lower Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'This raising exercise engages your abs for improved core stability and strength. You''ll also feel your hip flexors working to support the movement. The lying position provides back support and helps isolate the target muscles. This bodyweight exercise requires no equipment and can be done anywhere. Core strength is foundational for athletic performance and injury prevention.', '94391201', '94391201-Lying-Alternating-Slight-Bent-Back-Leg-Raise-(fema.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:35.010404+00', '1. Lie down in the appropriate position for Lying Alternating Slight Bent Back Leg Raise. 2. Keeping legs mostly straight, raise them toward the ceiling. 3. Lower with control, stopping just before touching down. 4. Alternate between sides/arms/legs with each repetition. 5. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, 'Lying', NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 70, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'leg_raise', 'Lying Slight Bent Back Leg Raise - Alternating', 'crunch, plank, v_up', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('82b38c53-2b27-4242-8920-d07bf8569d40', 'Partner Assisted Pull Up (Pull-Up Bar)', 'Back', 'Pull-Up Bar', '{"Lats"}'::text[], '{"Biceps","Upper Back"}'::text[], 'This pulling exercise emphasizes your lats for improved back development. Secondary activation of your biceps, upper back provides additional muscle engagement. A versatile bodyweight movement perfect for home or gym training. A strong back improves posture, prevents injury, and balances pressing movements. Perfect for including in both strength and hypertrophy programs.', '95101201', '95101201-Partner-Assisted-Pull-up-(female)_Back_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:35.667316+00', '1. Pull yourself up by driving your elbows down and back. 2. Continue until your chin clears the bar, then lower with control to a full hang. 3. Complete all reps with control before resting. Keep your shoulders relaxed and away from your ears. Beneficial for overall back development.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 70, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'pull_up', 'Partner Assisted Pull Up', 'lat_pulldown, bent_over_row, bicep_curl', TRUE, 'pull_up_bar', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('82bd977a-67a3-407f-b9e1-00ac9fd6d1a6', 'Walking On Spot Punch', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'The Walking On Spot Punch is an explosive exercise that combines cardiovascular training with dynamic stepping movements. Secondary activation of your shoulders provides additional muscle engagement. This bodyweight exercise requires no equipment and can be done anywhere. Develops fast-twitch muscle fibers for quicker, more powerful movements.', '98381201', '98381201-Walking-on-Spot-Punch-(female)_Plyometrics_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:39.91585+00', '1. Set up in the starting position for Walking On Spot Punch. 2. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your full body. 3. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 4. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 2, 2, NULL, 10, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 3, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Cardio', 50, 9, 8, FALSE, TRUE, 'walking', 'Walking On Spot Punch', 'core_exercise, shoulder_exercise, burpee', FALSE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 1, 60, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('82c53356-0ab7-40a8-8c9a-0d9003cb44f9', 'Back Hugs Chest Stretch', 'Chest', 'Bodyweight', '{"Chest"}'::text[], '{"Front Delts"}'::text[], 'This stretch specifically works on your chest, promoting flexibility and reducing muscle tightness. Your shoulders work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. Regular stretching improves flexibility, reduces injury risk, and aids recovery.', '94261201', '94261201-Back-Hugs-Chest-Stretch-(female)_Stretching_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:30.685158+00', '1. Move into the stretch position for Back Hugs Chest Stretch. 2. Ease into the stretch until you feel gentle tension (not pain). 3. Hold for 20-30 seconds, breathing deeply and relaxing into the stretch.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 1, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Stretch', 40, 2, 6, FALSE, TRUE, 'chest_stretch', 'Back Hugs Chest Stretch', 'stretch_shoulder, stretch_back', FALSE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 1, 30, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('82d39e9b-c453-4fb0-8ef4-a4cdcb32c175', 'Standing Chest Press (Band)', 'Chest', 'Resistance Band', '{"Chest"}'::text[], '{"Triceps","Front Delts"}'::text[], 'This pressing exercise focuses on your pectorals for improved chest strength and development. The triceps, front delts assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. The standing position engages your core for stability. The band creates increasing tension as it stretches, challenging the lockout. A well-developed chest contributes to upper body strength and aesthetics.', '9201201', '09201201-Band-Standing-Chest-Press-(female)_Chest_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:30.887491+00', '1. Secure the resistance band appropriately for Band Standing Chest Press. 2. Stand tall with your feet firmly planted. 3. Lower the weight toward your chest with control. 4. Press the weight up until your arms are extended (don''t lock elbows). 5. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, 'Standing', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 77, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'bench_press', 'Standing Chest Press', 'incline_press, decline_press, chest_fly, push_up, dip', FALSE, 'band', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 60, 85, 90, 50),
('82d946bd-586c-43e0-80ce-dd3bfd092c5e', 'Deep Lunge To Hamstring Stretch (Gymnastic Rings)', 'Legs', 'Gymnastic Rings', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'Target your hamstrings with this lunging stretch that helps restore range of motion. The lower back assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. Include this in your routine for better mobility and reduced muscle tension.', '81621201', '81621201-Deep-Lunge-to-Hamstring-Stretch-(female)_Stretchin.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:32.501166+00', '1. Step forward into a lunge until both knees are at about 90 degrees. 2. Push through your front/working leg to return to the starting position. 3. Move into the stretch position for Deep Lunge To Hamstring Stretch. 4. Ease into the stretch until you feel gentle tension (not pain). 5. Hold for 20-30 seconds, breathing deeply and relaxing into the stretch.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 1, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Stretch', 48, 2, 6, FALSE, TRUE, 'hamstring_stretch', 'Deep Lunge To Hamstring Stretch', 'squat, split_squat, step_up, leg_press', FALSE, 'gymnastic_rings', TRUE, 1, 30, 2, 68, 85, 85, 70),
('82e38e12-e979-43b1-94e8-44c364a69023', 'Seated Floor Side To Side Leg Raise In Out Crunch', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'The Seated Floor Side To Side Leg Raise In Out Crunch is a lower body raising exercise that targets your hip abductors. Secondary activation of your glutes provides additional muscle engagement. The seated position helps isolate the target muscles by removing momentum. Leg training boosts metabolism and builds functional, real-world strength.', '93381201', '93381201-Sitting-Floor-Side-to-Side-Leg-Raise-In-Out-Crunch.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:26.271124+00', '1. Position yourself on the floor for Seated Floor Side To Side Leg Raise In Out Crunch. 2. Sit on the floor with your legs positioned as required. 3. Curl your shoulders off the floor by contracting your abs. 4. Don''t pull on your neck—focus on the abdominal contraction. 5. Lower with control, maintaining some tension. 6. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 12, 20, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 65, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'leg_raise', 'Seated Floor Side To Side Leg Raise In Out Crunch', 'crunch, plank, v_up', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('82ee70dc-676c-4b25-91d5-48f1e26ef7d9', 'Lying Single Arm Press (Dumbbell)', 'Chest', 'Dumbbells, Flat Bench', '{"Chest"}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'The Dumbbell Lying One Arm Press is a pressing exercise that targets your chest muscles. The lying position provides back support and helps isolate the target muscles. Dumbbells allow each arm to work independently, helping correct imbalances. Chest strength improves pushing power for sports, daily tasks, and other lifts.', '3431201', '03431201-Dumbbell-Lying-One-Arm-Press_Chest_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:21.995567+00', '1. Select an appropriate weight dumbbell and hold it in one hand. 2. Lie down in the appropriate position for Dumbbell Lying One Arm Press. 3. Lower the weight toward your chest with control. 4. Press the weight up until your arms are extended (don''t lock elbows). 5. Complete all reps on one side, then switch to the other side. 6. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 7, 8, NULL, 5, 'Lying', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 77, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'arm_exercise', 'Lying Single Arm Press', 'bicep_curl, tricep_extension, hammer_curl', TRUE, 'dumbbell', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 92, 90, 92, 90),
('82fe3921-926b-44e8-9450-05ef91be1a60', 'Hundred', 'Full Body', 'Bodyweight', '{"Full Body"}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'Use this stretch to open up your full body area and enhance overall flexibility. Include this in your routine for better mobility and reduced muscle tension. Keep your core engaged throughout the exercise. Consistency with this movement will yield noticeable results.', '28461201', '28461201-Hundred_Pilates.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:34.073704+00', '1. Move into the stretch position for Hundred. 2. Ease into the stretch until you feel gentle tension (not pain). 3. Hold for 20-30 seconds, breathing deeply and relaxing into the stretch.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'general_exercise', 'Hundred', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('830b2117-02e4-4a0b-9e16-720c45ad4bb3', 'Knee In And Out Crunch', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'This crunching exercise engages your abs for improved core stability and strength. Your hip flexors work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. No equipment needed—your body provides all the resistance. Core strength is foundational for athletic performance and injury prevention.', '77521201', '77521201-Knee-In-and-Out-Crunch-(male)_Waist_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:24.307972+00', '1. Curl your shoulders off the floor by contracting your abs. 2. Don''t pull on your neck—focus on the abdominal contraction. 3. Lower with control, maintaining some tension. 4. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout. Ensure full range of motion on each rep.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 12, 20, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 70, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'crunch', 'Knee In And Out Crunch', 'leg_raise, plank, russian_twist, v_up', TRUE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('8310c372-00da-49ef-bd31-65da67ff4567', 'Side Duck Side', 'Full Body', 'Bodyweight', '{"Full Body"}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'Build power and athleticism with this high-intensity movement exercise that challenges your entire body. No equipment needed—your body provides all the resistance. Develops fast-twitch muscle fibers for quicker, more powerful movements. Can be modified for beginners or progressed for advanced athletes.', '76541201', '76541201-Side-Duck-Side-(male)_Plyometrics_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:24.941834+00', '1. Set up in the starting position for Side Duck Side. 2. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your full body. 3. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 4. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'general_exercise', 'Side Duck Side', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('832af955-9aab-415e-9085-d964befe5311', 'Seated Single Arm Concentration Curl (Cable)', 'Arms', 'Cables', '{"Biceps"}'::text[], '{"Forearms"}'::text[], 'This curling exercise focuses on your biceps for improved arm size and strength. The forearms assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. The seated position helps isolate the target muscles by removing momentum. Cables provide constant tension throughout the full range of motion. Arm strength supports grip, pulling, and pushing in compound movements.', '97431201', '97431201-Cable-Seated-One-Arm-Concentration-Curl-(female)_U.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:32.054831+00', '1. Adjust the cable machine to the correct height and attachment for Cable Seated One Arm Concentration Curl. 2. Sit with your back supported, core engaged, feet flat on the floor. 3. Keep your elbows in a fixed position throughout the movement. 4. Curl the weight up by contracting your biceps, squeezing at the top. 5. Lower with control, resisting the weight on the way down. 6. Complete all reps on one side, then switch to the other side. 7. Complete all reps with control before resting.', 'Curl', 'Pull', NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, 'Seated', NULL, NULL, NULL, 12, 20, NULL, 4, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 87, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'concentration_curl', 'Seated Single Arm Concentration Curl', 'tricep_pushdown, tricep_extension, bicep_curl, hammer_curl', FALSE, 'cable', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 85, 88, 30, 92),
('8333141e-71a7-4411-97bf-bfddf9e8a53e', 'Assisted Inverse Leg Curl (Cable)', 'Legs', 'Cables', '{"Hamstrings"}'::text[], '{"Glutes"}'::text[], 'Strengthen the back of your thighs with this curling exercise. You''ll also feel your calves working to support the movement. Cables provide constant tension throughout the full range of motion. Strong legs are the foundation for athletic performance and functional fitness.', '71051201', '71051201-Cable-Assisted-Inverse-Leg-Curl-(female)_Thighs_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:31.723232+00', '1. Adjust the cable machine to the correct height and attachment for Cable Assisted Inverse Leg Curl. 2. Curl your heels toward your glutes by bending at the knees. 3. Squeeze your hamstrings at peak contraction. 4. Extend legs back out with control. 5. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 7, 8, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 90, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'leg_curl', 'Assisted Inverse Leg Curl', 'romanian_deadlift, hip_thrust', FALSE, 'cable', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 85, 88, 30, 92),
('8337d269-cf5b-441f-98fa-41ed9d6aeabf', 'Incline Shrug (Dumbbell)', 'Back', 'Dumbbells', '{"Traps"}'::text[], '{"Upper Back"}'::text[], 'The Dumbbell Incline Shrug is a shrugging exercise that develops back strength and muscle. Using an incline changes the angle of resistance for varied muscle recruitment. Using dumbbells requires more stabilization than barbell variations. A strong back improves posture, prevents injury, and balances pressing movements.', '3291201', '03291201-Dumbbell-Incline-Shrug_Back.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:26.271124+00', '1. Select a pair of dumbbells at an appropriate weight for Dumbbell Incline Shrug. 2. Shrug your shoulders straight up toward your ears. 3. Hold briefly at the top, then lower with control. 4. Complete all reps with control before resting. Keep the movement smooth and controlled.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 85, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'shrug', 'Incline Shrug', 'deadlift, bent_over_row, face_pull', TRUE, 'dumbbell', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 92, 90, 92, 90),
('833d939c-975e-4a09-86f4-088262e2aa62', 'Burpee Squat', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'A challenging plyometric exercise, the Burpee Squat builds reactive power and improves conditioning. The chest, quads assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. A versatile bodyweight movement perfect for home or gym training. Plyometric training builds explosive power that transfers to sports and daily activities.', '45481201', '45481201-Burpee-Squat_Plyometrics.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:24.577164+00', '1. Push your hips back and bend your knees to lower your body. 2. Keep your chest up and knees tracking over your toes. 3. Drive through your heels to stand back up, squeezing your glutes at the top. 4. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout. Control the movement—avoid using momentum.', 'Squat', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 5, 4, NULL, 8, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 7, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Plyometrics', 85, 9, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'burpee', 'Burpee Squat', 'leg_press, leg_extension, leg_curl, lunge, front_squat, hack_squat', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('836bd182-a91d-430b-91d9-0b3af4a22178', 'Standing Double Crunch', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'This dynamic crunching movement gets your heart rate up while developing explosive strength. You''ll also feel your hip flexors working to support the movement. Performing this standing challenges your balance and core engagement. No equipment needed—your body provides all the resistance. Develops fast-twitch muscle fibers for quicker, more powerful movements.', '91541201', '91541201-Standing-Double-Crunch-(female)_Plyometrics_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:38.570929+00', '1. Stand tall with your feet firmly planted. 2. Curl your shoulders off the floor by contracting your abs. 3. Don''t pull on your neck—focus on the abdominal contraction. 4. Lower with control, maintaining some tension. 5. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout. Maintain a neutral spine throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, 'Standing', NULL, NULL, NULL, 12, 20, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 72, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'crunch', 'Standing Double Crunch', 'leg_raise, plank, russian_twist, v_up', TRUE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('8371d644-1c65-4f1e-ab30-ef986e825f84', 'Standing Crossover (Cable)', 'Full Body', 'Cables', '{"Full Body"}'::text[], '{"Shoulders","Core"}'::text[], 'The Cable Standing Crossover is an explosive exercise that combines cardiovascular training with dynamic movement movements. The shoulders, core assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. Performing this standing challenges your balance and core engagement. The cable setup allows you to adjust the angle of resistance. Great for improving athletic performance, burning calories, and building conditioning.', '81411201', '81411201-Cable-Standing-Crossover-(male)_Chest_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:29.483269+00', '1. Adjust the cable machine to the correct height and attachment for Cable Standing Crossover. 2. Begin in a standing position with good posture. 3. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 8, NULL, 5, 'Standing', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 62, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'chest_fly', 'Standing Crossover', 'bench_press, incline_press, push_up', FALSE, 'cable', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 85, 88, 30, 92),
('8373df9c-aa62-45f3-bb14-2ac6e10aeb4e', 'Spin Hook Kick', 'Full Body', 'Bodyweight', '{"Shoulders"}'::text[], '{"Biceps","Triceps","Core"}'::text[], 'A challenging plyometric exercise, the Spin Hook Kick builds reactive power and improves conditioning. Secondary activation of your shoulders, core provides additional muscle engagement. This bodyweight exercise requires no equipment and can be done anywhere. Great for improving athletic performance, burning calories, and building conditioning.', '23061201', '23061201-Spin-Hook-Kick_Plyometrics_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:29.242428+00', '1. Set up in the starting position for Spin Hook Kick. 2. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your full body. 3. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 4. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'cycling', 'Spin Hook Kick', 'core_exercise, shoulder_exercise, burpee', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65);
INSERT INTO _exercise_staging (id, name, category, equipment, primary_muscles, secondary_muscles, description, video_code, video_filename, gender, is_custom, created_at, steps_to_perform, movement_pattern, force_type, movement_type, laterality, plane_of_motion, difficulty_level, complexity_score, strength_rating, hypertrophy_rating, power_rating, endurance_rating, body_position, bench_angle, grip_type, grip_width, optimal_rep_range_min, optimal_rep_range_max, placement_in_workout, fatigability, popularity_score, home_gym_friendly, instructions, workout_type, practicality_score, fat_loss_rating, general_fitness_rating, is_compound, supersetable, exercise_family, base_exercise_name, complementary_families, is_equipment_primary, equipment_category, duration_based, recommended_sets, rest_seconds, muscles_worked_count, priority_build_muscle, priority_get_lean, priority_home, priority_gym) VALUES
('837b8c4c-0e7d-444d-a358-65212505f82a', 'Offset Leg Push Up', 'Chest', 'Bodyweight', '{"Chest"}'::text[], '{"Triceps","Front Delts"}'::text[], 'The Offset Leg Push Up is a pushing exercise that targets your chest muscles. The triceps, front delts assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. This bodyweight exercise requires no equipment and can be done anywhere. Chest strength improves pushing power for sports, daily tasks, and other lifts.', '85031201', '85031201-Offset-Leg-Push-up-(male)_Chest-FIX_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:27.805708+00', '1. Keep your body in a straight line from head to heels throughout. 2. Lower your chest toward the floor by bending your elbows. 3. Push through your palms to return to the starting position. 4. Complete all reps with control before resting. Don''t rush—quality over quantity.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 70, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'push_up', 'Offset Leg Push Up', 'bench_press, chest_fly, dip', TRUE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('837f322d-d814-415e-82d3-938f2ba088a1', 'Arms Full Circle Squat', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'Elevate your training with this squatting exercise that develops speed, power, and coordination. You''ll also feel your glutes, hamstrings working to support the movement. No equipment needed—your body provides all the resistance. Plyometric training builds explosive power that transfers to sports and daily activities.', '69291201', '69291201-Arms-Full-Circle-Squat-(female)_Plyometrics_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:30.54809+00', '1. Push your hips back and bend your knees to lower your body. 2. Keep your chest up and knees tracking over your toes. 3. Drive through your heels to stand back up, squeezing your glutes at the top. 4. Complete all reps with control before resting. Control the movement—avoid using momentum. Beneficial for overall plyometrics development.', 'Squat', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 85, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'squat', 'Arms Full Circle Squat', 'leg_press, front_squat, goblet_squat, lunge, leg_extension', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('838c6ac5-270b-4fbd-a16e-e85a89169b02', 'Ceiling Look Stretch', 'Full Body', 'Bodyweight', '{"Full Body"}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'Use this stretch to open up your full body area and enhance overall flexibility. Flexibility work like this enhances performance and prevents stiffness. Can be modified for beginners or progressed for advanced athletes.', '42801201', '42801201-Ceiling-Look-Stretch-(male)_Thighs.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:23.689343+00', '1. Move into the stretch position for Ceiling Look Stretch. 2. Ease into the stretch until you feel gentle tension (not pain). 3. Hold for 20-30 seconds, breathing deeply and relaxing into the stretch. Maintain a neutral spine throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 1, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Stretch', 40, 2, 6, FALSE, TRUE, 'stretch_general', 'Ceiling Look Stretch', 'stretch_hip, stretch_back, stretch_shoulder', FALSE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 1, 30, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('83a283a0-a10a-4b60-b292-6a25eaa9c2a3', 'Standing Butt Kick Side And Front Push', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], '{"Calves"}'::text[], 'This dynamic pushing movement gets your heart rate up while developing explosive strength. The hamstrings assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. The standing position engages your core for stability. No equipment needed—your body provides all the resistance. Great for improving athletic performance, burning calories, and building conditioning.', '93701201', '93701201-Standing-Butt-Kick-Side-and-Front-Push-(female)_Pl.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:38.425788+00', '1. Stand tall with your feet firmly planted. 2. Set up in the starting position for Standing Butt Kick Side And Front Push. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your full body. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 5. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, 'Standing', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 52, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'glute_kickback', 'Standing Butt Kick Side And Front Push', 'high_knees, jumping_jack, running', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('83a78584-8452-4af1-aa18-23e72fa7837d', 'Pullover (Machine) - Alternating', 'Chest', 'Lever Machine', '{"Chest"}'::text[], '{"Lats","Triceps"}'::text[], 'The Lever Alternating Pullover (plate Loaded) is a pulling exercise that develops back strength and muscle. Secondary activation of your lats, triceps provides additional muscle engagement. The fixed path allows you to focus purely on muscular effort. Back development is crucial for pulling strength and overall upper body function.', '93861201', '93861201-Lever-Alternating-Pullover-(plate-loaded)_Back_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:23.79417+00', '1. Adjust the machine settings (seat height, weight, pads) to fit your body for Lever Alternating Pullover. 2. With arms slightly bent, lower the weight behind your head in an arc. 3. Pull the weight back over your chest, squeezing your lats and chest. 4. Alternate between sides/arms/legs with each repetition. 5. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 58, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'pullover', 'Lever Pullover - Alternating', 'bicep_curl, face_pull, lat_pulldown', FALSE, 'machine', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 80, 75, 20, 88),
('83b0a6a3-874a-4d13-a575-1053a0e20147', 'Hip Thrust Bench Or Rack (Barbell)', 'Legs', 'Barbell', '{"Glutes"}'::text[], '{"Hamstrings","Core"}'::text[], 'This thrusting exercise isolates your glutes for improved hip strength and power. The hamstrings assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. Barbells enable bilateral loading for building raw strength. Leg training boosts metabolism and builds functional, real-world strength.', '99111201', '99111201-Barbell-Hip-Thrust-inside-Rack-(female)_Hips_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:31.013316+00', '1. Load a barbell and set it on a bench rack at the appropriate height. 2. Drive through your heels to lift your hips toward the ceiling. 3. Squeeze your glutes hard at the top of the movement. 4. Lower your hips back down with control. 5. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 7, 8, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 74, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'hip_thrust', 'Hip Thrust', 'glute_bridge, romanian_deadlift, leg_curl', TRUE, 'barbell', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 95, 80, 65, 95),
('83ba096a-f982-442b-9fde-51614c718221', 'Standing Bicep Curl - Single Arm (Dumbbell)', 'Arms', 'Dumbbells', '{"Biceps"}'::text[], '{"Forearms"}'::text[], 'The Dumbbell Standing Single Arm Biceps Curl is a curling exercise that isolates your biceps. Your forearms work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. Performing this standing challenges your balance and core engagement. The dumbbell variation provides freedom of movement and greater range of motion. Arm strength supports grip, pulling, and pushing in compound movements.', '67571201', '67571201-Dumbbell-Standing-Single-Arm-Biceps-Curl-(female)_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:33.168801+00', '1. Select an appropriate weight dumbbell and hold it in one hand. 2. Stand with feet about shoulder-width apart. 3. Keep your elbows in a fixed position throughout the movement. 4. Curl the weight up by contracting your biceps, squeezing at the top. 5. Lower with control, resisting the weight on the way down. 6. Complete all reps on one side, then switch to the other side. 7. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', 'Curl', 'Pull', NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, 'Standing', NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 89, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'bicep_curl', 'Standing Single Arm Biceps Curl', 'hammer_curl, preacher_curl, cable_curl', TRUE, 'dumbbell', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 92, 90, 92, 90),
('83c672df-4044-4261-9943-915d0c638d28', 'Supported Squat (Dumbbell)', 'Legs', 'Dumbbells', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'Target the front of your thighs with this squatting exercise for quad development. You''ll also feel your glutes, hamstrings working to support the movement. Using dumbbells requires more stabilization than barbell variations. Leg training boosts metabolism and builds functional, real-world strength.', '28031201', '28031201-Dumbbell-Supported-Squat-(female)_Thighs_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:33.298565+00', '1. Select a pair of dumbbells at an appropriate weight for Dumbbell Supported Squat. 2. Push your hips back and bend your knees to lower your body. 3. Keep your chest up and knees tracking over your toes. 4. Drive through your heels to stand back up, squeezing your glutes at the top. 5. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', 'Squat', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 10, 10, NULL, 4, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 5, 8, NULL, 9, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 97, 7, 9, TRUE, FALSE, 'squat', 'Supported Squat', 'leg_press, front_squat, goblet_squat, lunge, leg_extension', FALSE, 'dumbbell', FALSE, 4, 120, 5, 92, 90, 92, 90),
('83ca1d52-3ba5-4e3d-b952-876b7cd28219', 'Single Lean Back Quadriceps Stretch', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'Use this stretch to open up your quads area and enhance overall flexibility. Your hip flexors work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. Include this in your routine for better mobility and reduced muscle tension.', '84671201', '84671201-Single-Lean-Back-Quadriceps-Stretch-(female)_Stret.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:37.429219+00', '1. Move into the stretch position for Single Lean Back Quadriceps Stretch. 2. Ease into the stretch until you feel gentle tension (not pain). 3. Hold for 20-30 seconds, breathing deeply and relaxing into the stretch. 4. Switch sides and repeat for equal time.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 1, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Stretch', 40, 2, 6, FALSE, TRUE, 'stretch_general', 'Single Lean Back Quadriceps Stretch', 'stretch_hip, stretch_hamstring', FALSE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 1, 30, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('83ce2b52-a1d4-467e-9045-0c07e0f2bdc4', 'Bicycle Crunch', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'Strengthen your midsection with this crunching movement that works your abs. You''ll also feel your abs working to support the movement. This bodyweight exercise requires no equipment and can be done anywhere. A strong core improves posture, protects your spine, and enhances all other lifts.', '62121201', '62121201-Bicycle-Crunch-(female)_Waist_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:31.347577+00', '1. Bring one knee toward chest while extending the other leg. 2. Rotate to bring opposite elbow toward the bent knee. 3. Alternate sides in a pedaling motion. 4. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 12, 20, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 70, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'cycling', 'Bicycle Crunch', 'crunch, russian_twist, leg_raise', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('83cfc9a6-cbb4-460c-a7ae-519bcf823a96', 'Single Arm Clean (Kettlebell)', 'Full Body', 'Kettlebell', '{"Full Body"}'::text[], '{"Quads","Glutes","Traps"}'::text[], 'This full-body movement exercise challenges multiple muscle groups simultaneously. You''ll also feel your quads, glutes, traps working to support the movement. The kettlebell grip position adds a unique training stimulus. Compound movements like this develop coordination, power, and overall fitness.', '45431201', '45431201-Kettlebell-One-Arm-Clean_Weightlifting_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:28.851102+00', '1. Select an appropriately weighted kettlebell for Kettlebell One Arm Clean. 2. Explosively pull the weight upward from the starting position. 3. Pull yourself under the weight and catch it at shoulder level. 4. Stand to complete the lift, then lower with control. 5. Complete all reps on one side, then switch to the other side. 6. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 5, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 53, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'clean', 'Single Arm Clean', 'power_clean, deadlift, front_squat', FALSE, 'kettlebell', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 75, 88, 88, 78),
('83da06ee-fe21-46e9-a099-69bc89d24931', 'Lateral Hops', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Calves"}'::text[], 'The Lateral Hops is an explosive exercise that combines cardiovascular training with dynamic movement movements. No equipment needed—your body provides all the resistance. Develops fast-twitch muscle fibers for quicker, more powerful movements.', '47121201', '47121201-Lateral-Hops_Plyometrics_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:22.417605+00', '1. Set up in the starting position for Lateral Hops. 2. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your full body. 3. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 4. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 4, NULL, 8, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 7, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Plyometrics', 50, 9, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'hop', 'Lateral Hops', 'lat_pulldown, bent_over_row, pull_up', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('83da135f-f0da-499a-9413-bfd94e4d7913', 'Seated Reverse Fly (Machine)', 'Shoulders', 'Fly Machine', '{"Rear Delts"}'::text[], '{"Upper Back","Traps"}'::text[], 'Build stronger shoulders with this flying movement focusing on your rear delts. The upper back assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. Being seated provides stability, allowing you to focus on the working muscles. Machine exercises are great for isolating muscles and training to failure safely. Strong shoulders improve overhead strength and support nearly all upper body movements.', '28221201', '28221201-Lever-Seated-Reverse-Fly-(female)_Shoulders-FIX2_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:34.855778+00', '1. Adjust the machine settings (seat height, weight, pads) to fit your body for Lever Seated Reverse Fly. 2. Sit with your back supported, core engaged, feet flat on the floor. 3. With a slight bend in your elbows, move the weight in a wide arc. 4. Squeeze your chest muscles at the center/top of the movement. 5. Return with control, feeling the stretch at the bottom. 6. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions. Don''t rush—quality over quantity.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, 'Seated', NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 80, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'rear_delt', 'Lever Seated Reverse Fly', 'bench_press, incline_bench_press, push_up', FALSE, 'machine', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 80, 75, 20, 88),
('83ddd59f-49d3-4615-9bbb-bb1abda00434', 'Seated Over Head Straight Arm Stretch', 'Full Body', 'Bodyweight', '{"Full Body"}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'The Seated Over Head Straight Arm Stretch is a flexibility exercise that targets your full body, helping to release tension and improve range of motion. The seated position helps isolate the target muscles by removing momentum. Flexibility work like this enhances performance and prevents stiffness.', '83691201', '83691201-Seated-Over-Head-Straight-Arm-Stretch-(female)_Che.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:36.717157+00', '1. Sit with your back supported, core engaged, feet flat on the floor. 2. Move into the stretch position for Seated Over Head Straight Arm Stretch. 3. Ease into the stretch until you feel gentle tension (not pain). 4. Hold for 20-30 seconds, breathing deeply and relaxing into the stretch.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 3, 'Seated', NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 1, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Stretch', 42, 2, 6, FALSE, TRUE, 'stretch_general', 'Seated Over Head Straight Arm Stretch', 'stretch_hip, stretch_back, stretch_shoulder', FALSE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 1, 30, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('83e55eaa-934b-4f9c-9666-186b9a3ad5c0', 'Assisted Chest Dip Kneeling (Dip Bars)', 'Chest', 'Dip Bars', '{"Lower Chest"}'::text[], '{"Triceps","Front Delts"}'::text[], 'Target your chest with the Assisted Chest Dip (kneeling), an effective dipping movement for upper body strength. The triceps, front delts assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. Kneeling helps eliminate lower body momentum from the movement. No equipment needed—your body provides all the resistance. A well-developed chest contributes to upper body strength and aesthetics.', '91201', '00091201-Assisted-Chest-Dip-(kneeling)_Chest.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:26.39056+00', '1. Kneel on the floor (use a pad for comfort if needed). 2. Lower your body by bending your elbows to about 90 degrees. 3. Push back up until your arms are fully extended. 4. Complete all reps with control before resting. Start with lighter weight to perfect your form.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 70, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'dip', 'Assisted Chest Dip', 'bench_press, tricep_pushdown, push_up', TRUE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('83e89f18-5d8c-4b61-b978-061898970870', 'Frog Hops', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Calves"}'::text[], 'The Frog Hops is an explosive exercise that combines cardiovascular training with dynamic movement movements. This bodyweight exercise requires no equipment and can be done anywhere. Plyometric training builds explosive power that transfers to sports and daily activities.', '30881201', '30881201-Frog-Hops-(male)_Plyometrics_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:24.203368+00', '1. Set up in the starting position for Frog Hops. 2. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your full body. 3. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 4. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 4, NULL, 8, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 7, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Plyometrics', 50, 9, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'hop', 'Frog Hops', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('83fbb081-7b0e-4ad1-892e-e512dada2417', 'Lying Straight Arm Press On Floor (Dumbbell)', 'Chest', 'Dumbbells', '{"Chest"}'::text[], '{"Triceps"}'::text[], 'Target your chest with the Dumbbell Lying Straight Arm Press On Floor, an effective pressing movement for upper body strength. You''ll also feel your triceps working to support the movement. The lying position provides back support and helps isolate the target muscles. Dumbbells allow each arm to work independently, helping correct imbalances. A well-developed chest contributes to upper body strength and aesthetics.', '92131201', '92131201-Dumbbell-Lying-Straight-Arm-Press-on-Floor-(female.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:32.914483+00', '1. Select a pair of dumbbells at an appropriate weight for Dumbbell Lying Straight Arm Press On Floor. 2. Position yourself on the floor for Dumbbell Lying Straight Arm Press On Floor. 3. Lie down in the appropriate position for Dumbbell Lying Straight Arm Press On Floor. 4. Lower the weight toward your chest with control. 5. Press the weight up until your arms are extended (don''t lock elbows). 6. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 8, NULL, 5, 'Lying', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 82, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'arm_exercise', 'Lying Straight Arm Press On Floor', 'bicep_curl, tricep_extension, hammer_curl', TRUE, 'dumbbell', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 92, 90, 92, 90),
('83fe6be5-70b6-40f4-a55b-e05a6a807919', 'Weighted Hang Chin Up (Pull-Up Bar)', 'Back', 'Pull-Up Bar', '{"Lats"}'::text[], '{"Biceps","Upper Back"}'::text[], 'This movement exercise emphasizes your lats for improved back development. Your biceps work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. No equipment needed—your body provides all the resistance. A strong back improves posture, prevents injury, and balances pressing movements. Focus on controlled form throughout each repetition.', '41811201', '41811201-Weighted-Hang-Chin-Up_Back_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:28.397686+00', '1. Pull yourself up, focusing on bicep and lat engagement. 2. Raise until chin is over the bar, lower with full control. 3. Complete all reps with control before resting. Keep the movement smooth and controlled.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 4, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 70, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'pull_up', 'Weighted Hang Chin Up', 'lat_pulldown, bent_over_row, bicep_curl', TRUE, 'pull_up_bar', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('8401b279-eded-422c-8fb7-f741177362c2', 'Landmine Standing Side Bend (Landmine)', 'Core', 'Landmine Attachment, Barbell', '{"Obliques"}'::text[], '{"Abs"}'::text[], 'Strengthen your midsection with this movement movement that works your abs. The abs assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. Performing this standing challenges your balance and core engagement. Core strength is foundational for athletic performance and injury prevention.', '80461201', '80461201-Landmine-Standing-Side-Bend-(female)_Waist_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:34.603963+00', '1. Stand with feet about shoulder-width apart. 2. Set up in the starting position for Landmine Standing Side Bend. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your abs. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 5. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions. Keep your shoulders relaxed and away from your ears.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 7, 8, NULL, 5, 'Standing', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 52, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'side_bend', 'Landmine Standing Side Bend', 'russian_twist, woodchop, oblique_crunch', FALSE, 'barbell', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 95, 80, 65, 95),
('840e04bd-c271-4871-9b73-785e37e05e01', 'Triceps Press (Head Below Bench)', 'Arms', 'Bodyweight', '{"Triceps"}'::text[], '{"Chest","Shoulders"}'::text[], 'This pressing movement isolates your triceps for improved arm development. Arm strength supports grip, pulling, and pushing in compound movements.', '70871201', '70871201-Triceps-Press-(Head-Below-Bench)-(female)_Upper-Ar.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:39.79101+00', '1. Lower the weight toward your chest with control. 2. Press the weight up until your arms are extended (don''t lock elbows). 3. Complete all reps with control before resting. Exhale during the exertion phase of the movement.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 70, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'arm_exercise', 'Triceps Press', 'bench_press, chest_fly, push_up', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('841705c7-4522-4f45-a55f-1ee874c15cfe', 'Seated Side Leg Press On Chair (Machine)', 'Legs', 'Leg Press Machine', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'The Seated Side Leg Press On Chair is a pressing exercise that primarily loads your quadriceps. Your glutes work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. Being seated provides stability, allowing you to focus on the working muscles. Strong legs are the foundation for athletic performance and functional fitness.', '105051201', '105051201-Seated-Side-Leg-Press-on-Chair-(male)_Thighs_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:23.056255+00', '1. Position yourself with a sturdy chair for support or as part of the movement. 2. Sit with your back supported, core engaged, feet flat on the floor. 3. Position your feet on the platform and release the safety. 4. Lower the weight by bending your knees, then press back up powerfully. 5. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 10, 10, NULL, 4, 'Seated', NULL, NULL, NULL, 5, 8, NULL, 8, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 67, 7, 9, TRUE, FALSE, 'leg_press', 'Seated Side Leg Press On Chair', 'squat, hack_squat, lunge', TRUE, 'machine', FALSE, 4, 120, 4, 80, 75, 20, 88),
('8419dc0a-a79a-4331-b8c0-8110d0407acf', 'Prone I Stretch', 'Full Body', 'Bodyweight', '{"Full Body"}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'Use this stretch to open up your full body area and enhance overall flexibility. The lying position provides back support and helps isolate the target muscles. Include this in your routine for better mobility and reduced muscle tension. Keep your core engaged throughout the exercise.', '85341201', '85341201-Prone-I-Stretch-(male)_Stretching_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:25.233728+00', '1. Lie face down (prone position) for Prone I Stretch. 2. Move into the stretch position for Prone I Stretch. 3. Ease into the stretch until you feel gentle tension (not pain). 4. Hold for 20-30 seconds, breathing deeply and relaxing into the stretch.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 1, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Stretch', 40, 2, 6, FALSE, TRUE, 'stretch_general', 'Prone I Stretch', 'stretch_hip, stretch_back, stretch_shoulder', FALSE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 1, 30, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('841cfc22-1fee-4870-bfa0-0513b11d287d', 'Standing Balance Quadriceps Stretch', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'Use this stretch to open up your quads area and enhance overall flexibility. Secondary activation of your hip flexors provides additional muscle engagement. The standing position engages your core for stability. Flexibility work like this enhances performance and prevents stiffness.', '35041201', '35041201-Standing-Balance-Quadriceps-Stretch_Stretching_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:20.982555+00', '1. Stand tall with your feet firmly planted. 2. Move into the stretch position for Standing Balance Quadriceps Stretch. 3. Ease into the stretch until you feel gentle tension (not pain). 4. Hold for 20-30 seconds, breathing deeply and relaxing into the stretch.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 3, 'Standing', NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 1, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Stretch', 42, 2, 6, FALSE, TRUE, 'balance', 'Standing Balance Quadriceps Stretch', 'stretch_hip, stretch_hamstring', FALSE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 1, 30, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('84241262-2a8b-4d03-abc9-f43918bfe242', 'Hip Raise (Bent Knee)', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'Build a stronger core with the Hip Raise (bent Knee), focusing on your abs. A versatile bodyweight movement perfect for home or gym training. Core strength is foundational for athletic performance and injury prevention.', '71151201', '71151201-Hip-Raise-(bent-knee)-(VERSION-2)-(female)_Waist_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:34.073704+00', '1. Raise the weight in the prescribed direction for Hip Raise. 2. Lower with control, maintaining tension throughout. 3. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout. Keep your shoulders relaxed and away from your ears.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 70, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'glute_exercise', 'Hip Raise', 'hip_thrust, lunge, squat', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('8425ed13-2ddc-4cd1-be0d-4bad8add221e', 'Stationary Bike Run (Stationary Bike)', 'Full Body', 'Stationary Bike', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'Build your aerobic capacity with this steady-state cardio movement. Regular cardio training builds the aerobic base for better overall fitness. Keep your core engaged throughout the exercise.', '22641201', '22641201-Stationary-Bike-Run-(version-3)-(female)_Cardio.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:39.21093+00', '1. Set up in the starting position for Stationary Bike Run. 2. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your cardio. 3. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 4. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 2, 2, NULL, 10, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 3, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Cardio', 50, 9, 8, FALSE, TRUE, 'cycling', 'Stationary Bike Run', 'cycling, rowing_cardio, jump_rope', FALSE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 1, 60, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('842d1d7e-05fb-4622-a100-461e73eb7f16', 'Seated Hip Adduction (Machine)', 'Legs', 'Hip Adduction Machine', '{"Inner Thighs"}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'Build leg strength with this movement movement focusing on your adductors. Being seated provides stability, allowing you to focus on the working muscles. The fixed path allows you to focus purely on muscular effort. Strong legs are the foundation for athletic performance and functional fitness.', '5981201', '05981201-Lever-Seated-Hip-Adduction_Thighs-FIX_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:23.987963+00', '1. Adjust the machine settings (seat height, weight, pads) to fit your body for Lever Seated Hip Adduction. 2. Sit with your back supported, core engaged, feet flat on the floor. 3. Complete all reps with control before resting. Keep tension on the target muscles throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, 'Seated', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 60, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'hip_adduction', 'Lever Seated Hip Adduction', 'hip_abduction, squat, lunge', TRUE, 'machine', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 80, 75, 20, 88),
('843260e9-48c7-4563-8606-8ccb0da8434b', 'Kneeling Leg Circle', 'Shoulders', 'Bodyweight', '{"Shoulders"}'::text[], '{"Traps"}'::text[], 'Build leg strength with this movement movement focusing on your delts. Kneeling helps eliminate lower body momentum from the movement. No equipment needed—your body provides all the resistance. Strong legs are the foundation for athletic performance and functional fitness.', '58691201', '58691201-Kneeling-Leg-Circle-(female)_Hips_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:34.487002+00', '1. Kneel on the floor (use a pad for comfort if needed). 2. Set up in the starting position for Kneeling Leg Circle. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your delts. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 5. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'leg_exercise', 'Kneeling Leg Circle', 'squat, leg_extension, lunge', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('843360c1-3833-4db2-89ff-463011d0b880', 'Elbow Touch To Outer Throw', 'Back', 'Bodyweight', '{"Upper Back"}'::text[], '{"Lats","Biceps","Rear Delts"}'::text[], 'Target your chest with the Elbow Touch To Outer Throw, an effective rowing movement for upper body strength. The biceps, rear delts assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. No equipment needed—your body provides all the resistance. A well-developed chest contributes to upper body strength and aesthetics.', '87411201', '87411201-Elbow-Touch-to-Outer-Throw-(male)_Chest_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:28.968567+00', '1. Pull the weight toward your torso, leading with your elbow(s). 2. Squeeze your shoulder blades together at the peak contraction. 3. Extend back out with control, feeling the stretch in your back. 4. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout. Exhale during the exertion phase of the movement. A solid choice for chest day.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 70, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'general_exercise', 'Elbow Touch To Outer Throw', 'lat_pulldown, bent_over_row, pull_up', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('843ec2ca-f9b0-46f4-b5b7-e88bfcaf828d', 'Bent Over Row - Reverse Grip (Smith Machine)', 'Back', 'Smith Machine', '{Latissimus Dorsi}'::text[], '{"Lats","Biceps","Rear Delts"}'::text[], 'Target your rhomboids and mid-traps with this rowing movement. Secondary activation of your biceps, lats provides additional muscle engagement. The bent over position requires core engagement to maintain a neutral spine. The fixed path allows you to focus purely on muscular effort. A strong back improves posture, prevents injury, and balances pressing movements.', '13611201', '13611201-Smith-Reverse-Grip-Bent-Over-Row_Back_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:24.831811+00', '1. Set the Smith machine bar to the appropriate starting height for Smith Reverse Grip Bent Over Row. 2. Hinge at your hips, pushing them back while keeping your back flat. 3. Use a reverse grip (opposite of the standard grip for this exercise). 4. Pull the weight toward your torso, leading with your elbow(s). 5. Squeeze your shoulder blades together at the peak contraction. 6. Extend back out with control, feeling the stretch in your back. 7. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 10, 10, NULL, 4, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 5, 8, NULL, 8, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 78, 7, 9, TRUE, FALSE, 'bent_over_row', 'Smith Bent Over Row - Reverse Grip', 'Bent Over Row - Reverse Grip', FALSE, 'barbell', FALSE, 4, 120, 4, 80, 75, 20, 88),
('8447048e-1090-459f-8e98-583769a73c85', 'Elbow Planche', 'Chest', 'Bodyweight', '{"Chest"}'::text[], '{"Triceps","Front Delts","Core"}'::text[], 'The Elbow Planche is a movement exercise that targets your chest muscles. The triceps, front delts, core assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. No equipment needed—your body provides all the resistance. A well-developed chest contributes to upper body strength and aesthetics.', '106651201', '106651201-Elbow-Planche-(male)_Stretching_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:26.678791+00', '1. Set up in the starting position for Elbow Planche. 2. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your chest. 3. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 4. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 5, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 5, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'planche', 'Elbow Planche', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('844cad9d-09fc-421e-8470-180b69839aaa', 'Incline Shoulders Press (Barbell)', 'Shoulders', 'Barbell, Incline Bench', '{"Shoulders","Front Delts"}'::text[], '{"Side Delts","Triceps"}'::text[], 'Build stronger shoulders with this pressing movement focusing on your delts. The incline angle shifts emphasis toward the upper portion of the target muscles. Barbells enable bilateral loading for building raw strength. Shoulder development enhances both performance and upper body aesthetics.', '68151201', '68151201-Barbell-Incline-Shoulders-Press-(male)_Shoulders_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:27.504261+00', '1. Grip a barbell with hands at the appropriate width for Barbell Incline Shoulders Press. 2. Start with the weight at shoulder level. 3. Press directly overhead until your arms are fully extended. 4. Lower back to shoulder level with control. 5. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 7, 8, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 85, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'shoulder_exercise', 'Incline Shoulders Press', 'bench_press, chest_fly, shoulder_press, decline_bench_press', TRUE, 'barbell', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 95, 80, 65, 95),
('845380bb-97d3-46c7-816a-0cfa5b0e6463', 'Prone Incline Seal Row (Dumbbell)', 'Back', 'Dumbbells, Incline Bench', '{"Upper Back"}'::text[], '{"Lats","Biceps","Rear Delts"}'::text[], 'The Dumbbell Prone Incline Seal Row is a rowing exercise that builds thickness in your upper back. You''ll also feel your biceps, rear delts working to support the movement. Performing this lying down removes momentum for stricter form. Dumbbells allow each arm to work independently, helping correct imbalances. A strong back improves posture, prevents injury, and balances pressing movements.', '106401201', '106401201-Dumbbell-Prone-Incline-Seal-Row_Back-FIX_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:24.941834+00', '1. Select a pair of dumbbells at an appropriate weight for Dumbbell Prone Incline Seal Row. 2. Lie face down (prone position) for Dumbbell Prone Incline Seal Row. 3. Pull the weight toward your torso, leading with your elbow(s). 4. Squeeze your shoulder blades together at the peak contraction. 5. Extend back out with control, feeling the stretch in your back. 6. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 10, 10, NULL, 4, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 5, 8, NULL, 8, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 85, 7, 9, TRUE, FALSE, 'general_exercise', 'Prone Incline Seal Row', 'lat_pulldown, bent_over_row, pull_up', TRUE, 'dumbbell', FALSE, 4, 120, 4, 92, 90, 92, 90),
('845b329a-a48e-43b9-a68f-9dc98357fbd5', 'Glute Bridge Chest Press (Dumbbell)', 'Legs', 'Dumbbells', '{"Glutes"}'::text[], '{"Triceps","Front Delts"}'::text[], 'This pressing exercise focuses on your pectorals for improved chest strength and development. The hamstrings assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. The dumbbell variation provides freedom of movement and greater range of motion. Chest strength improves pushing power for sports, daily tasks, and other lifts.', '79941201', '79941201-Dumbbell-Glute-Bridge-Chest-Press-(male)_Chest_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:24.831811+00', '1. Select a pair of dumbbells at an appropriate weight for Dumbbell Glute Bridge Chest Press. 2. Lower the weight toward your chest with control. 3. Press the weight up until your arms are extended (don''t lock elbows). 4. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 7, 8, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 82, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'glute_bridge', 'Glute Bridge Chest Press', 'hip_thrust, romanian_deadlift', FALSE, 'dumbbell', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 92, 90, 92, 90),
('847dd54c-f201-4cab-98d3-c57979d32e77', 'Seated High Pulley Overhead Triceps Extension (Cable)', 'Arms', 'Cables', '{"Triceps"}'::text[], '{"Shoulders"}'::text[], 'This pulling movement isolates your triceps for improved arm development. The seated position helps isolate the target muscles by removing momentum. Cables provide constant tension throughout the full range of motion. Dedicated arm training builds both strength and muscular definition.', '59161201', '59161201-Cable-Seated-High-Pulley-Overhead-Tricep-Extension_Upper-Arms_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:26.146796+00', '1. Set the cable pulley to the highest position and attach your preferred handle. 2. Sit with your back supported, core engaged, feet flat on the floor. 3. Extend at the elbow until your arm is straight, squeezing the tricep. 4. Lower with control, keeping your upper arm stationary. 5. Complete all reps with control before resting. Start with lighter weight to perfect your form.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, 'Seated', NULL, NULL, NULL, 12, 20, NULL, 4, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 82, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'tricep_extension', 'Seated High Pulley Overhead Triceps Extension', 'tricep_pushdown, close_grip_bench', FALSE, 'cable', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 85, 88, 30, 92),
('848401e2-c446-444d-b73e-f8920b49a431', 'Lunge Back Crossover (TRX)', 'Legs', 'TRX', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'This lunging movement emphasizes your quadriceps for stronger, more powerful legs. Secondary activation of your front delts provides additional muscle engagement. Suspension training adds instability, increasing core activation throughout. Leg training boosts metabolism and builds functional, real-world strength.', '11191201', '11191201-Suspender-Lunge-Back-Crossover-(female)_Thighs_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:39.472701+00', '1. Adjust the TRX/suspension straps to the appropriate length for Suspender Lunge Back Crossover. 2. Step backward, lowering your back knee toward the floor. 3. Push through your front/working leg to return to the starting position. 4. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 60, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'chest_fly', 'Suspender Lunge Back Crossover', 'bench_press, incline_press, push_up', FALSE, 'trx', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 68, 85, 85, 70),
('84917865-a798-4b29-957f-7bc67a7cdff7', 'Stepback Row', 'Back', 'Bodyweight', '{"Upper Back"}'::text[], '{"Lats","Biceps","Rear Delts"}'::text[], 'Elevate your training with this rowing exercise that develops speed, power, and coordination. The quads assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. Plyometric training builds explosive power that transfers to sports and daily activities.', '97721201', '97721201-Stepback-Row-(male)_Plyometrics_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:22.938497+00', '1. Set up a box or step platform at the appropriate height. 2. Pull the weight toward your torso, leading with your elbow(s). 3. Squeeze your shoulder blades together at the peak contraction. 4. Extend back out with control, feeling the stretch in your back. 5. Complete all reps with control before resting. Keep your core engaged for stability.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 70, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'back_exercise', 'Stepback Row', 'lat_pulldown, bent_over_row, pull_up', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('84a539c8-d534-4e13-bd51-6640270c9c37', 'Side Step Up Down Punch Twist (Step Platform)', 'Legs', 'Step Platform', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'Elevate your training with this twisting exercise that develops speed, power, and coordination. The glutes, hamstrings assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. Plyometric training builds explosive power that transfers to sports and daily activities.', '97911201', '97911201-Side-Step-Up-Down-Punch-Twist-(female)_Plyometrics.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:37.303932+00', '1. Set up a box or step platform at the appropriate height. 2. Rotate your torso through the movement pattern for Side Step Up Down Punch Twist. 3. Control the rotation in both directions—avoid using momentum. 4. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 70, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'step_up', 'Side Step Up Down Punch Twist', 'core_exercise, shoulder_exercise, burpee', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('84a803de-f52a-4246-b418-45f742119431', 'Lying Single Arm Full Chest Press (Plate Loaded)', 'Chest', 'Chest Press Machine', '{"Chest"}'::text[], '{"Triceps","Front Delts"}'::text[], 'Build a stronger chest with this pressing movement that develops pressing power. Secondary activation of your triceps, front delts provides additional muscle engagement. Performing this lying down removes momentum for stricter form. The machine guides your movement path for safer, more controlled repetitions. A well-developed chest contributes to upper body strength and aesthetics.', '88071201', '88071201-Lever-Lying-Single-Arm-Full-Chest-Press-(plate-loa.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:29.971345+00', '1. Adjust the machine settings (seat height, weight, pads) to fit your body for Lever Lying Single Arm Full Chest Press (plate Loa. 2. Lie down in the appropriate position for Lever Lying Single Arm Full Chest Press (plate Loa. 3. Lower the weight toward your chest with control. 4. Press the weight up until your arms are extended (don''t lock elbows). 5. Complete all reps on one side, then switch to the other side. 6. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, 'Lying', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 73, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'bench_press', 'Lever Lying Single Arm Full Chest Press (plate Loa', 'incline_press, decline_press, chest_fly, push_up, dip', FALSE, 'plate', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 80, 75, 20, 88),
('84c73a3d-8533-414b-8e62-0f3fdbbf778d', 'Side Lying Kickout', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'The Side Lying Kickout is a kicking exercise that primarily loads your quadriceps. Performing this lying down removes momentum for stricter form. This bodyweight exercise requires no equipment and can be done anywhere. Strong legs are the foundation for athletic performance and functional fitness.', '57991201', '57991201-Side-Lying-Kickout-(female)_Hips_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:37.179953+00', '1. Lie on your side with your body aligned. 2. Set up in the starting position for Side Lying Kickout. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your quads. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 5. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, 'Lying', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'general_exercise', 'Side Lying Kickout', 'hip_flexor, lunge, dynamic_warmup', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('84d1038e-f504-4ad3-9fa4-e7b820753176', 'Shrug On Parallel Bars (Dip Bars)', 'Back', 'Dip Bars', '{"Traps"}'::text[], '{"Upper Back"}'::text[], 'The Shrug (on Parallel Bars) is a shrugging exercise that develops back strength and muscle. A strong back improves posture, prevents injury, and balances pressing movements.', '41761201', '41761201-Shrug-(on-parallel-bars)_Back_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:25.737494+00', '1. Shrug your shoulders straight up toward your ears. 2. Hold briefly at the top, then lower with control. 3. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 70, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'dip', 'Shrug', 'deadlift, bent_over_row, face_pull', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('84daa367-6ecb-4235-bc30-5a6cbbaffff3', 'Clean Grip Reverse Lunge (Kettlebell)', 'Legs', 'Kettlebell', '{"Quads","Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'Target the front of your thighs with this lunging exercise for quad development. Secondary activation of your glutes, hamstrings provides additional muscle engagement. The kettlebell grip position adds a unique training stimulus. Strong legs are the foundation for athletic performance and functional fitness.', '83301201', '83301201-Kettlebell-Clean-Grip-Reverse-Lunge-(male)_Thighs_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:26.507873+00', '1. Select an appropriately weighted kettlebell for Kettlebell Clean Grip Reverse Lunge. 2. Step backward, lowering your back knee toward the floor. 3. Push through your front/working leg to return to the starting position. 4. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 78, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'lunge', 'Clean Grip Reverse Lunge', 'split_squat, step_up, squat', FALSE, 'kettlebell', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 75, 88, 88, 78),
('84db68a8-4977-44c6-a719-1d6b6f0f63f6', 'Seated Chest Stretch (Chair)', 'Chest', 'Chair', '{"Chest"}'::text[], '{"Front Delts"}'::text[], 'Target your chest with this stretching stretch that helps restore range of motion. The shoulders assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. The seated position helps isolate the target muscles by removing momentum. Flexibility work like this enhances performance and prevents stiffness.', '91771201', '91771201-Sitting-Chest-Stretch-on-a-Chair-(female)_Stretchi.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:37.628647+00', '1. Position yourself with a sturdy chair for support or as part of the movement. 2. Sit with your back supported, core engaged, feet flat on the floor. 3. Move into the stretch position for Seated Chest Stretch On A Chair. 4. Ease into the stretch until you feel gentle tension (not pain). 5. Hold for 20-30 seconds, breathing deeply and relaxing into the stretch.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 1, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Stretch', 25, 2, 6, FALSE, TRUE, 'chest_stretch', 'Seated Chest Stretch On A Chair', 'stretch_shoulder, stretch_back', FALSE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 1, 30, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('84e109b0-8958-4cb7-a2f4-ab24760e8cfb', 'Lateral Shuffle Squat Tap', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'Build power and athleticism with this high-intensity squatting exercise that challenges your entire body. Your glutes, hamstrings work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. No equipment needed—your body provides all the resistance. Develops fast-twitch muscle fibers for quicker, more powerful movements. Control the negative portion for maximum muscle engagement.', '56731201', '56731201-Lateral-Shuffle-Squat-Tap-(Male)_Plyometrics_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:26.678791+00', '1. Push your hips back and bend your knees to lower your body. 2. Keep your chest up and knees tracking over your toes. 3. Drive through your heels to stand back up, squeezing your glutes at the top. 4. Complete all reps with control before resting. Focus on squeezing the target muscle at peak contraction.', 'Squat', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 5, 4, NULL, 8, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 7, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Plyometrics', 85, 9, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'shuffle', 'Lateral Shuffle Squat Tap', 'leg_press, leg_extension, leg_curl, lunge, front_squat, hack_squat', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('84e44567-1652-435f-bf37-25b2cee04d67', 'Hands Behind Double Superman Pulse', 'Back', 'Bodyweight', '{"Lower Back"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Upper Back"}'::text[], 'Build leg strength with this movement movement focusing on your lower back. You''ll also feel your glutes working to support the movement. A versatile bodyweight movement perfect for home or gym training. Lower body strength improves everything from walking to heavy compound lifts.', '94531201', '94531201-Hands-Behind-Double-Superman-Pulse-(female)_Hips_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:33.960339+00', '1. At the bottom or top, pulse up and down in small movements before completing the rep. 2. Set up in the starting position for Hands Behind Double Superman Pulse. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your lower back. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 5. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'back_extension', 'Hands Behind Double Superman Pulse', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('84e7f1e4-ea75-4770-a53b-1d65e4186c8f', 'Incline Finger Press', 'Arms', 'Bodyweight', '{"Upper Chest"}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'Build grip strength and forearm size with this pressing exercise. The incline angle shifts emphasis toward the upper portion of the target muscles. Arm strength supports grip, pulling, and pushing in compound movements.', '65811201', '65811201-Incline-Finger-Press-(male)_Forearms_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:22.938497+00', '1. Execute the pressing motion for Incline Finger Press, extending through the target muscles. 2. Set up in the starting position for Incline Finger Press. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your forearms. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 5. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 73, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'general_exercise', 'Incline Finger Press', 'bench_press, chest_fly, shoulder_press, decline_bench_press', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('84f5aae4-89d9-4a07-8b58-82325b18bcf0', 'Seated Jack (Chair)', 'Full Body', 'Chair', '{"Full Body"}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'This dynamic movement movement gets your heart rate up while developing explosive strength. The seated position helps isolate the target muscles by removing momentum. Plyometric training builds explosive power that transfers to sports and daily activities.', '91251201', '91251201-Sitting-Jack-on-a-Chair-(female)_Plyometrics_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:37.756436+00', '1. Position yourself with a sturdy chair for support or as part of the movement. 2. Sit with your back supported, core engaged, feet flat on the floor. 3. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout. Start with lighter weight to perfect your form.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 4, NULL, 8, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 7, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Plyometrics', 35, 9, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'jumping_jack', 'Seated Jack On A Chair', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('84f9056d-89df-4cb2-8f88-2c94a6b16707', 'Front Pulldown (Machine)', 'Back', 'Lat Pulldown Machine', '{"Lats"}'::text[], '{"Biceps","Upper Back"}'::text[], 'This pulling exercise emphasizes your lats for improved back development. You''ll also feel your biceps, upper back working to support the movement. The machine guides your movement path for safer, more controlled repetitions. Back development is crucial for pulling strength and overall upper body function.', '5791201', '05791201-Lever-Front-Pulldown_Back.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:27.67144+00', '1. Adjust the machine settings (seat height, weight, pads) to fit your body for Lever Front Pulldown. 2. Pull the bar/handle down toward your upper chest. 3. Drive your elbows down and back, squeezing your lats. 4. Control the weight back up without letting it yank your arms. 5. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 58, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'lat_pulldown', 'Lever Front Pulldown', 'pull_up, bent_over_row, cable_row, face_pull', FALSE, 'machine', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 80, 75, 20, 88),
('8506c0f5-df67-45b8-97e5-ce193cbc3715', 'Decline Chest Press (Plate Machine)', 'Chest', 'Machine', '{"Chest","Lower Chest"}'::text[], '{"Front Delts","Triceps"}'::text[], 'Build a stronger chest with this pressing movement that develops pressing power. Your triceps, front delts work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. Declining shifts the emphasis to hit the muscles from a different angle. Machine exercises are great for isolating muscles and training to failure safely. A well-developed chest contributes to upper body strength and aesthetics.', '107171201', '107171201-Lever-Decline-Chest-Press-(female)_Chest_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:34.724336+00', '1. Adjust the machine settings (seat height, weight, pads) to fit your body for Lever Decline Chest Press. 2. Lower the weight toward your chest with control. 3. Press the weight up until your arms are extended (don''t lock elbows). 4. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions. Keep the movement smooth and controlled.', 'Decline Press', 'Push', 'Compound', 'Bilateral', NULL, 1, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 81, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'decline_press', 'Lever Decline Chest Press', 'bench_press, incline_bench_press, chest_fly, dip', FALSE, 'machine', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 80, 75, 20, 88),
('85337f61-fcb9-415d-9245-1fe63450e090', 'Lying Raised Glute Abduction Around The World', 'Shoulders', 'Bodyweight', '{"Glutes"}'::text[], '{"Traps"}'::text[], 'Build stronger shoulders with this raising movement focusing on your delts. You''ll also feel your chest working to support the movement. The lying position provides back support and helps isolate the target muscles. This bodyweight exercise requires no equipment and can be done anywhere. Shoulder development enhances both performance and upper body aesthetics.', '94541201', '94541201-Lying-Raised-Glute-Abduction-Around-The-World-(fem.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:35.250398+00', '1. Lie down in the appropriate position for Lying Raised Glute Abduction Around The World. 2. Raise the weight in the prescribed direction for Lying Raised Glute Abduction Around The World. 3. Lower with control, maintaining tension throughout. 4. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, 'Lying', NULL, NULL, NULL, 12, 20, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 35, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'around_world', 'Lying Raised Glute Abduction Around The World', 'hip_thrust, glute_bridge, leg_curl', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('8534b76f-8782-4998-8cd3-082c9e4e7073', 'Low Lunge Twist', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'Use this stretch to open up your quads area and enhance overall flexibility. Secondary activation of your abs provides additional muscle engagement. Flexibility work like this enhances performance and prevents stiffness.', '79061201', '79061201-Low-Lunge-Twist-(female)_Stretching_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:35.010404+00', '1. Step forward into a lunge until both knees are at about 90 degrees. 2. Push through your front/working leg to return to the starting position. 3. Move into the stretch position for Low Lunge Twist. 4. Ease into the stretch until you feel gentle tension (not pain). 5. Hold for 20-30 seconds, breathing deeply and relaxing into the stretch.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 70, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'lunge', 'Low Lunge Twist', 'split_squat, step_up, squat', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('85396ccd-b4a7-426f-8b8b-2473d44fa76b', 'Chest Out Hands Behind (Hold)', 'Chest', 'Bodyweight', '{"Chest"}'::text[], '{"Shoulders"}'::text[], 'Target your chest with this movement stretch that helps restore range of motion. You''ll also feel your shoulders working to support the movement. Include this in your routine for better mobility and reduced muscle tension.', '105791201', '105791201-Chest-Out-Hands-Behind-(Hold)-(male)_Stretching_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:26.808474+00', '1. Move into the stretch position for Chest Out Hands Behind. 2. Ease into the stretch until you feel gentle tension (not pain). 3. Hold for 20-30 seconds, breathing deeply and relaxing into the stretch. 4. Hold the position for the prescribed time, maintaining tension. Keep your core engaged for stability.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'chest_exercise', 'Chest Out Hands Behind', 'bench_press, chest_fly, push_up', FALSE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('85398779-1bdb-4449-8faf-6e14c4d4c536', 'Standing Around The World', 'Shoulders', 'Bodyweight', '{"Shoulders"}'::text[], '{"Traps"}'::text[], 'The Bodyweight Standing Around The World is a movement exercise that targets your delts for shoulder development. The chest assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. The standing position engages your core for stability. This bodyweight exercise requires no equipment and can be done anywhere. Strong shoulders improve overhead strength and support nearly all upper body movements.', '65631201', '65631201-Bodyweight-Standing-Around-the-World-(female)_Shou.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:31.475486+00', '1. Begin in a standing position with good posture. 2. Set up in the starting position for Bodyweight Standing Around The World. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your delts. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 5. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, 'Standing', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 35, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'around_world', 'Standing Around The World', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('8539cb4d-92aa-4cfa-863d-3d7b416cb1d2', 'Four Limbed Staff', 'Full Body', 'Bodyweight', '{"Full Body"}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'The Four Limbed Staff is a flexibility exercise that targets your full body, helping to release tension and improve range of motion. Regular stretching improves flexibility, reduces injury risk, and aids recovery.', '59141201', '59141201-Four-Limbed-Staff-(female)_Stretching_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:33.640031+00', '1. Move into the stretch position for Four Limbed Staff. 2. Ease into the stretch until you feel gentle tension (not pain). 3. Hold for 20-30 seconds, breathing deeply and relaxing into the stretch.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'general_exercise', 'Four Limbed Staff', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('8543ad81-3068-4162-a10b-3fe406d83fdb', 'Side To Side Leg Swing', 'Full Body', 'Bodyweight', '{"Full Body"}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'Designed to lengthen your full body, the Side To Side Leg Swings helps improve mobility and prevent stiffness. Regular stretching improves flexibility, reduces injury risk, and aids recovery.', '46301201', '46301201-Side-to-Side-Leg-Swings-(male)_Hips.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:22.938497+00', '1. Hinge at your hips, letting the weight swing back between your legs. 2. Explosively drive hips forward, propelling the weight forward/up. 3. Let gravity bring it back as you hinge for the next rep. Ensure full range of motion on each rep.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'leg_exercise', 'Side To Side Leg Swing', 'high_knees, butt_kicks, jumping_jack', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('855f13e1-fbc2-4336-823b-f7334a1a8630', 'Standing Bicep Curl (Band) - Alternating', 'Arms', 'Resistance Band', '{"Biceps"}'::text[], '{"Forearms"}'::text[], 'The Band Standing Alternate Biceps Curl is a curling exercise that isolates your biceps. Your forearms work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. Performing this standing challenges your balance and core engagement. The band creates increasing tension as it stretches, challenging the lockout. Arm strength supports grip, pulling, and pushing in compound movements.', '70681201', '70681201-Band-Standing-Alternate-Biceps-Curl-(female)_Upper.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:30.887491+00', '1. Secure the resistance band appropriately for Band Standing Alternate Biceps Curl. 2. Stand with feet about shoulder-width apart. 3. Keep your elbows in a fixed position throughout the movement. 4. Curl the weight up by contracting your biceps, squeezing at the top. 5. Lower with control, resisting the weight on the way down. 6. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', 'Curl', 'Pull', NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, 'Standing', NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 87, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'bicep_curl', 'Standing Biceps Curl - Alternating', 'hammer_curl, preacher_curl, cable_curl', FALSE, 'band', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 60, 85, 90, 50),
('856374cc-01aa-4cd3-b882-d6b1cf317e2e', 'Seated Press Up (Chair)', 'Chest', 'Chair', '{"Chest"}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'Target your chest with the Seated Press Up On A Chair, an effective pressing movement for upper body strength. Being seated provides stability, allowing you to focus on the working muscles. Chest strength improves pushing power for sports, daily tasks, and other lifts.', '92111201', '92111201-Sitting-Press-Up-on-a-Chair-(female)_Chest_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:37.756436+00', '1. Position yourself with a sturdy chair for support or as part of the movement. 2. Sit with your back supported, core engaged, feet flat on the floor. 3. Lower the weight toward your chest with control. 4. Press the weight up until your arms are extended (don''t lock elbows). 5. Complete all reps with control before resting. Maintain a neutral spine throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 55, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'push_up', 'Seated Press Up On A Chair', 'bench_press, chest_fly, dip', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('85709385-6c40-484b-a0ca-8c0a43f7a8b2', 'High Row With Chest Support (Cable)', 'Back', 'Cables', '{"Upper Back"}'::text[], '{"Lats","Biceps","Rear Delts"}'::text[], 'Target your rhomboids and mid-traps with this rowing movement. Secondary activation of your biceps, rear delts provides additional muscle engagement. Cables provide constant tension throughout the full range of motion. Back development is crucial for pulling strength and overall upper body function.', '75971201', '75971201-Cable-High-Row-with-Chest-Support_Back_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:26.507873+00', '1. Set the cable pulley to the highest position and attach your preferred handle. 2. Pull the weight toward your torso, leading with your elbow(s). 3. Squeeze your shoulder blades together at the peak contraction. 4. Extend back out with control, feeling the stretch in your back. 5. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 8, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 80, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'cable_row', 'High Row With Chest Support', 'bench_press, chest_fly, push_up', FALSE, 'cable', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 85, 88, 30, 92),
('857cc5d3-47f9-4a88-898a-970026ac1a46', 'V Up (Dumbbell)', 'Core', 'Dumbbells', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'The Dumbbell V Up is a core movement exercise that primarily targets your abs. The hip flexors assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. The dumbbell variation provides freedom of movement and greater range of motion. A strong core improves posture, protects your spine, and enhances all other lifts.', '34461201', '34461201-Dumbbell-V-up-(female)_Waist_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:33.298565+00', '1. Select a pair of dumbbells at an appropriate weight for Dumbbell V Up. 2. Set up in the starting position for Dumbbell V Up. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your abs. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 5. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 8, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 62, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'v_up', 'V Up', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', TRUE, 'dumbbell', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 92, 90, 92, 90),
('857cf604-78e0-4819-835d-1b7035186abe', 'V Hold (beginner Level)', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'This movement exercise engages your abs for improved core stability and strength. No equipment needed—your body provides all the resistance. Core strength is foundational for athletic performance and injury prevention.', '88591201', '88591201-V-Hold-(beginner-level)-(male)_Waist_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:22.938497+00', '1. Hold the position for the prescribed time, maintaining tension. 2. Set up in the starting position for V Hold. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your abs. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. Focus on the mind-muscle connection.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 45, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'general_exercise', 'V Hold', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('857f1b4b-4008-4a28-a599-c020ecf38337', 'Plank Jack (Dumbbell)', 'Core', 'Dumbbells', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Shoulders","Lower Back"}'::text[], 'Elevate your training with this stabilization exercise that develops speed, power, and coordination. You''ll also feel your shoulders, lower back working to support the movement. The dumbbell variation provides freedom of movement and greater range of motion. Develops fast-twitch muscle fibers for quicker, more powerful movements.', '75451201', '75451201-Dumbbell-Plank-Jack-(female)_Plyometrics_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:33.034396+00', '1. Select a pair of dumbbells at an appropriate weight for Dumbbell Plank Jack. 2. Hold your body in a straight line from head to heels. 3. Don''t let your hips sag or pike up—engage your core and glutes. 4. Breathe steadily while maintaining the position. 5. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 4, NULL, 8, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 7, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Plyometrics', 82, 9, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'plank', 'Plank Jack', 'side_plank, dead_bug, hollow_hold', FALSE, 'dumbbell', FALSE, 3, 60, 4, 92, 90, 92, 90),
('85821f08-6a2d-485e-ba8f-f341cd14b44c', 'Decline Lying Leg Curl (Dumbbell)', 'Legs', 'Dumbbells, Decline Bench', '{"Hamstrings"}'::text[], '{"Glutes"}'::text[], 'This curling movement works your hamstrings for balanced leg development. Your calves work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. Performing this lying down removes momentum for stricter form. The dumbbell variation provides freedom of movement and greater range of motion. Lower body strength improves everything from walking to heavy compound lifts.', '47331201', '47331201-Dumbbell-Decline-Lying-Leg-Curl_Thighs_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:27.937212+00', '1. Select a pair of dumbbells at an appropriate weight for Dumbbell Decline Lying Leg Curl. 2. Lie down in the appropriate position for Dumbbell Decline Lying Leg Curl. 3. Curl your heels toward your glutes by bending at the knees. 4. Squeeze your hamstrings at peak contraction. 5. Extend legs back out with control. 6. Complete all reps with control before resting.', 'Leg Curl', 'Pull', 'Compound', 'Bilateral', NULL, 1, NULL, 7, 8, NULL, 5, 'Lying', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 95, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'leg_curl', 'Decline Lying Leg Curl', 'romanian_deadlift, hip_thrust', TRUE, 'dumbbell', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 92, 90, 92, 90),
('85833836-b497-495e-ab43-324b3657e8f2', 'Stepjack Back Squeeze', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'Build power and athleticism with this high-intensity stepping exercise that challenges your entire body. Secondary activation of your quads provides additional muscle engagement. Great for improving athletic performance, burning calories, and building conditioning.', '62041201', '62041201-Stepjack-Back-Squeeze-(female)_Plyometrics_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:39.21093+00', '1. Set up a box or step platform at the appropriate height. 2. Set up in the starting position for Stepjack Back Squeeze. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your full body. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 5. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 4, NULL, 8, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 7, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Plyometrics', 50, 9, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'back_exercise', 'Stepjack Back Squeeze', 'lat_pulldown, bent_over_row, pull_up', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('858723c5-a496-434c-b522-a82dfa08fe77', 'Bench Dip Knees Bent (Flat Bench)', 'Chest', 'Flat Bench', '{"Lower Chest"}'::text[], '{"Triceps","Front Delts"}'::text[], 'This dipping movement isolates your triceps for improved arm development. You''ll also feel your triceps, front delts working to support the movement. Arm strength supports grip, pulling, and pushing in compound movements.', '23761201', '23761201-Bench-Dip-(knees-bent)-(female)_Upper-arms.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:31.133197+00', '1. Lower your body by bending your elbows to about 90 degrees. 2. Push back up until your arms are fully extended. 3. Complete all reps with control before resting. Keep the movement smooth and controlled.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 70, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'dip', 'Bench Dip', 'bench_press, tricep_pushdown, push_up', TRUE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('858f14d6-4361-4b89-8cc6-312380c59514', 'Single Starfish Crunch', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'Build a stronger core with the Single Starfish Crunch, focusing on your abs. Secondary activation of your hip flexors provides additional muscle engagement. This bodyweight exercise requires no equipment and can be done anywhere. Building core stability helps with everything from heavy deadlifts to daily activities.', '67221201', '67221201-Single-Starfish-Crunch-(female)_Waist_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:37.628647+00', '1. Curl your shoulders off the floor by contracting your abs. 2. Don''t pull on your neck—focus on the abdominal contraction. 3. Lower with control, maintaining some tension. 4. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout. Control the movement—avoid using momentum. An effective movement for your core routine.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 12, 20, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 70, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'crunch', 'Single Starfish Crunch', 'leg_raise, plank, russian_twist, v_up', TRUE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('85a6826e-13eb-4409-8171-201db3bef280', 'Elevated Two Legs Hip Thrust (Step Platform)', 'Legs', 'Step Platform', '{"Glutes"}'::text[], '{"Hamstrings","Core"}'::text[], 'Build stronger glutes with this thrusting movement focused on hip extension. You''ll also feel your hamstrings working to support the movement. No equipment needed—your body provides all the resistance. Strong legs are the foundation for athletic performance and functional fitness.', '74131201', '74131201-Elevated-Two-Legs-Hip-Thrust-(female)_Hips_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:33.505723+00', '1. Drive through your heels to lift your hips toward the ceiling. 2. Squeeze your glutes hard at the top of the movement. 3. Lower your hips back down with control. 4. Complete all reps with control before resting. Don''t rush—quality over quantity. Beneficial for overall legs development.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 70, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'hip_thrust', 'Elevated Two Legs Hip Thrust', 'glute_bridge, romanian_deadlift, leg_curl', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('85b7f54f-882e-40bd-8601-1961e8f4b28e', 'Y Leg Squeeze And Curl', 'Arms', 'Bodyweight', '{"Biceps"}'::text[], '{"Forearms"}'::text[], 'The Y Leg Squeeze And Curl is a lower body curling exercise that targets your biceps. Your forearms work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. No equipment needed—your body provides all the resistance. Leg training boosts metabolism and builds functional, real-world strength.', '63871201', '63871201-Y-Leg-Squeeze-and-Curl-(female)_Hips_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:40.146812+00', '1. Curl your heels toward your glutes by bending at the knees. 2. Squeeze your hamstrings at peak contraction. 3. Extend legs back out with control. 4. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions. Keep the movement smooth and controlled.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 70, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'leg_exercise', 'Y Leg Squeeze And Curl', 'tricep_pushdown, tricep_extension, hammer_curl, preacher_curl', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('85bf4e3c-f4c1-4adb-8ad1-5e0745d770aa', 'Sideways Lifts Vertical Turn (Straight Legs)', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'This movement exercise engages your abs for improved core stability and strength. No equipment needed—your body provides all the resistance. Building core stability helps with everything from heavy deadlifts to daily activities. Perfect for including in both strength and hypertrophy programs.', '7241201', '07241201-Sideways-Lifts-Vertical-Turn-(straight-legs)_Waist.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:37.429219+00', '1. Set up in the starting position for Sideways Lifts Vertical Turn. 2. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your abs. 3. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 4. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'romanian_deadlift', 'Sideways Lifts Vertical Turn', 'deadlift, leg_curl, hip_thrust', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('85d13a4f-070a-44d8-86e2-f22b5c701903', 'Warrior II To Downward Facing Dog Pose', 'Back', 'Bodyweight', '{"Lats"}'::text[], '{"Hamstrings","Shoulders"}'::text[], 'Use this stretch to open up your full body area and enhance overall flexibility. Secondary activation of your hips, shoulders, quads provides additional muscle engagement. Regular stretching improves flexibility, reduces injury risk, and aids recovery.', '79721201', '79721201-Warrior-II-to-Downward-Facing-Dog-Pose-(female)_St.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:39.91585+00', '1. Move into the stretch position for Warrior II To Downward Facing Dog Pose. 2. Ease into the stretch until you feel gentle tension (not pain). 3. Hold for 20-30 seconds, breathing deeply and relaxing into the stretch.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 1, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Stretch', 50, 2, 6, FALSE, TRUE, 'yoga', 'Warrior II To Downward Facing Dog Pose', 'stretch_hip, stretch_back, plank', FALSE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 1, 30, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('85e3c349-1d55-446e-8fd2-e6962f0b6560', 'Single Leg Deadlift (Hack Squat Machine)', 'Legs', 'Machine', '{"Quads","Glutes"}'::text[], '{"Hamstrings","Traps"}'::text[], 'Target the front of your thighs with this squatting exercise for quad development. Your glutes work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. Machine exercises are great for isolating muscles and training to failure safely. Leg training boosts metabolism and builds functional, real-world strength.', '87991201', '87991201-Lever-Single-Leg-Deadlift-on Hack-Squat-Machine-(f.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:34.855778+00', '1. Adjust the machine settings (seat height, weight, pads) to fit your body for Lever Single Leg Deadlift On Hack Squat Machine. 2. Push your hips back and bend your knees to lower your body. 3. Keep your chest up and knees tracking over your toes. 4. Drive through your heels to stand back up, squeezing your glutes at the top. 5. Complete all reps on one side, then switch to the other side. 6. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', 'Squat', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 10, 10, NULL, 4, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, 6, NULL, 10, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 88, 7, 9, TRUE, FALSE, 'hack_squat', 'Lever Single Leg Deadlift On Hack Squat', 'leg_press, squat, leg_extension', TRUE, 'machine', FALSE, 4, 120, 6, 80, 75, 20, 88),
('85e62312-27bc-4c62-b572-8853e0ceecf4', 'Seated Opposite Grab (Chair)', 'Core', 'Chair', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'Build a stronger back with this movement movement targeting your abs. Being seated provides stability, allowing you to focus on the working muscles. A strong back improves posture, prevents injury, and balances pressing movements.', '91071201', '91071201-Sitting-Opposite-Grab-on-a-Chair-(female)_Back_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:37.756436+00', '1. Position yourself with a sturdy chair for support or as part of the movement. 2. Sit with your back supported, core engaged, feet flat on the floor. 3. Complete all reps with control before resting. Maintain a neutral spine throughout. Perfect for targeting your abs.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 35, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'core_exercise', 'Seated Opposite Grab On A Chair', 'plank, crunch, leg_raise', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('85f2ed42-21b3-4df2-8e8a-949311649b53', 'Behind The Back Triceps Dip (Cable)', 'Arms', 'Cables', '{"Triceps"}'::text[], '{"Chest","Shoulders"}'::text[], 'The Cable Behind The Back Triceps Dip targets your triceps through a dipping motion. The triceps, front delts assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. The cable setup allows you to adjust the angle of resistance. Dedicated arm training builds both strength and muscular definition.', '97921201', '97921201-Cable-Behind-The-Back-Tricep-Dip-(male)_Upper-Arms.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:26.808474+00', '1. Adjust the cable machine to the correct height and attachment for Cable Behind The Back Triceps Dip. 2. Lower your body by bending your elbows to about 90 degrees. 3. Push back up until your arms are fully extended. 4. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 7, 8, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 80, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'dip', 'Behind The Back Triceps Dip', 'bench_press, tricep_pushdown, push_up', FALSE, 'cable', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 85, 88, 30, 92),
('85f38bb8-1113-458d-85aa-b82fcf83ae9c', 'Prone Rear Delt Swing (Kettlebell)', 'Shoulders', 'Kettlebell', '{"Rear Delts"}'::text[], '{"Upper Back","Traps"}'::text[], 'Build stronger shoulders with this swinging movement focusing on your rear delts. Your upper back work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. Performing this lying down removes momentum for stricter form. The kettlebell grip position adds a unique training stimulus. Shoulder development enhances both performance and upper body aesthetics.', '68411201', '68411201-Kettlebell-Prone-Rear-Delt-Swing_Shoulders_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:21.890719+00', '1. Select an appropriately weighted kettlebell for Kettlebell Prone Rear Delt Swing. 2. Lie face down (prone position) for Kettlebell Prone Rear Delt Swing. 3. Hinge at your hips, letting the weight swing back between your legs. 4. Explosively drive hips forward, propelling the weight forward/up. 5. Let gravity bring it back as you hinge for the next rep. 6. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 58, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'rear_delt', 'Prone Rear Delt Swing', 'lateral_raise, shoulder_press, front_raise', FALSE, 'kettlebell', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 75, 88, 88, 78),
('8622d940-9797-4dbe-aa40-7d0a76b1f604', 'Kneeling Cobra Push Up', 'Chest', 'Bodyweight', '{"Chest"}'::text[], '{"Triceps","Front Delts"}'::text[], 'This pushing exercise focuses on your pectorals for improved chest strength and development. You''ll also feel your triceps, front delts working to support the movement. The kneeling position adds a core stability challenge. This bodyweight exercise requires no equipment and can be done anywhere. A well-developed chest contributes to upper body strength and aesthetics.', '70861201', '70861201-Kneeling-Cobra-Push-up-(female)_Chest_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:34.322534+00', '1. Kneel on the floor (use a pad for comfort if needed). 2. Keep your body in a straight line from head to heels throughout. 3. Lower your chest toward the floor by bending your elbows. 4. Push through your palms to return to the starting position. 5. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout. Keep tension on the target muscles throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 1, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Stretch', 70, 2, 6, FALSE, TRUE, 'push_up', 'Kneeling Cobra Push Up', 'bench_press, chest_fly, dip', FALSE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 1, 30, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('862a8f56-f4d8-4890-81f6-001a135b35c2', 'Double Knee Thrust And Swipe', 'Full Body', 'Bodyweight', '{"Full Body"}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'Build power and athleticism with this high-intensity thrusting exercise that challenges your entire body. A versatile bodyweight movement perfect for home or gym training. Great for improving athletic performance, burning calories, and building conditioning. Perfect for including in both strength and hypertrophy programs.', '66711201', '66711201-Double-Knee-Thrust-and-Swipe-(male)_Plyometrics_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:23.79417+00', '1. Drive through your heels to lift your hips toward the ceiling. 2. Squeeze your glutes hard at the top of the movement. 3. Lower your hips back down with control. 4. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions. Control the movement—avoid using momentum.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'knee_drive', 'Double Knee Thrust And Swipe', 'butt_kicks, jumping_jack, mountain_climber', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('862b0f02-5577-453b-9496-7f9e44430822', 'Kneeling Quadriceps Stretch', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'Designed to lengthen your quads, the Kneeling Quadriceps Stretch helps improve mobility and prevent stiffness. The hip flexors assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. The kneeling position adds a core stability challenge. Regular stretching improves flexibility, reduces injury risk, and aids recovery.', '76021201', '76021201-Kneeling-Quadriceps-Stretch-(female)_Stretching_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:34.487002+00', '1. Kneel on the floor (use a pad for comfort if needed). 2. Move into the stretch position for Kneeling Quadriceps Stretch. 3. Ease into the stretch until you feel gentle tension (not pain). 4. Hold for 20-30 seconds, breathing deeply and relaxing into the stretch.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 1, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Stretch', 40, 2, 6, FALSE, TRUE, 'stretch_general', 'Kneeling Quadriceps Stretch', 'stretch_hip, stretch_hamstring', FALSE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 1, 30, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('862fef1c-b300-4ab1-a8dc-ca448b3f0891', 'Lying Legs Extension - Alternating', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'The Lying Alternating Legs Extension is a lower body extension exercise that targets your core. The lying position provides back support and helps isolate the target muscles. No equipment needed—your body provides all the resistance. Leg training boosts metabolism and builds functional, real-world strength.', '95221201', '95221201-Lying-Alternating-Legs-Extension-(female)_Thighs_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:35.010404+00', '1. Lie down in the appropriate position for Lying Alternating Legs Extension. 2. Extend your legs until straight, squeezing your quads at the top. 3. Lower with control back to the starting position. 4. Alternate between sides/arms/legs with each repetition. 5. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions. Maintain a neutral spine throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, 'Lying', NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 70, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'leg_exercise', 'Lying Legs Extension - Alternating', 'leg_curl, squat, leg_press, lunge', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('86495770-f1c9-4313-a852-15cc8cd2d32e', 'Standing Balance Ankle Rotation', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'Build stronger calves with this targeted rotation exercise. The standing position engages your core for stability. No equipment needed—your body provides all the resistance. Leg training boosts metabolism and builds functional, real-world strength.', '73051201', '73051201-Standing-Balance-Ankle-Rotation-(female)_Calves_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:38.425788+00', '1. Stand tall with your feet firmly planted. 2. Rotate your torso through the movement pattern for Standing Balance Ankle Rotation. 3. Control the rotation in both directions—avoid using momentum. 4. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, 'Standing', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 52, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'balance', 'Standing Balance Ankle Rotation', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('864acf62-acdb-41ff-bb6a-af25c37100ec', 'Side Plank Lift Against Wall (Wall)', 'Core', 'Wall', '{"Core","Abs"}'::text[], '{"Shoulders"}'::text[], 'Strengthen your midsection with this stabilization movement that works your abs. Your shoulders, lower back work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. A strong core improves posture, protects your spine, and enhances all other lifts.', '74371201', '74371201-Side-Plank-Lift-against-Wall-(male)_Waist_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:23.689343+00', '1. Position yourself at the appropriate distance from a wall. 2. Hold your body in a straight line from head to heels. 3. Don''t let your hips sag or pike up—engage your core and glutes. 4. Breathe steadily while maintaining the position. 5. Complete all reps with control before resting. Keep tension on the target muscles throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 62, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'side_plank', 'Side Plank Lift Against Wall', 'plank, russian_twist, woodchop', FALSE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('865fc8fd-1153-4e7a-85a3-1dac47255381', 'Kneeling Crunch (Band)', 'Core', 'Resistance Band', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'Strengthen your midsection with this crunching movement that works your abs. Your hip flexors work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. Kneeling helps eliminate lower body momentum from the movement. Resistance bands provide accommodating resistance that increases through the range of motion. Building core stability helps with everything from heavy deadlifts to daily activities.', '9041201', '09041201-Band-Kneeling-Crunch-(female)_Waist_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:30.887491+00', '1. Secure the resistance band appropriately for Band Kneeling Crunch. 2. Kneel on the floor (use a pad for comfort if needed). 3. Curl your shoulders off the floor by contracting your abs. 4. Don''t pull on your neck—focus on the abdominal contraction. 5. Lower with control, maintaining some tension. 6. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 12, 20, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 75, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'crunch', 'Kneeling Crunch', 'leg_raise, plank, russian_twist, v_up', FALSE, 'band', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 60, 85, 90, 50),
('86618825-847e-4ac8-b52f-1f0885a10598', 'Single Arm High Row (Cable)', 'Back', 'Cables', '{"Upper Back"}'::text[], '{"Lats","Biceps","Rear Delts"}'::text[], 'This rowing exercise strengthens the muscles between your shoulder blades. The biceps, rear delts assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. The cable setup allows you to adjust the angle of resistance. Back development is crucial for pulling strength and overall upper body function. Works well as both a primary exercise or accessory movement.', '65101201', '65101201-Cable-Single-Arm-High-Row_Back_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:28.851102+00', '1. Set the cable pulley to the highest position and attach your preferred handle. 2. Pull the weight toward your torso, leading with your elbow(s). 3. Squeeze your shoulder blades together at the peak contraction. 4. Extend back out with control, feeling the stretch in your back. 5. Complete all reps on one side, then switch to the other side. 6. Complete all reps with control before resting. Don''t rush—quality over quantity.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 7, 8, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 75, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'cable_row', 'Single Arm High Row', 'bent_over_row, lat_pulldown, bicep_curl', FALSE, 'cable', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 85, 88, 30, 92),
('86631daa-910c-4084-9237-a1f8a7a7f1af', 'Kneeling Hamstring Reach (Gymnastic Rings)', 'Legs', 'Gymnastic Rings', '{"Hamstrings"}'::text[], '{"Glutes"}'::text[], 'The Kneeling Hamstring Reach provides a deep stretch for your hamstrings, ideal for recovery and mobility work. Secondary activation of your lower back provides additional muscle engagement. Kneeling helps eliminate lower body momentum from the movement. Include this in your routine for better mobility and reduced muscle tension.', '83791201', '83791201-Kneeling-Hamstring-Reach-(female)_Stretching_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:34.322534+00', '1. Kneel on the floor (use a pad for comfort if needed). 2. Move into the stretch position for Kneeling Hamstring Reach. 3. Ease into the stretch until you feel gentle tension (not pain). 4. Hold for 20-30 seconds, breathing deeply and relaxing into the stretch.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 38, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'general_exercise', 'Kneeling Hamstring Reach', 'squat, leg_extension, lunge', FALSE, 'gymnastic_rings', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 68, 85, 85, 70),
('867fd23f-6b4c-4525-b343-802ad97a9165', 'Lying Butterfly Leg Raise', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Lower Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'Build leg strength with this raising movement focusing on your abs. The hip flexors assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. Performing this lying down removes momentum for stricter form. A versatile bodyweight movement perfect for home or gym training. Leg training boosts metabolism and builds functional, real-world strength.', '73981201', '73981201-Lying-Butterfly-Leg-Raise-(female)_Hips_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:35.133808+00', '1. Lie down in the appropriate position for Lying Butterfly Leg Raise. 2. With a slight bend in your elbows, move the weight in a wide arc. 3. Squeeze your chest muscles at the center/top of the movement. 4. Return with control, feeling the stretch at the bottom. 5. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, 'Lying', NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 70, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'leg_raise', 'Lying Butterfly Leg Raise', 'crunch, plank, v_up', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('86913728-95d5-42b1-8278-c142683debc9', 'Burpee (Dumbbell)', 'Full Body', 'Dumbbells', '{"Full Body"}'::text[], '{"Chest","Quads","Core"}'::text[], 'The Dumbbell Burpee is a cardiovascular exercise that improves endurance and heart health. The chest, quads assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. The dumbbell variation provides freedom of movement and greater range of motion. Cardiovascular exercise improves heart health, endurance, and helps manage weight.', '12011201', '12011201-Dumbbell-burpee_Cardio.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:27.805708+00', '1. Select a pair of dumbbells at an appropriate weight for Dumbbell Burpee. 2. Squat down and place hands on the floor, jump feet back to plank. 3. Jump feet back toward hands, then explosively jump up with arms overhead. 4. Land softly and immediately begin the next rep. 5. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 4, NULL, 8, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 7, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Plyometrics', 62, 9, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'burpee', 'Burpee', 'mountain_climber, box_jump, jumping_jack', FALSE, 'dumbbell', FALSE, 3, 60, 4, 92, 90, 92, 90),
('8691fd94-20a1-47bc-a85b-853faff12924', 'Straight Leg Russian Twist (Dumbbell)', 'Core', 'Dumbbells', '{"Obliques"}'::text[], '{"Abs"}'::text[], 'The Dumbbell Straight Leg Russian Twist targets your obliques through a twisting motion, building rotational core strength. Secondary activation of your abs provides additional muscle engagement. Using dumbbells requires more stabilization than barbell variations. Core strength is foundational for athletic performance and injury prevention.', '42491201', '42491201-Dumbbell-Straight-Leg-Russian-Twist_Waist.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:29.61214+00', '1. Select a pair of dumbbells at an appropriate weight for Dumbbell Straight Leg Russian Twist. 2. Rotate your torso through the movement pattern for Dumbbell Straight Leg Russian Twist. 3. Control the rotation in both directions—avoid using momentum. 4. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 62, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'russian_twist', 'Straight Leg Russian Twist', 'crunch, plank, leg_raise, wood_chop', TRUE, 'dumbbell', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 92, 90, 92, 90),
('869a7d41-a8d0-40a6-8870-383f5534438f', 'Triceps Dip Floor (Dip Bars)', 'Arms', 'Dip Bars', '{"Triceps"}'::text[], '{"Chest","Shoulders"}'::text[], 'The Triceps Dip Floor targets your triceps through a dipping motion. You''ll also feel your triceps, front delts working to support the movement. A versatile bodyweight movement perfect for home or gym training. Arm strength supports grip, pulling, and pushing in compound movements.', '51101201', '51101201-Triceps-Dip-Floor-(female)_Upper-Arms_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:39.79101+00', '1. Position yourself on the floor for Triceps Dip Floor. 2. Lower your body by bending your elbows to about 90 degrees. 3. Push back up until your arms are fully extended. 4. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions. Keep your shoulders relaxed and away from your ears.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 65, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'dip', 'Triceps Dip Floor', 'bench_press, tricep_pushdown, push_up', TRUE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('869a966b-b2f1-49b0-a4c8-1b763b5ada2d', 'Incline Triceps Extension (EZ Bar)', 'Arms', 'EZ Bar, Incline Bench', '{"Triceps"}'::text[], '{"Chest","Shoulders"}'::text[], 'This extension movement isolates your triceps for improved arm development. The incline angle shifts emphasis toward the upper portion of the target muscles. Using a barbell provides stability for progressive overload. Arm strength supports grip, pulling, and pushing in compound movements.', '4491201', '04491201-EZ-Barbell-Incline-Triceps-Extension_Upper-Arms-FI.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:26.507873+00', '1. Grip a barbell with hands at the appropriate width for EZ Barbell Incline Triceps Extension. 2. Extend at the elbow until your arm is straight, squeezing the tricep. 3. Lower with control, keeping your upper arm stationary. 4. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 95, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'tricep_extension', 'EZ Incline Triceps Extension', 'EZ Incline Triceps Extension', FALSE, 'barbell', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 95, 80, 65, 95),
('869d0351-b827-4a24-8316-ca0adeb03bd0', 'Standing Opposite Straight Arm Clasp (Left Over Right)', 'Full Body', 'Bodyweight', '{"Full Body"}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'The Standing Opposite Straight Arm Clasp (left Over Ri is a compound movement exercise that engages your entire body. Performing this standing challenges your balance and core engagement. This bodyweight exercise requires no equipment and can be done anywhere. Compound movements like this develop coordination, power, and overall fitness.', '94151201', '94151201-Standing-Opposite-Straight-Arm-Clasp-(left-over-ri.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:38.7451+00', '1. Begin in a standing position with good posture. 2. Set up in the starting position for Standing Opposite Straight Arm Clasp (left Over Ri. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your full body. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 5. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, 'Standing', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 52, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'arm_exercise', 'Standing Opposite Straight Arm Clasp (left Over Ri', 'bicep_curl, tricep_extension, hammer_curl', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('869d8a0f-9e88-4eff-921a-13043ab43d51', 'Torque Tank Push', 'Full Body', 'Bodyweight', '{"Full Body"}'::text[], '{"Chest","Quads"}'::text[], 'Develop functional strength with the Torque Tank Push, a comprehensive pushing exercise. Secondary activation of your chest, quads provides additional muscle engagement. Full body exercises are time-efficient and build functional, real-world strength.', '87021201', '87021201-Torque-Tank-Push-(male)_Thighs_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:20.982555+00', '1. Set up in the starting position for Torque Tank Push. 2. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your full body. 3. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 4. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'general_exercise', 'Torque Tank Push', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('86a07343-578e-4e48-a5b7-55526a1838f6', 'Mountain Hops', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Calves"}'::text[], 'Build power and athleticism with this high-intensity movement exercise that challenges your entire body. No equipment needed—your body provides all the resistance. Develops fast-twitch muscle fibers for quicker, more powerful movements. Keep your core engaged throughout the exercise. Consistency with this movement will yield noticeable results.', '54931201', '54931201-Mountain-Hops-(female)_Plyometrics_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:35.532804+00', '1. Set up in the starting position for Mountain Hops. 2. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your full body. 3. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 4. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 4, NULL, 8, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 7, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Plyometrics', 50, 9, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'hop', 'Mountain Hops', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('86bb55f0-2db4-4aa9-bda6-7503b916e2fe', 'Front Raise (Cable)', 'Shoulders', 'Cables', '{"Front Delts"}'::text[], '{"Chest"}'::text[], 'Target your front delts with the Cable Front Raise, an effective shoulder raising exercise. Cables provide constant tension throughout the full range of motion. Strong shoulders improve overhead strength and support nearly all upper body movements.', '22301201', '22301201-Cable-Front-Raise-(female)_Shoulders.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:31.931873+00', '1. Adjust the cable machine to the correct height and attachment for Cable Front Raise. 2. Raise the weight in front of you to shoulder height. 3. Lower with control, maintaining tension throughout. 4. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout. Ensure full range of motion on each rep.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 12, 20, NULL, 4, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 80, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'front_raise', 'Front Raise', 'shoulder_press, lateral_raise, rear_delt_fly', FALSE, 'cable', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 85, 88, 30, 92),
('86cae56f-9ee3-4f07-8142-ad63f980f44f', 'Crossover Kneeling Hip Flexor Stretch', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Hips"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'Build leg strength with this stretching movement focusing on your chest. Secondary activation of your front delts provides additional muscle engagement. Kneeling helps eliminate lower body momentum from the movement. This bodyweight exercise requires no equipment and can be done anywhere. Strong legs are the foundation for athletic performance and functional fitness.', '2651201', '02651201-Crossover-Kneeling-Hip-Flexor-Stretch-(female)_Hip.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:32.501166+00', '1. Kneel on the floor (use a pad for comfort if needed). 2. Set up in the starting position for Crossover Kneeling Hip Flexor Stretch. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your chest. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 5. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 1, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Stretch', 40, 2, 6, FALSE, TRUE, 'hip_stretch', 'Crossover Kneeling Hip Flexor Stretch', 'stretch_hamstring, stretch_glute, stretch_back', FALSE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 1, 30, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('86cc5e54-b17a-466f-ac07-42f75f4526b9', 'Seated Delts Stretch (Chair)', 'Shoulders', 'Chair', '{"Shoulders"}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'Target your full body with this stretching stretch that helps restore range of motion. Being seated provides stability, allowing you to focus on the working muscles. Include this in your routine for better mobility and reduced muscle tension. Perfect for including in both strength and hypertrophy programs.', '91681201', '91681201-Sitting-Delts-Stretch-on-a-Chair-(female)_Stretchi.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:37.628647+00', '1. Position yourself with a sturdy chair for support or as part of the movement. 2. Sit with your back supported, core engaged, feet flat on the floor. 3. Move into the stretch position for Seated Delts Stretch On A Chair. 4. Ease into the stretch until you feel gentle tension (not pain). 5. Hold for 20-30 seconds, breathing deeply and relaxing into the stretch.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 1, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Stretch', 25, 2, 6, FALSE, TRUE, 'stretch_general', 'Seated Delts Stretch On A Chair', 'stretch_hip, stretch_back, stretch_shoulder', FALSE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 1, 30, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('86ce8e03-4b87-4fa1-9ebf-94539462e49a', 'Spider Plank', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Shoulders","Lower Back"}'::text[], 'Build leg strength with this stabilization movement focusing on your abs. The shoulders, lower back assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. A versatile bodyweight movement perfect for home or gym training. Strong legs are the foundation for athletic performance and functional fitness. Maintain proper breathing - exhale during the effort phase.', '39531201', '39531201-Spider-Plank-(female)_Hips_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:38.153182+00', '1. Hold your body in a straight line from head to heels. 2. Don''t let your hips sag or pike up—engage your core and glutes. 3. Breathe steadily while maintaining the position. 4. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout. Maintain consistent tempo throughout the set. Beneficial for overall legs development.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 70, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'plank', 'Spider Plank', 'side_plank, dead_bug, hollow_hold', TRUE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('86d1a839-bb58-4ae8-9c16-ee1e673c5f1c', 'Bench Dip On Floor', 'Chest', 'Bodyweight', '{"Lower Chest"}'::text[], '{"Triceps","Front Delts"}'::text[], 'Build stronger triceps with this dipping exercise for bigger arms. You''ll also feel your triceps, front delts working to support the movement. Arm strength supports grip, pulling, and pushing in compound movements.', '25461201', '25461201-Bench-dip-on-floor-(female)_Upper-Arms.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:31.133197+00', '1. Position yourself on the floor for Bench Dip On Floor. 2. Lower your body by bending your elbows to about 90 degrees. 3. Push back up until your arms are fully extended. 4. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 65, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'dip', 'Bench Dip On Floor', 'bench_press, tricep_pushdown, push_up', TRUE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('86d2bacf-56f5-43a7-affd-5e726551aa05', 'High Row (TRX)', 'Back', 'TRX', '{"Upper Back"}'::text[], '{"Lats","Biceps","Rear Delts"}'::text[], 'This rowing exercise strengthens the muscles between your shoulder blades. The biceps, rear delts assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. Suspension training adds instability, increasing core activation throughout. Back development is crucial for pulling strength and overall upper body function.', '94961201', '94961201-Suspender-High-Row_Back_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:21.995567+00', '1. Adjust the TRX/suspension straps to the appropriate length for Suspender High Row. 2. Pull the weight toward your torso, leading with your elbow(s). 3. Squeeze your shoulder blades together at the peak contraction. 4. Extend back out with control, feeling the stretch in your back. 5. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 60, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'cable_row', 'Suspender High Row', 'lat_pulldown, bent_over_row, pull_up', FALSE, 'trx', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 68, 85, 85, 70),
('86deb535-c4ae-45c2-bac5-c5625aaf1509', 'Shoulder Rotation Twist Split Lunge Stretch', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'Build stronger quads with this lunging movement that develops leg drive and power. Your glutes, hamstrings work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. No equipment needed—your body provides all the resistance. Lower body strength improves everything from walking to heavy compound lifts.', '56181201', '56181201-Shoulder-Rotation-Twist-Split-Lunge-Stretch-(female)_Hips_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:36.985772+00', '1. Step forward into a lunge until both knees are at about 90 degrees. 2. Push through your front/working leg to return to the starting position. 3. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions. Focus on squeezing the target muscle at peak contraction. This variation specifically emphasizes the quads.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 1, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Stretch', 60, 2, 6, FALSE, TRUE, 'hip_stretch', 'Shoulder Rotation Twist Split Lunge Stretch', 'squat, split_squat, step_up, leg_press', FALSE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 1, 30, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('86f6e017-8b30-4665-b43a-7dd127260673', 'Standing Elbow Push Up And Elbow Fly', 'Chest', 'Bodyweight', '{"Chest"}'::text[], '{"Front Delts"}'::text[], 'Target your chest with the Standing Elbow Push Up And Elbow Fly, an effective pushing movement for upper body strength. Your triceps, front delts work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. Performing this standing challenges your balance and core engagement. This bodyweight exercise requires no equipment and can be done anywhere. A well-developed chest contributes to upper body strength and aesthetics.', '94741201', '94741201-Standing-Elbow-Push-Up-And-Elbow-Fly-(female)_Ches.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:38.570929+00', '1. Stand tall with your feet firmly planted. 2. Keep your body in a straight line from head to heels throughout. 3. Lower your chest toward the floor by bending your elbows. 4. Push through your palms to return to the starting position. 5. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, 'Standing', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 72, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'push_up', 'Standing Elbow Push Up And Elbow Fly', 'bench_press, chest_fly, dip', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('870422af-770c-49e7-aeb4-889329fb3ae9', 'Elbow Prayer Push Circle Draw', 'Chest', 'Bodyweight', '{"Chest"}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'This pushing exercise focuses on your pectorals for improved chest strength and development. No equipment needed—your body provides all the resistance. Chest strength improves pushing power for sports, daily tasks, and other lifts.', '76411201', '76411201-Elbow-Prayer-Push-Circle Draw-(male)_Chest_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:21.732034+00', '1. Set up in the starting position for Elbow Prayer Push Circle Draw. 2. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your chest. 3. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 4. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 35, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'boxing', 'Elbow Prayer Push Circle Draw', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('8743089a-4af6-4933-95a9-5b043c1ed47d', 'Around Head Rotation (Kettlebell)', 'Shoulders', 'Kettlebell', '{"Rotator Cuff"}'::text[], '{"Shoulders"}'::text[], 'Build a stronger back with this rotation movement targeting your delts. The core assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. Kettlebells are excellent for building functional, real-world strength. A strong back improves posture, prevents injury, and balances pressing movements.', '71011201', '71011201-Kettlebell-Around-Head-Rotation-(female)_Back_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:34.196858+00', '1. Select an appropriately weighted kettlebell for Kettlebell Around Head Rotation. 2. Rotate your torso through the movement pattern for Kettlebell Around Head Rotation. 3. Control the rotation in both directions—avoid using momentum. 4. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 58, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'neck_stretch', 'Around Head Rotation', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'kettlebell', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 75, 88, 88, 78),
('8765b7bf-a379-40f5-895d-5a668b084a79', 'Assisted Chin Up - Neutral Grip (Machine)', 'Back', 'Lever Machine', '{"Lats"}'::text[], '{"Biceps","Upper Back"}'::text[], 'This movement exercise emphasizes your lats for improved back development. Secondary activation of your biceps provides additional muscle engagement. The machine guides your movement path for safer, more controlled repetitions. A strong back improves posture, prevents injury, and balances pressing movements.', '80111201', '80111201-Lever-Assisted-Neutral-Grip-Chin-Up-(male)_Back_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:25.123298+00', '1. Adjust the machine settings (seat height, weight, pads) to fit your body for Lever Assisted Neutral Grip Chin Up. 2. Use a neutral grip with palms facing each other. 3. Pull yourself up, focusing on bicep and lat engagement. 4. Raise until chin is over the bar, lower with full control. 5. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 78, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'pull_up', 'Lever Assisted Chin Up - Neutral Grip', 'Lever Assisted Chin Up - Neutral Grip', FALSE, 'machine', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 80, 75, 20, 88);
INSERT INTO _exercise_staging (id, name, category, equipment, primary_muscles, secondary_muscles, description, video_code, video_filename, gender, is_custom, created_at, steps_to_perform, movement_pattern, force_type, movement_type, laterality, plane_of_motion, difficulty_level, complexity_score, strength_rating, hypertrophy_rating, power_rating, endurance_rating, body_position, bench_angle, grip_type, grip_width, optimal_rep_range_min, optimal_rep_range_max, placement_in_workout, fatigability, popularity_score, home_gym_friendly, instructions, workout_type, practicality_score, fat_loss_rating, general_fitness_rating, is_compound, supersetable, exercise_family, base_exercise_name, complementary_families, is_equipment_primary, equipment_category, duration_based, recommended_sets, rest_seconds, muscles_worked_count, priority_build_muscle, priority_get_lean, priority_home, priority_gym) VALUES
('876b0197-d8ae-47c0-9f64-b363f3813b60', 'Assisted Pull Up (Pull-Up Bar)', 'Back', 'Pull-Up Bar', '{"Lats"}'::text[], '{"Biceps","Upper Back"}'::text[], 'This pulling exercise emphasizes your lats for improved back development. The biceps, upper back assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. This bodyweight exercise requires no equipment and can be done anywhere. A strong back improves posture, prevents injury, and balances pressing movements.', '25291201', '25291201-Assisted-Pull-up-(female)_Back_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:30.54809+00', '1. Pull yourself up by driving your elbows down and back. 2. Continue until your chin clears the bar, then lower with control to a full hang. 3. Complete all reps with control before resting. Start with lighter weight to perfect your form. This variation specifically emphasizes the lats.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 70, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'pull_up', 'Assisted Pull Up', 'lat_pulldown, bent_over_row, bicep_curl', TRUE, 'pull_up_bar', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('876e5fd5-cdde-4afa-886b-f5d4f798daea', 'Lunge (Barbell)', 'Legs', 'Barbell', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'Build stronger quads with this lunging movement that develops leg drive and power. Your glutes, hamstrings work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. Using a barbell provides stability for progressive overload. Lower body strength improves everything from walking to heavy compound lifts.', '541201', '00541201-Barbell-Lunge_Thighs-FIX_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:27.145158+00', '1. Grip a barbell with hands at the appropriate width for Barbell Lunge. 2. Step forward into a lunge until both knees are at about 90 degrees. 3. Push through your front/working leg to return to the starting position. 4. Complete all reps with control before resting.', 'Lunge', 'Push', 'Compound', 'Unilateral (Alternating)', NULL, 3, NULL, 7, 8, NULL, 5, 'Standing', NULL, 'Overhand (Pronated)', 'Standard', 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 82, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'lunge', 'Lunge', 'split_squat, step_up, squat', FALSE, 'barbell', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 95, 80, 65, 95),
('877a7269-da34-4d38-995e-9320aa94e3ea', 'Prayer Push Knee Thrust', 'Full Body', 'Bodyweight', '{"Full Body"}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'This dynamic pushing movement gets your heart rate up while developing explosive strength. No equipment needed—your body provides all the resistance. Plyometric training builds explosive power that transfers to sports and daily activities. Progress gradually by increasing resistance over time.', '77811201', '77811201-Prayer-Push-Knee-Thrust-(female)_Plyometrics_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:35.801913+00', '1. Drive through your heels to lift your hips toward the ceiling. 2. Squeeze your glutes hard at the top of the movement. 3. Lower your hips back down with control. 4. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout. Focus on squeezing the target muscle at peak contraction. An effective movement for your plyometrics routine.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 35, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'knee_drive', 'Prayer Push Knee Thrust', 'butt_kicks, jumping_jack, mountain_climber', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('877fb07c-e59c-4e82-8fd8-0836a4988ee1', 'Seated Wide Pulldown (Machine)', 'Back', 'Lat Pulldown Machine', '{"Lats"}'::text[], '{"Biceps","Upper Back"}'::text[], 'This pulling exercise emphasizes your lats for improved back development. You''ll also feel your biceps, upper back working to support the movement. Being seated provides stability, allowing you to focus on the working muscles. The fixed path allows you to focus purely on muscular effort. Back development is crucial for pulling strength and overall upper body function.', '88481201', '88481201-Lever-Seated-Wide-Pulldown-(plate-loaded)-(male)_B.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:21.995567+00', '1. Adjust the machine settings (seat height, weight, pads) to fit your body for Lever Seated Wide Pulldown. 2. Sit with your back supported, core engaged, feet flat on the floor. 3. Use a wide grip (wider than shoulder-width) for this variation. 4. Pull the bar/handle down toward your upper chest. 5. Drive your elbows down and back, squeezing your lats. 6. Control the weight back up without letting it yank your arms. 7. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, 'Seated', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 60, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'lat_pulldown', 'Lever Seated Wide Pulldown', 'pull_up, bent_over_row, cable_row, face_pull', FALSE, 'machine', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 80, 75, 20, 88),
('8780373d-eb65-4de4-a525-f2dee284754d', 'Floor Fly (Dumbbell)', 'Chest', 'Dumbbells', '{"Chest"}'::text[], '{"Front Delts"}'::text[], 'Target your chest with the Dumbbell Floor Fly, an effective flying movement for upper body strength. You''ll also feel your front delts working to support the movement. The dumbbell variation provides freedom of movement and greater range of motion. A well-developed chest contributes to upper body strength and aesthetics.', '41491201', '41491201-Dumbbell-Floor-Fly_Chest.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:22.644637+00', '1. Select a pair of dumbbells at an appropriate weight for Dumbbell Floor Fly. 2. Position yourself on the floor for Dumbbell Floor Fly. 3. With a slight bend in your elbows, move the weight in a wide arc. 4. Squeeze your chest muscles at the center/top of the movement. 5. Return with control, feeling the stretch at the bottom. 6. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 77, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'chest_fly', 'Floor Fly', 'bench_press, incline_press, push_up', TRUE, 'dumbbell', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 92, 90, 92, 90),
('87840845-80cb-41b9-bac5-0fdec782dc75', 'Hanging Oblique Knee Raise (Pull-Up Bar)', 'Core', 'Pull-Up Bar', '{"Obliques"}'::text[], '{"Abs"}'::text[], 'Build a stronger core with the Hanging Oblique Knee Raise, focusing on your abs. Secondary activation of your hip flexors provides additional muscle engagement. The hanging position challenges your grip while targeting the primary muscles. A versatile bodyweight movement perfect for home or gym training. A strong core improves posture, protects your spine, and enhances all other lifts.', '30901201', '30901201-Hanging-Oblique-Knee-Raise-(female)_Waist.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:33.960339+00', '1. Grip the bar and hang with arms fully extended, engaging your shoulders. 2. Raise the weight in the prescribed direction for Hanging Oblique Knee Raise. 3. Lower with control, maintaining tension throughout. 4. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 70, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'leg_raise', 'Hanging Oblique Knee Raise', 'crunch, plank, v_up', FALSE, 'pull_up_bar', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('87b9ad28-9bfa-4b09-a75c-484f105e78cb', 'Standing T Spine Press', 'Full Body', 'Bodyweight', '{"Full Body"}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'The Bodyweight Standing T Spine Press is a pressing exercise that develops back strength and muscle. Performing this standing challenges your balance and core engagement. This bodyweight exercise requires no equipment and can be done anywhere. Back development is crucial for pulling strength and overall upper body function.', '83431201', '83431201-Bodyweight-Standing-T-spine-Press-(female)_Back_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:31.60311+00', '1. Begin in a standing position with good posture. 2. Execute the pressing motion for Bodyweight Standing T Spine Press, extending through the target muscles. 3. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, 'Standing', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 72, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'cycling', 'Standing T Spine Press', 'lateral_raise, front_raise, rear_delt_fly, upright_row', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('87cbc084-c1cf-4a40-a75e-cc55adff4cc9', 'Straight Leg Diagonal Kickback (Cable)', 'Legs', 'Cables', '{"Glutes"}'::text[], '{"Rear Delts"}'::text[], 'This kicking exercise isolates your glutes for improved hip strength and power. Your hamstrings work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. Cable resistance creates smooth, continuous muscle engagement. Leg training boosts metabolism and builds functional, real-world strength.', '83391201', '83391201-Cable-Straight-Leg-Diagonal-Kickback-(male)_Hips_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:26.93819+00', '1. Adjust the cable machine to the correct height and attachment for Cable Straight Leg Diagonal Kickback. 2. Keep your upper arm stationary and extend your forearm back. 3. Squeeze at full extension, then return with control. 4. Complete all reps with control before resting. Focus on the mind-muscle connection.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 12, 20, NULL, 4, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 60, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'romanian_deadlift', 'Straight Leg Diagonal Kickback', 'deadlift, leg_curl, hip_thrust', FALSE, 'cable', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 85, 88, 30, 92),
('87d2f5e0-802a-47aa-8b13-4d23950c7626', 'Step Over Box (Dumbbell)', 'Full Body', 'Dumbbells', '{"Full Body"}'::text[], '{"Quads"}'::text[], 'Build leg strength with this stepping movement focusing on your full body. Secondary activation of your quads provides additional muscle engagement. Using dumbbells requires more stabilization than barbell variations. Strong legs are the foundation for athletic performance and functional fitness.', '96121201', '96121201-Dumbbell-Step-over-Box-(male)_Thighs_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:24.307972+00', '1. Select a pair of dumbbells at an appropriate weight for Dumbbell Step Over Box. 2. Set up a box or step platform at the appropriate height. 3. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 8, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 62, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'general_exercise', 'Step Over Box', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', TRUE, 'dumbbell', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 92, 90, 92, 90),
('87d4c9ec-9bb5-4aae-a8c4-5b1d66f79c53', 'Standing Leg Calf Raise (Barbell)', 'Legs', 'Barbell', '{"Calves"}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'The Barbell Standing Leg Calf Raise isolates your calf muscles through a raising motion. Performing this standing challenges your balance and core engagement. Barbells enable bilateral loading for building raw strength. Lower body strength improves everything from walking to heavy compound lifts.', '1081201', '01081201-Barbell-Standing-Leg-Calf-Raise_Calves.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:26.93819+00', '1. Grip a barbell with hands at the appropriate width for Barbell Standing Leg Calf Raise. 2. Stand with feet about shoulder-width apart. 3. Lower your heels below the platform to get a full stretch. 4. Rise up onto your toes as high as possible, squeezing your calves. 5. Lower with control and repeat. 6. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, 'Standing', NULL, NULL, NULL, 12, 20, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 94, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'calf_raise', 'Standing Leg Calf Raise', 'calf_raise, seated_calf_raise', FALSE, 'barbell', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 95, 80, 65, 95),
('87d56c1a-3913-4e3c-83f0-df35b844dad4', 'Lying Bent Leg Tuck', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'This movement exercise engages your abs for improved core stability and strength. Performing this lying down removes momentum for stricter form. No equipment needed—your body provides all the resistance. A strong core improves posture, protects your spine, and enhances all other lifts. Keep your core engaged throughout the exercise.', '67201201', '67201201-Lying-Bent-Leg-Tuck-(female)_Waist_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:35.133808+00', '1. Lie down in the appropriate position for Lying Bent Leg Tuck. 2. Set up in the starting position for Lying Bent Leg Tuck. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your abs. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 5. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, 'Lying', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'leg_exercise', 'Lying Bent Leg Tuck', 'squat, lunge, leg_press', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('87d72fc0-89f4-4469-b9b3-b2296e78123f', 'Criss Cross Arms Outer Rotation', 'Full Body', 'Bodyweight', '{"Full Body"}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'The Criss Cross Arms Outer Rotation is an explosive exercise that combines cardiovascular training with dynamic rotation movements. Your shoulders, core work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. A versatile bodyweight movement perfect for home or gym training. Great for improving athletic performance, burning calories, and building conditioning.', '78181201', '78181201-Criss-Cross-Arms-Outer-Rotation-(male)_Plyometrics.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:26.507873+00', '1. Rotate your torso through the movement pattern for Criss Cross Arms Outer Rotation. 2. Control the rotation in both directions—avoid using momentum. 3. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'boxing', 'Criss Cross Arms Outer Rotation', 'bicep_curl, tricep_extension, hammer_curl', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('87ddd982-9f74-4ac5-99e6-b34775ee3a20', 'Standing Double Elbow Touch And Elbow Raise', 'Shoulders', 'Bodyweight', '{"Rear Delts"}'::text[], '{"Upper Back","Rotator Cuff"}'::text[], 'This raising exercise engages your abs for improved core stability and strength. The obliques assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. The standing position engages your core for stability. A versatile bodyweight movement perfect for home or gym training. Building core stability helps with everything from heavy deadlifts to daily activities. Quality repetitions are more important than quantity.', '96161201', '96161201-Standing-Double-Elbow-Touch-and-Elbow-Raise-(femal.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:38.570929+00', '1. Begin in a standing position with good posture. 2. Raise the weight in the prescribed direction for Standing Double Elbow Touch And Elbow Raise. 3. Lower with control, maintaining tension throughout. 4. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, 'Standing', NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 72, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'general_exercise', 'Standing Double Elbow Touch And Elbow Raise', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('87e779d3-4db3-4703-9e86-e037422632da', 'Lying Crunch Through Legs Abduction', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'This crunching exercise engages your abs for improved core stability and strength. The hip flexors assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. The lying position provides back support and helps isolate the target muscles. A versatile bodyweight movement perfect for home or gym training. A strong core improves posture, protects your spine, and enhances all other lifts.', '67181201', '67181201-Lying-Crunch-Through-Legs-Abduction-(male)_Waist_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:20.667107+00', '1. Lie down in the appropriate position for Lying Crunch Through Legs Abduction. 2. Curl your shoulders off the floor by contracting your abs. 3. Don''t pull on your neck—focus on the abdominal contraction. 4. Lower with control, maintaining some tension. 5. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, 'Lying', NULL, NULL, NULL, 12, 20, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 70, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'hip_abduction', 'Lying Crunch Through Legs Abduction', 'plank, leg_raise, russian_twist, sit_up', TRUE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('8802a295-4a05-4f5d-b299-ce3dc66250a9', 'Kneeling Side Leg To Kick', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'Build leg strength with this kicking movement focusing on your core. The kneeling position adds a core stability challenge. This bodyweight exercise requires no equipment and can be done anywhere. Strong legs are the foundation for athletic performance and functional fitness.', '46911201', '46911201-Kneeling-Side-Leg-to-Kick-(male)_Hips.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:29.242428+00', '1. Kneel on the floor (use a pad for comfort if needed). 2. Set up in the starting position for Kneeling Side Leg To Kick. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your core. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 5. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'leg_exercise', 'Kneeling Side Leg To Kick', 'hip_flexor, lunge, dynamic_warmup', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('88049cae-03fd-460e-8f3f-16dd1894b52e', 'Standing Elbow Touches (hands On Neck)', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'Strengthen your midsection with this movement movement that works your abs. Your obliques work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. Performing this standing challenges your balance and core engagement. No equipment needed—your body provides all the resistance. A strong core improves posture, protects your spine, and enhances all other lifts.', '76011201', '76011201-Bodyweight-Standing-Elbow-Touches-(Hands-on-neck)-.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:31.475486+00', '1. Stand with feet about shoulder-width apart. 2. Set up in the starting position for Bodyweight Standing Elbow Touches. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your abs. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 5. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, 'Standing', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 34, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'neck_exercise', 'Standing Elbow Touches', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('88168fde-8103-405a-821b-da0490f2ff67', 'Standing Hip Circle', 'Shoulders', 'Bodyweight', '{"Shoulders"}'::text[], '{"Traps"}'::text[], 'Target your delts with the Standing Hip Circle, an effective shoulder movement exercise. Performing this standing challenges your balance and core engagement. A versatile bodyweight movement perfect for home or gym training. Strong shoulders improve overhead strength and support nearly all upper body movements.', '34111201', '34111201-Standing-Hip-Circle-(female).mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:38.7451+00', '1. Stand tall with your feet firmly planted. 2. Set up in the starting position for Standing Hip Circle. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your delts. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 5. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, 'Standing', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 52, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'hip_circle', 'Standing Hip Circle', 'hip_thrust, lunge, squat', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('88172bd4-a6af-4699-98b3-b76b4ae0bc53', 'Seated Triceps Extension (Chair)', 'Arms', 'Chair', '{"Triceps"}'::text[], '{"Chest","Shoulders"}'::text[], 'This extension movement isolates your triceps for improved arm development. The seated position helps isolate the target muscles by removing momentum. Dedicated arm training builds both strength and muscular definition.', '90891201', '90891201-Sitting-Triceps-Extension-on-a-Chair-(female)_Uppe.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:37.99429+00', '1. Position yourself with a sturdy chair for support or as part of the movement. 2. Sit with your back supported, core engaged, feet flat on the floor. 3. Extend at the elbow until your arm is straight, squeezing the tricep. 4. Lower with control, keeping your upper arm stationary. 5. Complete all reps with control before resting. Focus on squeezing the target muscle at peak contraction.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 65, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'tricep_extension', 'Seated Triceps Extension On A Chair', 'tricep_pushdown, close_grip_bench', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('881edc30-12c3-4c63-9606-9b1e5ec779ab', 'March On Spot Overhead Press (Dumbbell)', 'Shoulders', 'Dumbbells', '{"Front Delts"}'::text[], '{"Side Delts","Triceps"}'::text[], 'This dynamic pressing movement gets your heart rate up while developing explosive strength. Secondary activation of your triceps provides additional muscle engagement. The dumbbell variation provides freedom of movement and greater range of motion. Plyometric training builds explosive power that transfers to sports and daily activities.', '82671201', '82671201-Dumbbell-March-on-Spot-Overhead-Press-(male)_Plyom.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:20.392006+00', '1. Select a pair of dumbbells at an appropriate weight for Dumbbell March On Spot Overhead Press. 2. Start with the weight at shoulder level. 3. Press directly overhead until your arms are fully extended. 4. Lower back to shoulder level with control. 5. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 8, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 97, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'shoulder_press', 'March On Spot Overhead Press', 'lateral_raise, front_raise, rear_delt', TRUE, 'dumbbell', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 92, 90, 92, 90),
('881f14f0-2844-46df-a8e6-b83682bc0c75', 'Isometric Hold Push Up', 'Chest', 'Bodyweight', '{"Chest"}'::text[], '{"Triceps","Front Delts"}'::text[], 'The Isometric Hold Push Up is a pushing exercise that targets your chest muscles. Secondary activation of your triceps, front delts provides additional muscle engagement. No equipment needed—your body provides all the resistance. Chest strength improves pushing power for sports, daily tasks, and other lifts.', '93251201', '93251201-Isometric-Hold-Push-up-(female)_Chest_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:34.196858+00', '1. Keep your body in a straight line from head to heels throughout. 2. Lower your chest toward the floor by bending your elbows. 3. Push through your palms to return to the starting position. 4. Hold the position for the prescribed time, maintaining tension. Exhale during the exertion phase of the movement.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 65, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'push_up', 'Isometric Hold Push Up', 'bench_press, chest_fly, dip', TRUE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('88202d6f-da98-427b-8b41-0b06cba39665', 'Lat Stretch (TRX)', 'Back', 'TRX', '{"Lats"}'::text[], '{"Lower Back"}'::text[], 'The Suspender Lat Stretch is a stretching exercise that targets your latissimus dorsi for a wider back. Suspension training adds instability, increasing core activation throughout. A strong back improves posture, prevents injury, and balances pressing movements.', '11181201', '11181201-Suspender-Lat-Stretch-(female)_Back_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:39.472701+00', '1. Adjust the TRX/suspension straps to the appropriate length for Suspender Lat Stretch. 2. Set up in the starting position for Suspender Lat Stretch. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your lats. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 5. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 1, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Stretch', 30, 2, 6, FALSE, TRUE, 'lat_stretch', 'Suspender Lat Stretch', 'stretch_hip, stretch_back', FALSE, 'trx', TRUE, 1, 30, 2, 68, 85, 85, 70),
('8828ee16-68bc-4844-a78e-b5840cb715bf', 'Sliding Leg Curl On Floor (Towel)', 'Legs', 'Towel', '{"Hamstrings"}'::text[], '{"Glutes"}'::text[], 'The Sliding Leg Curl On Floor With Towel targets your hamstrings through a controlled curling motion. Your calves work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. Strong legs are the foundation for athletic performance and functional fitness.', '57721201', '57721201-Sliding-Leg-Curl-on-Floor-with-Towel-(female)_Hips.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:37.99429+00', '1. Position yourself on the floor for Sliding Leg Curl On Floor With Towel. 2. Curl your heels toward your glutes by bending at the knees. 3. Squeeze your hamstrings at peak contraction. 4. Extend legs back out with control. 5. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 75, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'leg_curl', 'Sliding Leg Curl On Floor With Towel', 'romanian_deadlift, hip_thrust', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('882bf1dd-6d1f-4e34-ad88-9bbed51939df', 'Place Jog', 'Full Body', 'Bodyweight', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'This cardio exercise keeps your heart rate elevated for improved cardiovascular fitness. Cardiovascular exercise improves heart health, endurance, and helps manage weight. Aim for full range of motion on every rep.', '6441201', '06441201-Place-Jog-(female)_Cardio_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:35.667316+00', '1. Set up in the starting position for Place Jog. 2. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your cardio. 3. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 4. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'running', 'Place Jog', 'cycling, rowing_cardio, jump_rope', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('88304d90-f434-46eb-90c0-b1d1c24d4d0c', 'Lying Anterior Pelvic Shift', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'The Lying Anterior Pelvic Shift is a lower body movement exercise that targets your core. The lying position provides back support and helps isolate the target muscles. This bodyweight exercise requires no equipment and can be done anywhere. Strong legs are the foundation for athletic performance and functional fitness.', '79411201', '79411201-Lying-Anterior-Pelvic-Shift-(female)_Hips_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:35.010404+00', '1. Lie down in the appropriate position for Lying Anterior Pelvic Shift. 2. Set up in the starting position for Lying Anterior Pelvic Shift. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your core. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 5. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, 'Lying', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'general_exercise', 'Lying Anterior Pelvic Shift', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('88339d82-2e4a-4645-bdf4-1416cf96b9c9', 'Ballerina Side Bends', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Obliques"}'::text[], '{"Abs"}'::text[], 'This movement exercise engages your abs for improved core stability and strength. The abs assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. No equipment needed—your body provides all the resistance. Building core stability helps with everything from heavy deadlifts to daily activities.', '59591201', '59591201-Ballerina-Side-Bends-(female)_Waist_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:30.685158+00', '1. Set up in the starting position for Ballerina Side Bends. 2. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your abs. 3. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 4. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'side_bend', 'Ballerina Side Bends', 'russian_twist, woodchop, oblique_crunch', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('8833de46-664c-4f28-b90e-e1ab5b3c1689', 'Lying Supine Single Leg Circle', 'Shoulders', 'Bodyweight', '{"Shoulders"}'::text[], '{"Traps"}'::text[], 'Build leg strength with this movement movement focusing on your delts. The lying position provides back support and helps isolate the target muscles. No equipment needed—your body provides all the resistance. Strong legs are the foundation for athletic performance and functional fitness.', '100221201', '100221201-Lying-Supine-Single-Leg-Circle-(female)_Hips_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:35.38119+00', '1. Lie on your back with your body relaxed but ready. 2. Complete all reps on one side, then switch to the other side. 3. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, 'Lying', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 45, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'leg_exercise', 'Lying Supine Single Leg Circle', 'squat, lunge, leg_press', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('88440e2d-70c2-4f65-ac26-58c94dc858dd', 'Siting Floor Leg Raise', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Lower Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'The Siting Floor Leg Raise is a core raising exercise that primarily targets your abs. You''ll also feel your hip flexors working to support the movement. A versatile bodyweight movement perfect for home or gym training. A strong core improves posture, protects your spine, and enhances all other lifts.', '94871201', '94871201-Siting-Floor-Leg-Raise-(male)_Waist_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:29.242428+00', '1. Position yourself on the floor for Siting Floor Leg Raise. 2. Keeping legs mostly straight, raise them toward the ceiling. 3. Lower with control, stopping just before touching down. 4. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 65, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'leg_raise', 'Siting Floor Leg Raise', 'crunch, plank, v_up', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('8847982a-ca3b-42fc-b77e-e5778c905207', 'Chest To Wall Middle Split (Wall)', 'Chest', 'Wall', '{"Chest"}'::text[], '{"Shoulders"}'::text[], 'Use this stretch to open up your chest area and enhance overall flexibility. The shoulders assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. Flexibility work like this enhances performance and prevents stiffness.', '94631201', '94631201-Chest-to-Wall-Middle-Split-(male)_Stretching_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:25.87243+00', '1. Position yourself at the appropriate distance from a wall. 2. Move into the stretch position for Chest To Wall Middle Split. 3. Ease into the stretch until you feel gentle tension (not pain). 4. Hold for 20-30 seconds, breathing deeply and relaxing into the stretch.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 42, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'chest_exercise', 'Chest To Wall Middle Split', 'bench_press, chest_fly, push_up', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('884954f3-3d9f-4585-be78-5509067edd7a', 'Supine Crunch (TRX)', 'Core', 'TRX', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'This crunching exercise engages your abs for improved core stability and strength. The hip flexors assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. Performing this lying down removes momentum for stricter form. Suspension training adds instability, increasing core activation throughout. Core strength is foundational for athletic performance and injury prevention.', '11471201', '11471201-Suspender-Supine-Crunch_Waist-FIX_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:39.623429+00', '1. Adjust the TRX/suspension straps to the appropriate length for Suspender Supine Crunch. 2. Lie face up (supine position) for Suspender Supine Crunch. 3. Curl your shoulders off the floor by contracting your abs. 4. Don''t pull on your neck—focus on the abdominal contraction. 5. Lower with control, maintaining some tension. 6. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 12, 20, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 60, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'crunch', 'Suspender Supine Crunch', 'leg_raise, plank, russian_twist, v_up', TRUE, 'trx', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 68, 85, 85, 70),
('8863dfe8-e451-4049-9e22-102514c78a59', 'Seated Side Neck Stretch', 'Neck', 'Bodyweight', '{"Neck"}'::text[], '{"Traps"}'::text[], 'Target your neck with this stretching stretch that helps restore range of motion. The upper back assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. The seated position helps isolate the target muscles by removing momentum. Regular stretching improves flexibility, reduces injury risk, and aids recovery.', '61711201', '61711201-Sitting-Side-Neck-Stretch-(female)_Stretching_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:37.877283+00', '1. Sit with your back supported, core engaged, feet flat on the floor. 2. Move into the stretch position for Seated Side Neck Stretch. 3. Ease into the stretch until you feel gentle tension (not pain). 4. Hold for 20-30 seconds, breathing deeply and relaxing into the stretch. 5. Switch sides and repeat for equal time. Exhale during the exertion phase of the movement.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 1, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Stretch', 40, 2, 6, FALSE, TRUE, 'neck_stretch', 'Seated Side Neck Stretch', 'stretch_hip, stretch_back', FALSE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 1, 30, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('8865b0e0-a756-4df6-b022-fff6d72afdfd', 'Seated Hip Abduction (Resistance Band)', 'Legs', 'Resistance Band', '{"Glutes"}'::text[], '{"Hip Abductors"}'::text[], 'The Resistance Band Seated Hip Abduction is a lower body movement exercise that targets your hip abductors. The glutes assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. Being seated provides stability, allowing you to focus on the working muscles. Bands are joint-friendly and portable, perfect for any training environment. Lower body strength improves everything from walking to heavy compound lifts.', '67851201', '67851201-Resistance-Band-Seated-Hip-Abduction-(VERSION-2)_H.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:27.384461+00', '1. Secure the resistance band appropriately for Resistance Band Seated Hip Abduction. 2. Sit with your back supported, core engaged, feet flat on the floor. 3. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, 'Seated', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 57, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'hip_abduction', 'Seated Hip Abduction', 'hip_adduction, glute_bridge, clamshell', FALSE, 'band', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 60, 85, 90, 50),
('886845ca-4553-4686-8b33-6c0b7d7af02c', 'Standing Single Arm Extension (Kettlebell)', 'Arms', 'Kettlebell', '{"Triceps"}'::text[], '{"Chest","Shoulders"}'::text[], 'This extension movement isolates your triceps for improved arm development. Performing this standing challenges your balance and core engagement. Kettlebells are excellent for building functional, real-world strength. Dedicated arm training builds both strength and muscular definition.', '58631201', '58631201-Kettlebell-Standing-One-Arm-Extension_Upper-Arms_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:24.099303+00', '1. Select an appropriately weighted kettlebell for Kettlebell Standing One Arm Extension. 2. Begin in a standing position with good posture. 3. Extend through the target joint(s) for Kettlebell Standing One Arm Extension. 4. Complete all reps on one side, then switch to the other side. 5. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 4, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, 'Standing', NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 75, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'arm_exercise', 'Standing Single Arm Extension', 'bicep_curl, tricep_extension, hammer_curl', FALSE, 'kettlebell', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 75, 88, 88, 78),
('8876a8fc-afed-4b4a-acd6-ba1bbd8d2121', 'Seated Straight Arm Back Squeeze (Chair)', 'Back', 'Chair', '{"Upper Back"}'::text[], '{"Rear Delts"}'::text[], 'This movement exercise strengthens the muscles between your shoulder blades. Your rear delts work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. The seated position helps isolate the target muscles by removing momentum. Back development is crucial for pulling strength and overall upper body function.', '91161201', '91161201-Sitting-Straight-Arm-Back-Squeeze-on-a-Chair-(fema.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:37.877283+00', '1. Position yourself with a sturdy chair for support or as part of the movement. 2. Sit with your back supported, core engaged, feet flat on the floor. 3. Complete all reps with control before resting. Start with lighter weight to perfect your form. Works well for upper back activation.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 35, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'back_exercise', 'Seated Straight Arm Back Squeeze On A Chair', 'lat_pulldown, bent_over_row, pull_up', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('88783bbf-6352-4f6d-ba6a-31b76ac77602', 'Romanian Deadlift Bicep Curl Kickback', 'Arms', 'Bodyweight', '{"Hamstrings","Glutes","Biceps"}'::text[], '{"Lower Back"}'::text[], 'Strengthen the back of your thighs with this curling exercise. Your glutes, lower back work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. A versatile bodyweight movement perfect for home or gym training. Strong legs are the foundation for athletic performance and functional fitness.', '87491201', '87491201-Bodyweight-Romanian-Deadlift-Biceps-Curl-Kickback-.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:31.475486+00', '1. Keep your elbows in a fixed position throughout the movement. 2. Curl the weight up by contracting your biceps, squeezing at the top. 3. Lower with control, resisting the weight on the way down. 4. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout. Maintain consistent tempo throughout the set. Include this in your legs training.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 100, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'romanian_deadlift', 'Romanian Deadlift Biceps Curl Kickback', 'deadlift, leg_curl, hip_thrust', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('888eb3de-b49c-4f91-b070-14d0712a9f5f', 'Squeeze Press On Floor (Dumbbell)', 'Chest', 'Dumbbells', '{"Chest"}'::text[], '{"Triceps","Front Delts"}'::text[], 'Target your chest with the Dumbbell Squeeze Press On Floor, an effective pressing movement for upper body strength. Dumbbells allow each arm to work independently, helping correct imbalances. Chest strength improves pushing power for sports, daily tasks, and other lifts.', '54571201', '54571201-Dumbbell-Squeeze-Press-on-Floor_Chest_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:22.247914+00', '1. Select a pair of dumbbells at an appropriate weight for Dumbbell Squeeze Press On Floor. 2. Position yourself on the floor for Dumbbell Squeeze Press On Floor. 3. Lower the weight toward your chest with control. 4. Press the weight up until your arms are extended (don''t lock elbows). 5. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 8, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 82, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'squeeze_press', 'Squeeze Press On Floor', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', TRUE, 'dumbbell', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 92, 90, 92, 90),
('88b05455-beae-4556-a476-b70a23c8ab4a', 'Ear To Knee Side Bend', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Obliques"}'::text[], '{"Abs"}'::text[], 'This movement exercise engages your abs for improved core stability and strength. Secondary activation of your abs provides additional muscle engagement. No equipment needed—your body provides all the resistance. Core strength is foundational for athletic performance and injury prevention.', '63801201', '63801201-Ear-to-Knee-Side-Bend-(female)_Waist_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:33.298565+00', '1. Set up in the starting position for Ear To Knee Side Bend. 2. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your abs. 3. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 4. Complete all reps with control before resting. Maintain a neutral spine throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'side_bend', 'Ear To Knee Side Bend', 'russian_twist, woodchop, oblique_crunch', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('88b19791-9e72-46cf-ad43-78fbc2ea6094', 'Bent Press (Kettlebell)', 'Core', 'Kettlebell', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'Build a stronger core with the Kettlebell Bent Press, focusing on your abs. The kettlebell grip position adds a unique training stimulus. Building core stability helps with everything from heavy deadlifts to daily activities.', '5241201', '05241201-Kettlebell-Bent-Press_Waist-FIX_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:22.755209+00', '1. Select an appropriately weighted kettlebell for Kettlebell Bent Press. 2. Execute the pressing motion for Kettlebell Bent Press, extending through the target muscles. 3. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout. Maintain a neutral spine throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 78, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'general_exercise', 'Bent Press', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'kettlebell', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 75, 88, 88, 78),
('88d6dec3-154f-4717-8514-41ec3df5ebd3', 'Pull Through Rope (Cable)', 'Legs', 'Cables', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'This pulling exercise isolates your glutes for improved hip strength and power. You''ll also feel your hamstrings working to support the movement. The cable setup allows you to adjust the angle of resistance. Strong legs are the foundation for athletic performance and functional fitness.', '1961201', '01961201-Cable-Pull-Through-(with-rope)_Hips_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:24.099303+00', '1. Adjust the cable machine to the correct height and attachment for Cable Pull Through. 2. Set up in the starting position for Cable Pull Through. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your glutes. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 5. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout. Control the movement—avoid using momentum.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 8, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 52, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'pull_through', 'Pull Through', 'lat_pulldown, bent_over_row, pull_up', FALSE, 'cable', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 85, 88, 30, 92),
('88db3851-105e-4efe-903d-e9558226b672', 'Toe Walk', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'The Toe Walk isolates your calf muscles through a stepping motion. A versatile bodyweight movement perfect for home or gym training. Leg training boosts metabolism and builds functional, real-world strength.', '48021201', '48021201-Toe-Walk_Calves_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:20.982555+00', '1. Set up in the starting position for Toe Walk. 2. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your calves. 3. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 4. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'walking', 'Toe Walk', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('88fcea27-736d-4082-b033-a445b53c3014', 'Assisted Standing Shoulder Flexion (Resistance Band)', 'Full Body', 'Resistance Band', '{"Full Body"}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'Build total body strength and coordination with this multi-joint flexion movement. Performing this standing challenges your balance and core engagement. Resistance bands provide accommodating resistance that increases through the range of motion. Compound movements like this develop coordination, power, and overall fitness.', '101581201', '101581201-Resistance-Band-Assisted-Standing-Shoulder-Flexio.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:35.936279+00', '1. Secure the resistance band appropriately for Resistance Band Assisted Standing Shoulder Flexion. 2. Stand with feet about shoulder-width apart. 3. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, 'Standing', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 47, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'shoulder_exercise', 'Assisted Standing Shoulder Flexion', 'lateral_raise, shoulder_press, front_raise', FALSE, 'band', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 60, 85, 90, 50),
