('891259d0-6856-492e-b02b-097345b7df6c', 'Spine Stretch', 'Back', 'Bodyweight', '{"Upper Back"}'::text[], '{"Obliques"}'::text[], 'The Spine Stretch provides a deep stretch for your full body, ideal for recovery and mobility work. Include this in your routine for better mobility and reduced muscle tension.', '43131201', '43131201-Spine-Stretch-(female)_Back.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:38.153182+00', '1. Move into the stretch position for Spine Stretch. 2. Ease into the stretch until you feel gentle tension (not pain). 3. Hold for 20-30 seconds, breathing deeply and relaxing into the stretch.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 1, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Stretch', 40, 2, 6, FALSE, TRUE, 'stretch_general', 'Spine Stretch', 'running, elliptical, rowing_cardio', FALSE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 1, 30, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('891a6708-8c33-4a12-b101-b04fd9947634', 'Bulgarian Split Squat (Dumbbell)', 'Legs', 'Dumbbells', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'Target the front of your thighs with this squatting exercise for quad development. You''ll also feel your glutes, hamstrings working to support the movement. The dumbbell variation provides freedom of movement and greater range of motion. Leg training boosts metabolism and builds functional, real-world strength.', '22901201', '22901201-Dumbbell-Bulgarian-Split-Squat-(female)_Thighs.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:32.735372+00', '1. Select a pair of dumbbells at an appropriate weight for Dumbbell Bulgarian Split Squat. 2. Push your hips back and bend your knees to lower your body. 3. Keep your chest up and knees tracking over your toes. 4. Drive through your heels to stand back up, squeezing your glutes at the top. 5. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', 'Squat', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 10, 10, NULL, 4, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 5, 8, NULL, 9, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 97, 7, 9, TRUE, FALSE, 'split_squat', 'Bulgarian Split Squat', 'split_squat, lunge, leg_press', FALSE, 'dumbbell', FALSE, 4, 120, 5, 92, 90, 92, 90),
('8930dc63-cd6d-48d8-a336-42da20b1ada0', 'Lying Scissor Kick', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'Build leg strength with this kicking movement focusing on your abs. Your hip flexors work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. The lying position provides back support and helps isolate the target muscles. A versatile bodyweight movement perfect for home or gym training. Lower body strength improves everything from walking to heavy compound lifts.', '6221201', '06221201-Lying-Scissor-Kick-(female)_Hips_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:35.38119+00', '1. Lie down in the appropriate position for Lying Scissor Kick. 2. Set up in the starting position for Lying Scissor Kick. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your abs. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 5. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, 'Lying', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'leg_raise', 'Lying Scissor Kick', 'crunch, plank, v_up', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('893315e1-7d9b-4770-956a-61dc2e04b442', 'Weighted Lying Neck Flexion', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'The Weighted Lying Neck Flexion targets your neck muscles through a controlled flexion motion. The lying position provides back support and helps isolate the target muscles. A versatile bodyweight movement perfect for home or gym training. Include this exercise in your routine for balanced strength development.', '10431201', '10431201-Weighted-Lying-Neck-Flexion_neck.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:29.837118+00', '1. Lie down in the appropriate position for Weighted Lying Neck Flexion. 2. Set up in the starting position for Weighted Lying Neck Flexion. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your core. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 5. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, 'Lying', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'neck_exercise', 'Weighted Lying Neck Flexion', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('89376f2d-a377-48d9-b803-515f596c85bf', 'Standing Leg Lift - Alternating', 'Full Body', 'Bodyweight', '{"Full Body"}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'The Standing Alternate Leg Lift is an explosive exercise that combines cardiovascular training with dynamic movement movements. Performing this standing challenges your balance and core engagement. No equipment needed—your body provides all the resistance. Plyometric training builds explosive power that transfers to sports and daily activities.', '88341201', '88341201-Standing-Alternate-Leg-Lift-(female)_Plyometrics_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:38.285955+00', '1. Begin in a standing position with good posture. 2. Alternate between sides/arms/legs with each repetition. 3. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions. Focus on the mind-muscle connection.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, 'Standing', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 52, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'leg_exercise', 'Standing Leg Lift - Alternating', 'crunch, plank, russian_twist, hanging_knee_raise', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('89380eca-7195-419f-a0ff-2460b7204aef', 'Side Plank', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Core","Abs"}'::text[], '{"Shoulders"}'::text[], 'The Side Plank is a core stabilization exercise that primarily targets your abs. You''ll also feel your shoulders, lower back working to support the movement. This bodyweight exercise requires no equipment and can be done anywhere. Building core stability helps with everything from heavy deadlifts to daily activities.', '48111201', '48111201-Side-Plank-(VERSION-2)-(female)_Waist_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:37.179953+00', '1. Hold your body in a straight line from head to heels. 2. Don''t let your hips sag or pike up—engage your core and glutes. 3. Breathe steadily while maintaining the position. 4. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions. Keep your shoulders relaxed and away from your ears. Ideal for abs strength and endurance.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 70, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'side_plank', 'Side Plank', 'plank, russian_twist, woodchop', FALSE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('893ad120-a494-478e-b9f5-9b09fd8a26df', 'Seated Overhead Stretch (Chair)', 'Full Body', 'Chair', '{"Full Body"}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'Target your full body with this stretching stretch that helps restore range of motion. Being seated provides stability, allowing you to focus on the working muscles. Include this in your routine for better mobility and reduced muscle tension. Aim for full range of motion on every rep.', '84311201', '84311201-Seated-Overhead-Stretch-on-a-Chair-(male)_Stretchi.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:21.249384+00', '1. Position yourself with a sturdy chair for support or as part of the movement. 2. Sit with your back supported, core engaged, feet flat on the floor. 3. Move into the stretch position for Seated Overhead Stretch On A Chair. 4. Ease into the stretch until you feel gentle tension (not pain). 5. Hold for 20-30 seconds, breathing deeply and relaxing into the stretch.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 3, 'Seated', NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 1, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Stretch', 27, 2, 6, FALSE, TRUE, 'stretch_general', 'Seated Overhead Stretch On A Chair', 'stretch_hip, stretch_back, stretch_shoulder', FALSE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 1, 30, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('8948b814-a006-4bdd-980f-99411f1a306e', 'Seated Swimming Knee Raise (Chair)', 'Core', 'Chair', '{"Lower Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'The Seated Swimming Knee Raise On A Chair is a core raising exercise that primarily targets your abs. The hip flexors assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. The seated position helps isolate the target muscles by removing momentum. Core strength is foundational for athletic performance and injury prevention.', '69051201', '69051201-Sitting-Swimming-Knee-Raise-on-a-Chair-(female)_Wa.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:37.877283+00', '1. Position yourself with a sturdy chair for support or as part of the movement. 2. Sit with your back supported, core engaged, feet flat on the floor. 3. Raise the weight in the prescribed direction for Seated Swimming Knee Raise On A Chair. 4. Lower with control, maintaining tension throughout. 5. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 55, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'leg_raise', 'Seated Swimming Knee Raise On A Chair', 'crunch, plank, v_up', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('895eeb30-ed8b-4cc9-bf6f-b06a486ed522', 'Elevated Squat (Machine)', 'Legs', 'Lever Machine', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'The Lever Elevanted Squat is a squatting exercise that primarily loads your quadriceps. The glutes, hamstrings assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. The machine guides your movement path for safer, more controlled repetitions. Leg training boosts metabolism and builds functional, real-world strength.', '66081201', '66081201-Lever-Elevanted-Squat-(male)_Thighs_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:26.808474+00', '1. Adjust the machine settings (seat height, weight, pads) to fit your body for Lever Elevanted Squat. 2. Push your hips back and bend your knees to lower your body. 3. Keep your chest up and knees tracking over your toes. 4. Drive through your heels to stand back up, squeezing your glutes at the top. 5. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', 'Squat', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 10, 10, NULL, 4, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 5, 8, NULL, 9, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 93, 7, 9, TRUE, FALSE, 'squat', 'Lever Elevanted Squat', 'leg_press, front_squat, goblet_squat, lunge, leg_extension', FALSE, 'machine', FALSE, 4, 120, 5, 80, 75, 20, 88),
('89631873-8e27-4ba3-99c4-ba545403d6fe', 'Guillotine Bench Press (Barbell)', 'Chest', 'Barbell, Flat Bench', '{"Chest"}'::text[], '{"Triceps","Front Delts"}'::text[], 'This pressing exercise focuses on your pectorals for improved chest strength and development. Secondary activation of your triceps, front delts provides additional muscle engagement. The barbell allows you to handle heavier loads for maximum strength gains. A well-developed chest contributes to upper body strength and aesthetics.', '451201', '00451201-Barbell-Guillotine-Bench-Press_Chest.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:23.586683+00', '1. Load a barbell and set it on a bench rack at the appropriate height. 2. Lower the weight toward your chest with control. 3. Press the weight up until your arms are extended (don''t lock elbows). 4. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout. Start with lighter weight to perfect your form.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 10, 10, NULL, 4, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 5, 8, NULL, 8, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 97, 7, 9, TRUE, FALSE, 'bench_press', 'Guillotine Bench Press', 'incline_press, decline_press, chest_fly, push_up, dip', TRUE, 'barbell', FALSE, 4, 120, 4, 95, 80, 65, 95),
('8967f8f3-c77c-43e6-a5d7-c7c59833d45a', 'Ring Weighted Inverted Row - Neutral Grip (Gymnastic Rings)', 'Back', 'Gymnastic Rings', '{"Upper Back"}'::text[], '{"Lats","Biceps","Rear Delts"}'::text[], 'The Ring Weighted Neutral Grip Inverted Row is a rowing exercise that builds thickness in your upper back. The biceps assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. Back development is crucial for pulling strength and overall upper body function.', '76501201', '76501201-Ring-Weighted-Neutral-Grip-Inverted-Row_Back_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:23.586683+00', '1. Use a neutral grip with palms facing each other. 2. Pull the weight toward your torso, leading with your elbow(s). 3. Squeeze your shoulder blades together at the peak contraction. 4. Extend back out with control, feeling the stretch in your back. 5. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 4, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 58, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'general_exercise', 'Ring Weighted Inverted Row - Neutral Grip', 'Ring Weighted Inverted Row - Neutral Grip', FALSE, 'gymnastic_rings', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 68, 85, 85, 70),
('896b8985-84c1-4fba-80cf-1d77876e0a18', 'Spine Stretch Forward', 'Back', 'Bodyweight', '{"Upper Back"}'::text[], '{"Obliques"}'::text[], 'The Spine Stretch Forward is a flexibility exercise that targets your spine, helping to release tension and improve range of motion. You''ll also feel your lower back working to support the movement. Include this in your routine for better mobility and reduced muscle tension.', '43151201', '43151201-Spine-Stretch-Forward-(male)_Pilates.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:21.995567+00', '1. Move into the stretch position for Spine Stretch Forward. 2. Ease into the stretch until you feel gentle tension (not pain). 3. Hold for 20-30 seconds, breathing deeply and relaxing into the stretch.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 1, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Stretch', 40, 2, 6, FALSE, TRUE, 'stretch_general', 'Spine Stretch Forward', 'running, elliptical, rowing_cardio', FALSE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 1, 30, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('896f5de0-a156-4607-b9ac-16951dc82bc6', 'Tibialis Raise (Wall Supported)', 'Legs', 'Wall', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'This raising movement focuses on your gastrocnemius and soleus. Strong legs are the foundation for athletic performance and functional fitness. Keep your core engaged throughout the exercise.', '85361201', '85361201-Bodyweight-Tibialias-Raise-Wall-Supported-(male)_C.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:27.145158+00', '1. Position yourself at the appropriate distance from a wall. 2. Raise the weight in the prescribed direction for Bodyweight Tibialis Raise Wall Supported. 3. Lower with control, maintaining tension throughout. 4. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 62, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'general_exercise', 'Tibialis Raise Wall Supported', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('8973ab3f-6b2b-4e94-b1e2-15aca66a2461', '45 Degree Lean Back Knee Raise - Alternating', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Lower Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'This raising exercise engages your abs for improved core stability and strength. The hip flexors assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. No equipment needed—your body provides all the resistance. Building core stability helps with everything from heavy deadlifts to daily activities.', '83141201', '83141201-45-Degree-Lean-Back-Alternate-Knee-Raise-(male)_Wa.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:21.452942+00', '1. Raise the weight in the prescribed direction for 45 Degree Lean Back Alternate Knee Raise. 2. Lower with control, maintaining tension throughout. 3. Alternate between sides/arms/legs with each repetition. 4. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 70, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'leg_raise', '45 Degree Lean Back Knee Raise - Alternating', 'crunch, plank, v_up', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('898f31e4-2dc4-4f8c-a7f4-cf61eadbebe9', 'Lying Figure 8 With Nose', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'Strengthen your neck with this movement exercise for improved stability. Performing this lying down removes momentum for stricter form. This bodyweight exercise requires no equipment and can be done anywhere. Include this exercise in your routine for balanced strength development.', '94031201', '94031201-Lying-Figure-8-with-Nose-(female)_Neck_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:35.133808+00', '1. Lie down in the appropriate position for Lying Figure 8 With Nose. 2. Set up in the starting position for Lying Figure 8 With Nose. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your core. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 5. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, 'Lying', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 35, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'general_exercise', 'Lying Figure 8 With Nose', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('898fbdfd-cea1-4625-8555-da614be13f50', 'Pigeon Hip Stretch', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Hips"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'Use this stretch to open up your hips area and enhance overall flexibility. Include this in your routine for better mobility and reduced muscle tension. This is a great exercise for all fitness levels with proper scaling.', '22801201', '22801201-Pigeon-Hip-Stretch-(female)_Hips-FIX_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:35.667316+00', '1. Move into the stretch position for Pigeon Hip Stretch. 2. Ease into the stretch until you feel gentle tension (not pain). 3. Hold for 20-30 seconds, breathing deeply and relaxing into the stretch.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 1, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Stretch', 40, 2, 6, FALSE, TRUE, 'hip_stretch', 'Pigeon Hip Stretch', 'stretch_hamstring, stretch_glute, stretch_back', FALSE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 1, 30, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('8990d702-6071-4eca-83fa-9c5b2be3591b', 'Half Side Split Lunge Twisting Inner Thigh Tap', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Inner Thighs"}'::text[], '{"Glutes"}'::text[], 'The Half Side Split Lunge Twisting Inner Thigh Tap is a lower body lunging exercise that targets your adductors. The glutes, hamstrings assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. A versatile bodyweight movement perfect for home or gym training. Leg training boosts metabolism and builds functional, real-world strength.', '88351201', '88351201-Half-Side-Split-Lunge-Twisting-Inner-Thigh-Tap-(fe.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:33.778367+00', '1. Step to the side, bending that knee while keeping the other leg straight. 2. Push through your front/working leg to return to the starting position. 3. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions. Exhale during the exertion phase of the movement.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 62, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'hip_adduction', 'Half Side Split Lunge Twisting Inner Thigh Tap', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('8997320b-c2aa-4011-8923-46c39353b031', 'Seated Leg Raise And Abductor On A Ch - Alternating', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Lower Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'Strengthen your midsection with this raising movement that works your abs. Secondary activation of your hip flexors provides additional muscle engagement. Being seated provides stability, allowing you to focus on the working muscles. Building core stability helps with everything from heavy deadlifts to daily activities.', '91061201', '91061201-Sitting-Alternating-Leg-Raise-and-Abductor-on-a-Ch.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:37.628647+00', '1. Sit with your back supported, core engaged, feet flat on the floor. 2. Keeping legs mostly straight, raise them toward the ceiling. 3. Lower with control, stopping just before touching down. 4. Alternate between sides/arms/legs with each repetition. 5. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 12, 20, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 70, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'leg_raise', 'Seated Leg Raise And Abductor On A Ch - Alternating', 'crunch, plank, v_up', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('899b3fb9-d6b5-4757-b6a4-8469642326ed', 'Seated Curl (Cable)', 'Arms', 'Cables', '{"Biceps"}'::text[], '{"Forearms"}'::text[], 'Build bigger biceps with this curling movement that targets the front of your arms. Secondary activation of your forearms provides additional muscle engagement. The seated position helps isolate the target muscles by removing momentum. The cable setup allows you to adjust the angle of resistance. Dedicated arm training builds both strength and muscular definition.', '16411201', '16411201-Cable-Seated-Curl_Upper-Arms_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:25.737494+00', '1. Adjust the cable machine to the correct height and attachment for Cable Seated Curl. 2. Sit with your back supported, core engaged, feet flat on the floor. 3. Keep your elbows in a fixed position throughout the movement. 4. Curl the weight up by contracting your biceps, squeezing at the top. 5. Lower with control, resisting the weight on the way down. 6. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', 'Curl', 'Pull', NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, 'Seated', NULL, NULL, NULL, 12, 20, NULL, 4, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 82, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'leg_curl', 'Seated Curl', 'romanian_deadlift, hip_thrust', FALSE, 'cable', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 85, 88, 30, 92),
('899d805b-1995-47fa-825d-3200812941df', 'Rear Delt Circle', 'Shoulders', 'Bodyweight', '{"Rear Delts"}'::text[], '{"Upper Back","Traps"}'::text[], 'Build balanced shoulders by working the posterior delts with this movement exercise. The upper back assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. This bodyweight exercise requires no equipment and can be done anywhere. Back development is crucial for pulling strength and overall upper body function.', '95441201', '95441201-Bodyweight-Rear-Delt-Circle-(female)_Back_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:31.475486+00', '1. Set up in the starting position for Bodyweight Rear Delt Circle. 2. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your rear delts. 3. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 4. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'rear_delt', 'Rear Delt Circle', 'lateral_raise, shoulder_press, front_raise', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
