('89cb0883-4fb8-4e68-80e3-4170654d8f2d', 'Forward Neck Stretch', 'Neck', 'Bodyweight', '{"Neck"}'::text[], '{"Traps"}'::text[], 'The Forward Neck Stretch provides a deep stretch for your neck, ideal for recovery and mobility work. Regular stretching improves flexibility, reduces injury risk, and aids recovery.', '73081201', '73081201-Forward-Neck-Stretch-(female)_Neck_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:33.640031+00', '1. Move into the stretch position for Forward Neck Stretch. 2. Ease into the stretch until you feel gentle tension (not pain). 3. Hold for 20-30 seconds, breathing deeply and relaxing into the stretch.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 1, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Stretch', 40, 2, 6, FALSE, TRUE, 'neck_stretch', 'Forward Neck Stretch', 'stretch_hip, stretch_back', FALSE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 1, 30, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('89cc17c2-8222-4223-8b51-cc3317e49c7f', 'Deep Push Up On Parallel Bars (Dip Bars)', 'Chest', 'Dip Bars', '{"Chest"}'::text[], '{"Triceps","Front Delts"}'::text[], 'Build a stronger chest with this pushing movement that develops pressing power. Secondary activation of your triceps, front delts provides additional muscle engagement. Chest strength improves pushing power for sports, daily tasks, and other lifts.', '69101201', '69101201-Deep-Push-up-on-Parallel-Bars-(male)_Chest_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:26.39056+00', '1. Keep your body in a straight line from head to heels throughout. 2. Lower your chest toward the floor by bending your elbows. 3. Push through your palms to return to the starting position. 4. Complete all reps with control before resting. Ensure full range of motion on each rep. This exercise is excellent for chest development.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 70, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'dip', 'Deep Push Up On Parallel Bars', 'bench_press, chest_fly, dip, tricep_pushdown', TRUE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('89d7f263-46d1-4780-9d30-43929cc14b97', 'Hammer Grip Incline Bench Two Arm Row (Dumbbell)', 'Back', 'Dumbbells, Incline Bench', '{"Upper Back"}'::text[], '{"Lats","Biceps","Rear Delts"}'::text[], 'The Dumbbell Hammer Grip Incline Bench Two Arm Row is a rowing exercise that builds thickness in your upper back. Secondary activation of your biceps, rear delts provides additional muscle engagement. The incline angle shifts emphasis toward the upper portion of the target muscles. Using dumbbells requires more stabilization than barbell variations. Back development is crucial for pulling strength and overall upper body function.', '39011201', '39011201-Dumbbell-Hammer-Grip-Incline-Bench-Two-Arm-Row-(female)_Back.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:32.735372+00', '1. Select a pair of dumbbells at an appropriate weight for Dumbbell Hammer Grip Incline Bench Two Arm Row. 2. Use a hammer/neutral grip with palms facing each other throughout. 3. Pull the weight toward your torso, leading with your elbow(s). 4. Squeeze your shoulder blades together at the peak contraction. 5. Extend back out with control, feeling the stretch in your back. 6. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 10, 10, NULL, 4, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 5, 8, NULL, 8, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 85, 7, 9, TRUE, FALSE, 'incline_press', 'Hammer Grip Incline Bench Two Arm Row', 'bench_press, shoulder_press, chest_fly', TRUE, 'dumbbell', FALSE, 4, 120, 4, 92, 90, 92, 90),
('89da3492-6ad9-4f09-a4fc-5f29507ad06c', 'Ring Single Leg Curl (Gymnastic Rings)', 'Legs', 'Gymnastic Rings', '{"Hamstrings"}'::text[], '{"Glutes"}'::text[], 'This curling movement works your hamstrings for balanced leg development. Secondary activation of your calves provides additional muscle engagement. Leg training boosts metabolism and builds functional, real-world strength.', '77091201', '77091201-Ring-Single-Leg-Curl-(VERSION-2)_Thighs_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:24.307972+00', '1. Curl your heels toward your glutes by bending at the knees. 2. Squeeze your hamstrings at peak contraction. 3. Extend legs back out with control. 4. Complete all reps on one side, then switch to the other side. 5. Complete all reps with control before resting. Engage your stabilizer muscles for better control.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 63, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'leg_curl', 'Ring Single Leg Curl', 'romanian_deadlift, hip_thrust', FALSE, 'gymnastic_rings', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 68, 85, 85, 70),
('89e19a5f-ee25-4855-baf3-747215c5e34d', 'Seated Backbend (Chair)', 'Back', 'Chair', '{"Lower Back"}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'Target your lower back with this movement stretch that helps restore range of motion. The seated position helps isolate the target muscles by removing momentum. Include this in your routine for better mobility and reduced muscle tension.', '104461201', '104461201-Sitting-Backbend-on-a-Chair_Hips_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:29.483269+00', '1. Position yourself with a sturdy chair for support or as part of the movement. 2. Sit with your back supported, core engaged, feet flat on the floor. 3. Move into the stretch position for Seated Backbend On A Chair. 4. Ease into the stretch until you feel gentle tension (not pain). 5. Hold for 20-30 seconds, breathing deeply and relaxing into the stretch.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 35, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'back_exercise', 'Seated Backbend On A Chair', 'lat_pulldown, bent_over_row, pull_up', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('89e6f34b-2fa5-4f17-8849-1d1462f2c579', 'Lying Supine Shoulder External Rotation (Dumbbell)', 'Shoulders', 'Dumbbells, Flat Bench', '{"Rotator Cuff"}'::text[], '{"Shoulders"}'::text[], 'Target your rotator cuff with the Dumbbell Lying Supine Shoulder External Rotation, an effective shoulder rotation exercise. Performing this lying down removes momentum for stricter form. Dumbbells allow each arm to work independently, helping correct imbalances. Strong shoulders improve overhead strength and support nearly all upper body movements.', '101531201', '101531201-Dumbbell-Lying-Supine-Shoulder-External-Rotation-.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:32.914483+00', '1. Select a pair of dumbbells at an appropriate weight for Dumbbell Lying Supine Shoulder External Rotation. 2. Lie on your back with your body relaxed but ready. 3. Rotate your torso through the movement pattern for Dumbbell Lying Supine Shoulder External Rotation. 4. Control the rotation in both directions—avoid using momentum. 5. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 8, NULL, 5, 'Lying', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 62, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'external_rotation', 'Lying Supine Shoulder External Rotation', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', TRUE, 'dumbbell', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 92, 90, 92, 90),
('89ed34dc-1537-4378-852a-a708bc49d83e', 'Shrug Shrug Machine (Machine)', 'Shoulders', 'Machine', '{"Traps"}'::text[], '{"Triceps","Front Delts"}'::text[], 'Build a stronger back with this pressing movement targeting your chest. Secondary activation of your triceps, front delts provides additional muscle engagement. The machine guides your movement path for safer, more controlled repetitions. A strong back improves posture, prevents injury, and balances pressing movements.', '12211201', '12211201-Lever-Shrug-(Bench-Press-Machine)_Back_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:21.995567+00', '1. Adjust the machine settings (seat height, weight, pads) to fit your body for Lever Shrug. 2. Lower the weight toward your chest with control. 3. Press the weight up until your arms are extended (don''t lock elbows). 4. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 10, 10, NULL, 4, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 5, 8, NULL, 8, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 93, 7, 9, TRUE, FALSE, 'bench_press', 'Lever Shrug', 'incline_press, decline_press, chest_fly, push_up, dip', FALSE, 'machine', FALSE, 4, 120, 4, 80, 75, 20, 88),
('89f99a14-8d33-43b5-9ad9-7b22ed010f10', 'Chest Bench Press Forearms (Flat Bench)', 'Chest', 'Flat Bench', '{"Chest"}'::text[], '{"Triceps","Front Delts"}'::text[], 'This pressing exercise focuses on your pectorals for improved chest strength and development. Secondary activation of your triceps, front delts provides additional muscle engagement. Chest strength improves pushing power for sports, daily tasks, and other lifts.', '66281201', '66281201-Chest-Bench-Press---Forearms-(WRONG-RIGHT)-(female)_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:32.166461+00', '1. Lower the weight toward your chest with control. 2. Press the weight up until your arms are extended (don''t lock elbows). 3. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout. Keep the movement smooth and controlled.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 85, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'bench_press', 'Chest Bench Press Forearms', 'incline_press, decline_press, chest_fly, push_up, dip', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('8a18824e-a1f5-4840-a12e-c9ae93423e33', 'Butt Kick To Knee Thrust - Alternating', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], '{"Calves"}'::text[], 'Build power and athleticism with this high-intensity kicking exercise that challenges your entire body. Secondary activation of your hamstrings provides additional muscle engagement. No equipment needed—your body provides all the resistance. Great for improving athletic performance, burning calories, and building conditioning.', '88661201', '88661201-Alternate-Butt-Kick-to-Knee-Thrust-(female)_Plyome.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:30.412523+00', '1. Drive through your heels to lift your hips toward the ceiling. 2. Squeeze your glutes hard at the top of the movement. 3. Lower your hips back down with control. 4. Alternate between sides/arms/legs with each repetition. 5. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions. Keep your core engaged for stability.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'knee_drive', 'Butt Kick To Knee Thrust - Alternating', 'butt_kicks, jumping_jack, mountain_climber', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('8a2b2261-860d-48ba-bd5e-be985f84ae9f', 'Roll Iliospsoas', 'Full Body', 'Bodyweight', '{"Full Body"}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'Use this stretch to open up your full body area and enhance overall flexibility. Flexibility work like this enhances performance and prevents stiffness. Maintain proper breathing - exhale during the effort phase.', '45991201', '45991201-Roll-Iliospsoas_Hips.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:21.109351+00', '1. Move into the stretch position for Roll Iliospsoas. 2. Ease into the stretch until you feel gentle tension (not pain). 3. Hold for 20-30 seconds, breathing deeply and relaxing into the stretch.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'general_exercise', 'Roll Iliospsoas', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('8a2e0412-c327-4e81-a373-584e98a434b3', 'Walking On Spot Hands On Shoulder', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'A challenging plyometric exercise, the Walking On Spot Hands On Shoulder (front Pov) builds reactive power and improves conditioning. This bodyweight exercise requires no equipment and can be done anywhere. Develops fast-twitch muscle fibers for quicker, more powerful movements.', '92591201', '92591201-Walking-On-Spot-Hands-On-Shoulder-(front-POV)-(fem.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:39.91585+00', '1. Set up in the starting position for Walking On Spot Hands On Shoulder. 2. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your full body. 3. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 4. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 2, 2, NULL, 10, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 3, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Cardio', 50, 9, 8, FALSE, TRUE, 'walking', 'Walking On Spot Hands On Shoulder', 'lateral_raise, shoulder_press, front_raise', FALSE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 1, 60, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('8a3c3413-faa2-4530-bc44-14f4e66de8ac', 'Incline Bicep Curl (Dumbbell)', 'Arms', 'Dumbbells, Incline Bench', '{"Biceps"}'::text[], '{"Forearms"}'::text[], 'This curling exercise focuses on your biceps for improved arm size and strength. The forearms assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. The incline angle shifts emphasis toward the upper portion of the target muscles. Dumbbells allow each arm to work independently, helping correct imbalances. Arm strength supports grip, pulling, and pushing in compound movements.', '3151201', '03151201-Dumbbell-Incline-Biceps-Curl_Upper-Arms.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:28.397686+00', '1. Select a pair of dumbbells at an appropriate weight for Dumbbell Incline Biceps Curl. 2. Keep your elbows in a fixed position throughout the movement. 3. Curl the weight up by contracting your biceps, squeezing at the top. 4. Lower with control, resisting the weight on the way down. 5. Complete all reps with control before resting. Ensure full range of motion on each rep.', 'Curl', 'Pull', NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 95, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'bicep_curl', 'Incline Biceps Curl', 'hammer_curl, preacher_curl, cable_curl', TRUE, 'dumbbell', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 92, 90, 92, 90),
('8a3cccca-70a5-477e-adf1-4ff12d67bac8', 'Hanging Advanced Tucked Front Hold (Pull-Up Bar)', 'Core', 'Pull-Up Bar', '{"Lower Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors","Forearms"}'::text[], 'Strengthen your midsection with this movement movement that works your abs. Your hip flexors, grip work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. Hanging adds a grip and core stability component to the exercise. Machine exercises are great for isolating muscles and training to failure safely. Building core stability helps with everything from heavy deadlifts to daily activities.', '90441201', '90441201-Hanging-Advanced-Tucked-Front-Lever-Hold-(male)_Wa.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:21.608253+00', '1. Adjust the machine settings (seat height, weight, pads) to fit your body for Hanging Advanced Tucked Front Lever Hold. 2. Grip the bar and hang with arms fully extended, engaging your shoulders. 3. Hold the position for the prescribed time, maintaining tension.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 5, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 5, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'front_lever', 'Hanging Advanced Tucked Front Lever Hold', 'pull_up, lat_pulldown, grip_training', FALSE, 'pull_up_bar', TRUE, 3, 90, 4, 80, 75, 20, 88),
('8a488e5d-f4b2-4696-9ffa-cd68630f574a', 'Pull Up - Close Grip (Pull-Up Bar)', 'Back', 'Pull-Up Bar', '{"Lats"}'::text[], '{"Biceps","Upper Back"}'::text[], 'This pulling exercise emphasizes your lats for improved back development. Secondary activation of your biceps, upper back provides additional muscle engagement. A versatile bodyweight movement perfect for home or gym training. Back development is crucial for pulling strength and overall upper body function. This is a great exercise for all fitness levels with proper scaling. Consistency with this movement will yield noticeable results.', '54791201', '54791201-Close-Grip-Pull-Up_Back_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:26.808474+00', '1. Use a close/narrow grip (hands closer than shoulder-width). 2. Pull yourself up by driving your elbows down and back. 3. Continue until your chin clears the bar, then lower with control to a full hang. 4. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 70, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'pull_up', 'Pull Up - Close Grip', 'Pull Up - Close Grip', TRUE, 'pull_up_bar', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('8a495f5c-40ed-4526-bf85-1830f0a6c372', 'Seated Wide Squat (Machine)', 'Legs', 'Lever Machine', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'Build stronger quads with this squatting movement that develops leg drive and power. Your glutes, hamstrings work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. Being seated provides stability, allowing you to focus on the working muscles. The machine guides your movement path for safer, more controlled repetitions. Strong legs are the foundation for athletic performance and functional fitness.', '15741201', '15741201-Lever-Seated-Wide-Squat_Thighs_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:27.145158+00', '1. Adjust the machine settings (seat height, weight, pads) to fit your body for Lever Seated Wide Squat. 2. Sit with your back supported, core engaged, feet flat on the floor. 3. Push your hips back and bend your knees to lower your body. 4. Keep your chest up and knees tracking over your toes. 5. Drive through your heels to stand back up, squeezing your glutes at the top. 6. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', 'Squat', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 10, 10, NULL, 4, 'Seated', NULL, NULL, NULL, 5, 8, NULL, 9, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 95, 7, 9, TRUE, FALSE, 'squat', 'Lever Seated Wide Squat', 'leg_press, front_squat, goblet_squat, lunge, leg_extension', FALSE, 'machine', FALSE, 4, 120, 5, 80, 75, 20, 88),
('8a5dcf7c-439f-40e4-bcea-30268ec1f09c', 'Standing Hip Abduction', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Glutes"}'::text[], '{"Hip Abductors"}'::text[], 'Build leg strength with this movement movement focusing on your glute med/abductors. You''ll also feel your glutes working to support the movement. The standing position engages your core for stability. A versatile bodyweight movement perfect for home or gym training. Strong legs are the foundation for athletic performance and functional fitness.', '7911201', '07911201-Standing-Hip-Abduction-(female)_Hips_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:38.7451+00', '1. Stand tall with your feet firmly planted. 2. Set up in the starting position for Standing Hip Abduction. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your glute med/abductors. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 5. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, 'Standing', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 52, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'hip_abduction', 'Standing Hip Abduction', 'hip_adduction, glute_bridge, clamshell', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('8a60b9ef-68ae-465d-b40d-e74cba9a3978', 'Standing Crossed Legs Twisting Bend Stretch (Stick)', 'Back', 'Bodyweight', '{"Upper Back"}'::text[], '{"Obliques"}'::text[], 'Elevate your training with this stretching exercise that develops speed, power, and coordination. The shoulders, core assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. The standing position engages your core for stability. A versatile bodyweight movement perfect for home or gym training. Develops fast-twitch muscle fibers for quicker, more powerful movements.', '103611201', '103611201-Stick-Standing-Crossed-Legs-Twisting-Bend-Stretch.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:28.52454+00', '1. Begin in a standing position with good posture. 2. Rotate your torso through the movement pattern for Stick Standing Crossed Legs Twisting Bend Stretch. 3. Control the rotation in both directions—avoid using momentum. 4. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 3, 'Standing', NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 1, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Stretch', 34, 2, 6, FALSE, TRUE, 'stretch_general', 'Stick Standing Crossed Legs Twisting Bend Stretch', 'stretch_hip, stretch_back, stretch_shoulder', FALSE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 1, 30, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('8a61552e-e7a8-4c67-a4c3-b4c5ea63998a', 'Peterson Step From Stepbox (Step Platform)', 'Legs', 'Step Platform', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'The Bodyweight Peterson Step From Stepbox is a lower body stepping exercise that targets your full body. Secondary activation of your quads provides additional muscle engagement. Strong legs are the foundation for athletic performance and functional fitness.', '96051201', '96051201-Bodyweight-Peterson-Step-from-StepBox-(female)_Thi.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:31.475486+00', '1. Set up a box or step platform at the appropriate height. 2. Set up in the starting position for Bodyweight Peterson Step From Stepbox. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your full body. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 5. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'general_exercise', 'Peterson Step From Stepbox', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('8a6b1141-4b6c-444a-a5c7-43d243780a8a', 'Standing Opposite Straight Arm Clasp Raise (Right Over Left)', 'Full Body', 'Bodyweight', '{"Full Body"}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'This full-body raising exercise challenges multiple muscle groups simultaneously. Performing this standing challenges your balance and core engagement. No equipment needed—your body provides all the resistance. Full body exercises are time-efficient and build functional, real-world strength.', '94591201', '94591201-Standing-Opposite-Straight-Arm-Clasp-Raise-(right-.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:38.870314+00', '1. Stand tall with your feet firmly planted. 2. Raise the weight in the prescribed direction for Standing Opposite Straight Arm Clasp Raise (right. 3. Lower with control, maintaining tension throughout. 4. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, 'Standing', NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 72, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'arm_exercise', 'Standing Opposite Straight Arm Clasp Raise (right', 'shoulder_press, lateral_raise, front_raise', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('8a6efc7c-685a-4fcb-9198-7598ca8f8e84', 'Weighted Bag Wood Chop Squat', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'This squatting movement focuses on your obliques for a complete core workout. You''ll also feel your shoulders working to support the movement. This bodyweight exercise requires no equipment and can be done anywhere. Core strength is foundational for athletic performance and injury prevention.', '65051201', '65051201-Weighted-Bag-Wood-Chop-Squat_Waist_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:22.755209+00', '1. Push your hips back and bend your knees to lower your body. 2. Keep your chest up and knees tracking over your toes. 3. Drive through your heels to stand back up, squeezing your glutes at the top. 4. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout. Maintain a neutral spine throughout.', 'Squat', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 4, NULL, 5, 4, NULL, 8, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 7, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Plyometrics', 85, 9, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'woodchop', 'Weighted Bag Wood Chop Squat', 'leg_press, leg_extension, leg_curl, lunge, front_squat, hack_squat', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('8a7d6a65-fce4-45a1-8430-ea176b3cf179', 'Straight Arm Pulldown Rope (Cable)', 'Back', 'Cables', '{"Lats"}'::text[], '{"Biceps","Upper Back"}'::text[], 'This pulling exercise emphasizes your lats for improved back development. Cables provide constant tension throughout the full range of motion. Back development is crucial for pulling strength and overall upper body function.', '107081201', '107081201-Cable-Straight-Arm-Pulldown-(with-rope)-(female)_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:32.054831+00', '1. Adjust the cable machine to the correct height and attachment for Cable Straight Arm Pulldown. 2. Pull the bar/handle down toward your upper chest. 3. Drive your elbows down and back, squeezing your lats. 4. Control the weight back up without letting it yank your arms. 5. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 8, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 52, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'lat_pulldown', 'Straight Arm Pulldown', 'pull_up, bent_over_row, cable_row, face_pull', TRUE, 'cable', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 85, 88, 30, 92),
('8a862238-6c06-49e1-843a-c5ae54de90cb', '3 Leg Dog Pose', 'Back', 'Bodyweight', '{"Lats"}'::text[], '{"Hamstrings","Shoulders"}'::text[], 'Build total body strength and coordination with this multi-joint movement movement. No equipment needed—your body provides all the resistance. Full body exercises are time-efficient and build functional, real-world strength.', '58871201', '58871201-3-Leg-Dog-Pose-(female)_Stretching_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:30.292204+00', '1. Set up in the starting position for 3 Leg Dog Pose. 2. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your full body. 3. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 4. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 1, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Stretch', 50, 2, 6, FALSE, TRUE, 'leg_exercise', '3 Leg Dog Pose', 'stretch_hip, stretch_back, plank', FALSE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 1, 30, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('8a8d1c6b-65e5-487d-87c4-30b9ffb179ed', 'Elbows Back Stretch', 'Back', 'Bodyweight', '{"Lats"}'::text[], '{"Lower Back"}'::text[], 'The Elbows Back Stretch is a stretching exercise that targets your chest muscles. A versatile bodyweight movement perfect for home or gym training. A well-developed chest contributes to upper body strength and aesthetics.', '4441201', '04441201-Elbows-Back-Stretch-(female)_Chest.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:33.505723+00', '1. Set up in the starting position for Elbows Back Stretch. 2. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your chest. 3. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 4. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 1, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Stretch', 40, 2, 6, FALSE, TRUE, 'back_stretch', 'Elbows Back Stretch', 'stretch_hip, stretch_hamstring, stretch_shoulder', FALSE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 1, 30, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('8a9958ae-5823-4b4e-a6f5-bb6ab7f95a36', 'Seated Under Knee Crossed Arms Lean Back', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'Build rotational power and define your waistline with the Seated Under Knee Crossed Arms Lean Back. Your abs work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. Being seated provides stability, allowing you to focus on the working muscles. Building core stability helps with everything from heavy deadlifts to daily activities.', '82351201', '82351201-Seated-Under-Knee-Crossed-Arms-Lean-Back-(female)_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:36.848698+00', '1. Sit with your back supported, core engaged, feet flat on the floor. 2. Set up in the starting position for Seated Under Knee Crossed Arms Lean Back. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your obliques. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 5. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, 'Seated', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 52, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'boxing', 'Seated Under Knee Crossed Arms Lean Back', 'stretch_hip, dynamic_warmup, yoga_pose', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('8aa8b0e0-bec2-49ae-b26a-e24d91c4a6f1', 'Jump Box Over', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Calves"}'::text[], 'This dynamic jumping movement gets your heart rate up while developing explosive strength. Secondary activation of your quads, calves provides additional muscle engagement. Great for improving athletic performance, burning calories, and building conditioning.', '38871201', '38871201-Jump-Box-Over-(male)_Plyometrics_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:26.507873+00', '1. Set up a box or step platform at the appropriate height. 2. Set up in the starting position for Jump Box Over. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your full body. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 5. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 5, 4, NULL, 8, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 7, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Plyometrics', 50, 9, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'general_exercise', 'Jump Box Over', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('8ab1374c-30b1-418c-b0a6-1220b7b21624', 'Twist Step Stretch', 'Back', 'Bodyweight', '{"Upper Back"}'::text[], '{"Obliques"}'::text[], 'The Twist Step Stretch provides a deep stretch for your full body, ideal for recovery and mobility work. Regular stretching improves flexibility, reduces injury risk, and aids recovery.', '39561201', '39561201-Twist-Step-Stretch-(female)_Hips_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:39.79101+00', '1. Set up a box or step platform at the appropriate height. 2. Rotate your torso through the movement pattern for Twist Step Stretch. 3. Control the rotation in both directions—avoid using momentum.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 1, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Stretch', 40, 2, 6, FALSE, TRUE, 'stretch_general', 'Twist Step Stretch', 'stretch_hip, stretch_back, stretch_shoulder', FALSE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 1, 30, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('8abdf75b-2c0e-40b3-bdc4-974939097ec7', 'Walk Burpee', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'This stepping exercise engages your abs for improved core stability and strength. You''ll also feel your chest, quads working to support the movement. No equipment needed—your body provides all the resistance. A strong core improves posture, protects your spine, and enhances all other lifts.', '105211201', '105211201-Walk-Burpee-(male)_Waist_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:29.36063+00', '1. Squat down and place hands on the floor, jump feet back to plank. 2. Jump feet back toward hands, then explosively jump up with arms overhead. 3. Land softly and immediately begin the next rep. 4. Complete all reps with control before resting. Focus on the mind-muscle connection.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 4, NULL, 8, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 7, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Plyometrics', 50, 9, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'burpee', 'Walk Burpee', 'mountain_climber, box_jump, jumping_jack', TRUE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('8ac50ea4-e17d-4ec2-b100-fc82ff1eef35', 'Ed Bar Back Stretch', 'Back', 'Bodyweight', '{"Lats"}'::text[], '{"Lower Back"}'::text[], 'The Ed Bar Back Stretch provides a deep stretch for your back, ideal for recovery and mobility work. Regular stretching improves flexibility, reduces injury risk, and aids recovery.', '10521201', '10521201-Fixed-Bar-Back-Stretch_Back.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:30.292204+00', '1. Move into the stretch position for Ed Bar Back Stretch. 2. Ease into the stretch until you feel gentle tension (not pain). 3. Hold for 20-30 seconds, breathing deeply and relaxing into the stretch.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 1, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Stretch', 40, 2, 6, FALSE, TRUE, 'back_stretch', 'Ed Bar Back Stretch', 'stretch_hip, stretch_hamstring, stretch_shoulder', FALSE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 1, 30, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('8ace1fdd-924b-4cc4-a5f0-63bd3022de5d', 'Rollout (TRX)', 'Core', 'TRX', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'The Suspender Rollout is a core movement exercise that primarily targets your abs. You''ll also feel your lats, shoulders working to support the movement. The TRX allows you to adjust difficulty by changing your body angle. Core strength is foundational for athletic performance and injury prevention.', '47991201', '47991201-Suspender-Rollout-(VERSION-2)-(female)_Waist_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:39.472701+00', '1. Adjust the TRX/suspension straps to the appropriate length for Suspender Rollout. 2. Set up in the starting position for Suspender Rollout. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your abs. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 5. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 40, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'ab_rollout', 'Suspender Rollout', 'plank, crunch, dead_bug', FALSE, 'trx', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 68, 85, 85, 70),
('8ae9700a-f8f5-4598-b0cd-273ce202cc6b', 'Ipsilateral Glute Bridge Single Arm Chest (Dumbbell)', 'Legs', 'Dumbbells', '{"Glutes"}'::text[], '{"Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'This bridging exercise isolates your glutes for improved hip strength and power. You''ll also feel your hamstrings working to support the movement. The dumbbell variation provides freedom of movement and greater range of motion. Lower body strength improves everything from walking to heavy compound lifts.', '76531201', '76531201-Dumbbell-Ipsilateral-Glute-Bridge-Single-Arm-Chest.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:24.203368+00', '1. Select an appropriate weight dumbbell and hold it in one hand. 2. Drive through your heels to lift your hips toward the ceiling. 3. Squeeze your glutes hard at the top of the movement. 4. Lower your hips back down with control. 5. Complete all reps on one side, then switch to the other side. 6. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 7, 8, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 67, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'glute_bridge', 'Ipsilateral Glute Bridge Single Arm Chest', 'hip_thrust, romanian_deadlift', FALSE, 'dumbbell', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 92, 90, 92, 90),
('8af0b240-7c1d-41c9-98c6-c6c2cf487356', 'Weighted Crunch', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'This crunching exercise engages your abs for improved core stability and strength. Secondary activation of your hip flexors provides additional muscle engagement. This bodyweight exercise requires no equipment and can be done anywhere. Building core stability helps with everything from heavy deadlifts to daily activities. Can be modified for beginners or progressed for advanced athletes.', '42521201', '42521201-Weighted-Crunch-(VERSION-2)_Waist.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:27.67144+00', '1. Curl your shoulders off the floor by contracting your abs. 2. Don''t pull on your neck—focus on the abdominal contraction. 3. Lower with control, maintaining some tension. 4. Complete all reps with control before resting. Maintain consistent tempo throughout the set.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 12, 20, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 70, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'crunch', 'Weighted Crunch', 'leg_raise, plank, russian_twist, v_up', TRUE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('8af53642-98b2-4006-b536-3dee97eaebae', 'Pistol Squat To Box (Plyo Box)', 'Legs', 'Plyo Box', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'This squatting movement emphasizes your quadriceps for stronger, more powerful legs. Your glutes work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. Leg training boosts metabolism and builds functional, real-world strength.', '29851201', '29851201-Pistol-Squat-to-Box-(female)_Thighs_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:35.667316+00', '1. Set up a box or step platform at the appropriate height. 2. Push your hips back and bend your knees to lower your body. 3. Keep your chest up and knees tracking over your toes. 4. Drive through your heels to stand back up, squeezing your glutes at the top. 5. Complete all reps with control before resting. Don''t rush—quality over quantity.', 'Squat', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 4, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 85, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'pistol_squat', 'Pistol Squat To Box', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', TRUE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('8af5ebd7-d213-4381-9124-f0790d8376ca', 'Bouncing Shift', 'Full Body', 'Bodyweight', '{"Full Body"}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'The Bodyweight Bouncing Shift is an explosive exercise that combines cardiovascular training with dynamic movement movements. This bodyweight exercise requires no equipment and can be done anywhere. Plyometric training builds explosive power that transfers to sports and daily activities.', '93781201', '93781201-Bodyweight-Bouncing-Shift-(female)_Plyometrics_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:31.347577+00', '1. Set up in the starting position for Bodyweight Bouncing Shift. 2. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your full body. 3. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 4. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'general_exercise', 'Bouncing Shift', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('8b25684e-c788-4568-9ada-f7abd7df6645', '90 To 90 Knee Thrust', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Hips"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'Use this stretch to open up your full body area and enhance overall flexibility. Regular stretching improves flexibility, reduces injury risk, and aids recovery. Quality repetitions are more important than quantity.', '77661201', '77661201-90-to-90-Knee-Thrust-(female)_Hips_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:30.292204+00', '1. Drive through your heels to lift your hips toward the ceiling. 2. Squeeze your glutes hard at the top of the movement. 3. Lower your hips back down with control. Focus on maintaining proper breathing throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'knee_drive', '90 To 90 Knee Thrust', 'butt_kicks, jumping_jack, mountain_climber', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('8b2a91d0-06db-49f9-bd6f-01fa9cd4a0b1', 'Standing Behind Head Military Press (Smith Machine)', 'Shoulders', 'Smith Machine', '{"Shoulders"}'::text[], '{"Side Delts","Triceps"}'::text[], 'Build stronger shoulders with this pressing movement focusing on your delts. Secondary activation of your triceps provides additional muscle engagement. The standing position engages your core for stability. The machine guides your movement path for safer, more controlled repetitions. Shoulder development enhances both performance and upper body aesthetics.', '7721201', '07721201-Smith-Standing-Behind-Head-Military-Press_Shoulder.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:23.056255+00', '1. Set the Smith machine bar to the appropriate starting height for Smith Standing Behind Head Military Press. 2. Stand with feet about shoulder-width apart. 3. Start with the weight at shoulder level. 4. Press directly overhead until your arms are fully extended. 5. Lower back to shoulder level with control. 6. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 10, 10, NULL, 4, 'Standing', NULL, NULL, NULL, 5, 8, NULL, 8, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 95, 7, 9, TRUE, FALSE, 'shoulder_press', 'Smith Standing Behind Head Military Press', 'Standing Behind Head Military Press', FALSE, 'barbell', FALSE, 4, 120, 4, 80, 75, 20, 88);
